{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:19:14.613Z","ordinal":13362,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-7ae7badf-a301-4b8a-8b07-94822a42cd2c","process_id":"44251","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,56p' docs/standards/controls.md; sed -n '724,740p' docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md; rg -n 'method-admission-broadened|required-rule-removed|four strict|exactly.*four' tools/quality-workflow docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation* docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md | head -20; rg -n 'controlRegister|ControlRegister|strict-enforcement' tools/quality-workflow/*.ts tools/quality-workflow/*.json"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '1,56p' docs/standards/controls.md; sed -n '724,740p' docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md; rg -n 'method-admission-broadened|required-rule-removed|four strict|exactly.*four' tools/quality-workflow docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation* docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md | head -20; rg -n 'controlRegister|ControlRegister|strict-enforcement' tools/quality-workflow/*.ts tools/quality-workflow/*.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\ndocument_type: standard\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: taxkit-ci-release-maintainer\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-04\nreview_trigger: public boundary, workflow, action, release graph, or repeated-review finding change\n---\n\n# Controls and automation governance\n\nThe Quality workflow is the executable CI owner for the local release-facing\ngraph. It has read-only repository permission, a timeout, cancellation\nconcurrency, an explicit `taxkit-ci-release-maintainer` pin-update owner, and\nfull-SHA action pins. It invokes `bun run release:check -- --ci` on every\nconfigured pull request and on pushes to `main`; feature-branch pushes are\nintentionally covered by the pull-request event rather than running the same\nQuality graph a second time. There are deliberately no path filters, so a new\nor renamed release boundary cannot be skipped. The preceding bootstrap steps\nmaterialise complete `main` comparison history, resolve cache identities,\nperform a frozen Bun install and install Chromium plus its system packages\nthrough the app-local Playwright executable; a shallow checkout, cached\n`node_modules`, skipped install or floating browser-tool resolution fails\npolicy. The Schema-decoded workflow,\ncontrol register and negative corpus are owned by `tools/quality-workflow/` and\nrun through `bun run check:quality-workflow`.\n\n`bun run test:quality-workflow` runs the policy cases and six isolated\nrelease-boundary mutations through Bun-hosted Effect Vitest. Each mutation\nruns its real owning command. Scoped temporary clones retain relative symbolic\nlinks and clean up on success, failure and interruption; child processes and\nthe loopback-port reservation have the same lifetime owner. Syntax inspection\nuses immutable traversal and checked record/array access. The root verification\nalso runs `bun run check:quality-workflow:types`, covering the policy and tests.\nThis changes local checking, not CI permissions or provider authority.\n\nThe same scoped runner also executes four clean-slate enforcement mutations\nfrom `fixtures/strict-enforcement-defects.json`. Each changes only the copied\nlint configuration and runs the real `test:oxlint:task` verifier. Removed/disabled\nrequired rules and broadened synthetic assignment/method admissions must fail.\nThe fixture Schema admits exactly the four named modes; each named test asserts\nthe complete ordered corpus and selects exactly one fixture. All ten deliberate\nfaults have independent scoped repository copies, results and finite five-minute\ntest deadlines. The source-only documentation check is a separate named test,\nwith a temporary Git index and no package build before or after its command.\nGrouping a growing lint corpus under one shared deadline previously timed out\non the hosted runner; the deadline length and all rejection assertions remain. The target and command are fixed in code. Synthetic\ncanary exceptions admit no production source. Retain the existing five-control\nregister and six release-boundary oracles; this adds attached T002 proof.\n\nEvery eligible deterministic command under that graph is a Turbo task. Quality\nbinds the Vercel team cache as read/write on all configured events.\nSame-repository pull requests and `main` receive the existing team-scoped\nremote-cache token; forks do not. The workflow policy rejects a missing\nbinding, remote read-only regression, `pull_request_target` and step-level\ncache-mode overrides. This\ningress. Bounded Effect traversal owns repeated I/O; pure classification uses\npersistent collections. `check:skills:types` checks this suite during root\nverification. A readLink assertion proves the actual canonical symlink target.\n\nThe Quality-workflow test owner uses Bun-hosted Effect Vitest, Effect FileSystem,\nand scoped platform child processes. Its isolated release-boundary suite runs\nall six retained owning commands and four strict-enforcement mutations as\nindependent named tests with their existing five-minute deadlines and scoped\ntemporary repository copies. A separate test proves documentation tools work\nbefore any package build in a fresh source-only copy. The suite preserves\nrelative links and removes each copy on completion or interruption. The native\nEffect Bun HTTP server owns the short-lived loopback-port reservation. Its\npolicy source and tests have a focused `check:quality-workflow:types` project in\nroot verification and all eleven canonical strict rules. The executable alone\nhas an exact runtime admission. This local test-host qualification does not\nchange the hosted workflow or establish publication/deployment.\n\ndocs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md:589:four strict settings); 21 skill cases passed. Unchanged app/package/browser\ndocs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md:1383:failed hosted run `37200459089`: the four strict mutation cases and fresh-source\ndocs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md:1404:The four strict cases each take 43.934–44.871 seconds locally. Deployment-tool,\ntools/quality-workflow/fixtures/strict-enforcement-defects.json:3:    \"id\": \"required-rule-removed\",\ntools/quality-workflow/fixtures/strict-enforcement-defects.json:30:    \"id\": \"method-admission-broadened\",\ntools/quality-workflow/release-boundary.test.ts:259:    \"required-rule-removed\",\ntools/quality-workflow/release-boundary.test.ts:262:    \"method-admission-broadened\",\ntools/quality-workflow/release-boundary.test.ts:288:          \"required-rule-removed\",\ntools/quality-workflow/release-boundary.test.ts:291:          \"method-admission-broadened\",\ntools/quality-workflow/schemas.ts:96:      \"required-rule-removed\",\ntools/quality-workflow/schemas.ts:99:      \"method-admission-broadened\",\ntools/quality-workflow/release-boundary.test.ts:276:              \"tools/quality-workflow/fixtures/strict-enforcement-defects.json\"\ntools/quality-workflow/schemas.ts:111:const ControlRegisterEntry = Schema.Struct({\ntools/quality-workflow/schemas.ts:122:export type ControlRegisterEntry = typeof ControlRegisterEntry.Type;\ntools/quality-workflow/schemas.ts:123:export const ControlRegister = Schema.Array(ControlRegisterEntry);\ntools/quality-workflow/policy.ts:21:  ControlRegisterEntry,\ntools/quality-workflow/policy.ts:955:  control: ControlRegisterEntry,\ntools/quality-workflow/policy.ts:967:const inspectControls = (controls: readonly ControlRegisterEntry[]) => [\ntools/quality-workflow/policy.ts:1229:  controls: readonly ControlRegisterEntry[],\ntools/quality-workflow/policy.test.ts:14:  ControlRegister,\ntools/quality-workflow/policy.test.ts:526:          yield* Schema.decodeUnknownEffect(ControlRegister)(controlsJson);\ntools/quality-workflow/check.runtime.ts:19:  ControlRegister,\ntools/quality-workflow/check.runtime.ts:51:      ControlRegister\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\ndocument_type: standard\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: taxkit-ci-release-maintainer\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-04\nreview_trigger: public boundary, workflow, action, release graph, or repeated-review finding change\n---\n\n# Controls and automation governance\n\nThe Quality workflow is the executable CI owner for the local release-facing\ngraph. It has read-only repository permission, a timeout, cancellation\nconcurrency, an explicit `taxkit-ci-release-maintainer` pin-update owner, and\nfull-SHA action pins. It invokes `bun run release:check -- --ci` on every\nconfigured pull request and on pushes to `main`; feature-branch pushes are\nintentionally covered by the pull-request event rather than running the same\nQuality graph a second time. There are deliberately no path filters, so a new\nor renamed release boundary cannot be skipped. The preceding bootstrap steps\nmaterialise complete `main` comparison history, resolve cache identities,\nperform a frozen Bun install and install Chromium plus its system packages\nthrough the app-local Playwright executable; a shallow checkout, cached\n`node_modules`, skipped install or floating browser-tool resolution fails\npolicy. The Schema-decoded workflow,\ncontrol register and negative corpus are owned by `tools/quality-workflow/` and\nrun through `bun run check:quality-workflow`.\n\n`bun run test:quality-workflow` runs the policy cases and six isolated\nrelease-boundary mutations through Bun-hosted Effect Vitest. Each mutation\nruns its real owning command. Scoped temporary clones retain relative symbolic\nlinks and clean up on success, failure and interruption; child processes and\nthe loopback-port reservation have the same lifetime owner. Syntax inspection\nuses immu