{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:20:09.916Z","ordinal":13368,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_06b7a884f26959d3016ac26e8b275087d0956706f00784f027","status":"completed","call_id":"call_C71HWNf3I6QgimAdeVxlbwWp","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport json\\np=Path('docs/standards/controls.md');s=p.read_text().replace('last_reviewed: 2026-10-04','last_reviewed: 2026-10-05',1).replace('also executes four clean-slate enforcement mutations','also executes six clean-slate enforcement mutations').replace('required rules and broadened synthetic assignment/method admissions must fail.\\\\nThe fixture Schema admits exactly the four named modes;', 'required rules, broadened synthetic assignment/method admissions, a removed\\\\nwhole-source selector and a wildcard fixture exclusion must fail. The latter\\\\ntwo changes run the same real verifier and retain their exact scope/exclusion\\\\nfailure messages.\\\\nThe fixture Schema admits exactly the six named modes;').replace('All ten deliberate\\\\nfaults','All twelve deliberate\\\\nfaults');p.write_text(s)\\np=Path('docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md');s=p.read_text().replace('all six retained owning commands and four strict-enforcement mutations as','all six retained owning commands and six strict-enforcement mutations as');s+='''\\n\\nCanonical strict coverage includes every owned `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, `.jsx`,\\n`.mjs` and `.cjs` path, including newly added root/config/app/tool files. The\\nexisting explicit generated/vendor exclusions remain. Exactly five unexecuted\\ninputs under `tools/oxlint/fixtures/` retain their intentionally isolated Effect\\nand Bun rule contexts. Other rules still inspect them; they are read as lint\\ninput bytes, outside the owning TypeScript project and application execution.\\nTheir purpose ends when those focused binding/host-rule cases are retired.\\nActual CLI neighbours reject each exclusion spreading to a directory wildcard.\\nNative checks also assert the exact exclusion list and whole-source selector.\\nValid CommonJS has its own positive and negative input; ES-module syntax cannot\\nstand in for a CommonJS policy test. All six extensions must admit one file and\\nreject the named bad constructs through the actual lint binary. Fresh isolated\\ncopies prove removing that selector or broadening the fixture exclusion fails\\nthe complete verifier. No host runtime or mutable-operation admission expands.\\n''';p.write_text(s)\\nreceipt='docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-owned-source-coverage.json'\\nPath(receipt).write_text(json.dumps({'document_type':'migration-receipt','date':'2026-10-05','issue':'DEV-73','parent_revision':'cd5b2a8dec1fdd53375486852485a898215d9ede','status':'implementation-in-progress','authority':{'principal':'Cooper Corbett','operation':'local implementation, tested commits, pushes and draft PRs','repository':'crcorbett/taxkit','environment':'local pinned macOS/Bun/Chromium; no provider operation'},'implemented':['Canonical whole-source selector covers six extensions across current/future owned root/app/tool/config files','Five exact unexecuted lint-only inputs preserve isolated host/binding-rule contexts; neighbouring files remain strict','Actual six-extension and five-neighbour admission/rejection controls with exact file count and expected rules','Valid CommonJS positive/negative fixtures, separately from ESM syntax','Two new isolated real-verifier mutations reject removed whole-source coverage and broadened fixture exclusions; existing controls/deadlines preserved'],'checks':[],'documentation_impact':{'Change required':['oxlint.config.ts','tools/oxlint/portable-rules.test.ts','tools/quality-workflow/schemas.ts','tools/quality-workflow/release-boundary.test.ts','tools/quality-workflow/fixtures/strict-enforcement-defects.json','docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md','docs/standards/controls.md','do