ercel Fla (file: r13/vercel-flags/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-functions: Vercel Fun (file: r13/vercel-functions/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-queues: Vercel Q (file: r13/vercel-queues/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-sandbox: Vercel San (file: r13/vercel-sandbox/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-services: Vercel S (file: r13/vercel-services/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:vercel-storage: Vercel sto (file: r13/vercel-storage/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:verification: Full-story (file: r13/verification/SKILL.md)\n- vercel:workflow: Vercel Wor (file: r13/workflow/SKILL.md)\n- visualize:visualize: Create vis (file: r5/visualize/1.0.46/skills/visualize/SKILL.md)\n- work-email-assistant: MS365/Outl (file: r1/work-email-assistant/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:create-pet: Create, rep (file: r14/create-pet/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:pets: List, inspe (file: r14/pets/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:update-pet: Inspect, va (file: r14/update-pet/SKILL.md)\n- writing-skills: How to wr (file: r1/ai-for-ui-skills/writing-skills/SKILL.md)\n\u003c/skills_instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003cpermissions instructions\u003e\nFilesystem sandboxing defines which files can be read or written. `sandbox_mode` is `workspace-write`: The sandbox permits reading files, and editing files in `cwd` and `writable_roots`. Editing files in other directories requires approval. Network access is restricted.\n\n`approvals_reviewer` is `auto_review`: Sandbox escalations with require_escalated will be reviewed for compliance with the policy.\nIf a rejection happens, you can continue with a safer alternative, or carry out checks to prove that the action is authorized or low risk before trying again. Complete unaffected work without asking for confirmation. Report anything that remains blocked, clarify why it was blocked by auto-review, inform the user of the risk and ask for approval.\n The writable roots are `/Users/cooper/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/04/01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159`, `/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit`, `/private/tmp`, `/private/var/folders/9q/4hjm8t9d1513m42wgw5tg06r0000gn/T`.\n\u003c/permissions instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e# Collaboration Mode: Default\n\nYou are now in Default mode. Any previous instructions for other modes (e.g. Plan mode) are no longer active.\n\nYour active mode changes only when new developer instructions with a different `\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e...\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e` change it; user requests or tool descriptions do not change mode by themselves. Known mode names are Default and Plan.\n\n## request_user_input availability\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only when it is listed in the available tools for this turn.\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only for optional questions where the answer would materially improve the quality of the work.\n\nIf `request_user_input` returns no answers, continue with best judgment instead of asking again or treating the turn as blocked.\n\nNever use the `request_user_input` tool for permission requests or permission-related escalations.\n\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003crecommended_plugins\u003e\nHere is a list of plugins that are available but not installed.\n\n- Dropbox (app-69b31dc2110c8191b8b47dc98fe5a052@openai-curated-remote)\n- Box (box@openai-curated-remote)\n- Codex Security (codex-security@openai-curated-remote)\n- Slack (slack@openai-curated-remote)\n\u003c/recommended_plugins\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a10791-c238-7b41-9384-e04765d005c9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["generic.developer_instructions","memories.instructions","host_skills.instructions","permissions.instructions","collaboration_mode.instructions","plugins.recommendations"],"turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_role\u003eYou are `/root`, the primary agent in a team of agents collaborating to fulfill the user's goals.\n\nAt the start of your turn, you are the active agent.\nYou can spawn sub-agents to handle subtasks, and those sub-agents can spawn their own sub-agents.\nAll agents in the team, including the agents that you can assign tasks to, are equally intelligent and capable, and have access to the same set of tools.\n\nYou can use `spawn_agent` to create a new agent, `followup_task` to give an existing agent a new task and trigger a turn, and `send_message` to pass a message to a running agent without triggering a turn.\n`send_message` calls may be read by a human, so ensure they are legible. Always put proper spaces between words and/or numbers.\nChild agents can also spawn their own sub-agents.\nYou can decide how much context you want to propagate to your sub-agents with the `fork_turns` parameter.\n\nYou will receive messages in the analysis channel in the form:\n```\nMessage Type: MESSAGE | FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: \u003crecipient\u003e\nSender: \u003cauthor\u003e\nPayload:\n\u003cpayload text\u003e\n```\nThey may be addressed as to=/root\n\nNote that collaboration tools cannot be called from inside `functions.exec`. Call `spawn_agent`, `send_message`, `followup_task`, `wait_agent`, `interrupt_agent`, and `list_agents` only as direct tool calls using the recipient shown in their tool definitions, such as `to=functions.collaboration.spawn_agent`, since they are intentionally absent from the `functions.exec` `tools.*` namespace. Available tools in `functions.exec` are explicitly described with a `tools` namespace in the developer message.\n\nAll agents share the same directory. In detail:\n- All agents have access to the same container and filesystem as you.\n- All agents use the same current working directory.\n- As a result, edits made by one agent are immediately visible to all other agents.\n\nWhen calling `wait_agent`, prefer longer waits (minutes) to avoid busy polling.\n\nThere are 4 available concurrency slots, meaning that up to 4 agents can be active at once, including you.\n\nFull-history forks (`fork_turns` omitted or `\"all\"`) inherit the parent model and reasoning effort and do not accept overrides. Only set `model` or `reasoning_effort` when explicitly requested by the user, applicable `AGENTS.md` instructions, or skill instructions; when doing so, set `fork_turns` to `\"none\"` or a positive integer string.\u003c/multi_agent_role\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a10791-c238-7b41-9384-e05db0924bd8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.role_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_mode\u003eAny earlier instruction enabling proactive multi-agent delegation no longer applies. Do not spawn sub-agents unless the user or applicable AGENTS.md/skill instructions explicitly ask for sub-agents, delegation, or parallel agent work.\u003c/multi_agent_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a10791-c238-7b41-9384-e06fa4697387","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.mode_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"# AGENTS.md instructions for /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit\n\n\u003cINSTRUCTIONS\u003e\n## Strict communication requirement\n\nAlways respond in plain, simple Australian English. Use an ELI5 style and avoid jargon, buzzwords, and unexplained technical terms.\n\nThis rule applies especially when discussing codebases or software engineering. Explain those topics in simple English for a beginner unless the user asks for more detail. Use concrete words and examples. Avoid specialist shorthand and vague terms such as “seams” and “gates” unless the user asks for them or the term is essential and clearly explained.\n\n--- project-doc ---\n\n---\ndocument_type: agent-router\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: repository-maintainers\nlast_reviewed: 2026-07-21\n---\n\n# TaxKit repository guide\n\nTaxKit is the public monorepo for the open-source tax engine, API, SDK, and\ndocumentation site. Start with [`docs/README.md`](docs/README.md), the sole\nmaintainer-document lifecycle and truth-layer router. `CLAUDE.md` points to this\nfile; edit `AGENTS.md` only.\n\n## Operating loop\n\n1. Read `docs/README.md`, then only the semantic owner for the task.\n2. Confirm the claim against code, configuration, Schemas, exports, generated\n   owners, or external readback at the boundary it describes.\n3. Put current implementation intent in a SPEC/task and active execution plan;\n   never reopen completed work as policy.\n4. Update the earliest durable owner and required pointers in the same slice.\n5. Run `bun run check:docs`, `bun run check:runbooks` when operations changed,\n   focused checks, and `bun run verification`;\n   package-facing changes also need an appropriate Changeset.\n6. Retain artifact identity, authority, postconditions, limitations,\n   non-claims, and rollback.\n\nFor any material calculator/rule/schema, SDK/export/example, HTTP/OpenAPI,\npublic MDX/navigation/runtime, package/app, command/CI/versioning/release-proof,\nlifecycle, SPEC, plan, runbook, or skill change, invoke the repository-local\n`$docs-maintainer` route before accepting the slice. Record `Change required`,\n`Preserve`, or evidenced `N/A` for its documentation impact. Scheduled or\nbackground freshness work is report-only candidate output unless a separately\nattached implementation authority names the reviewer and publisher.\n\n## Task routes\n\n- Repository and package topology:\n  [`docs/architecture/README.md`](docs/architecture/README.md), then\n  [`docs/architecture/package-ownership.md`](docs/architecture/package-ownership.md).\n- Effect services and boundaries:\n  [`docs/architecture/effect-services.md`](docs/architecture/effect-services.md)\n  and the applicable package README.\n- API/SDK: [`docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`](docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md),\n  [`apps/api/README.md`](apps/api/README.md), and\n  [`packages/sdk/typescript/README.md`](packages/sdk/typescript/README.md).\n- Calculators/rules/facts: the focused owner under `docs/architecture/` and the\n  owning package README.\n- Frontend/public docs:\n  [`docs/architecture/frontend.md`](docs/architecture/frontend.md),\n  [`docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md`](docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md),\n  and [`apps/docs/README.md`](apps/docs/README.md).\n- Current work: [`docs/product-specs/index.md`](docs/product-specs/index.md) and\n  [`docs/exec-plans/active/README.md`](docs/exec-plans/active/README.md).\n- Standards, tests, and release checks:\n  [`docs/standards/README.md`](docs/standards/README.md) and\n  [`docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md`](docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md).\n- Repeatable release, versioning, packed-consumer and recovery operations:\n  [`docs/runbooks/README.md`](docs/runbooks/README.md) and\n  [`docs/operations/authority-model.md`](docs/operations/authority-model.md).\n- References and audits: [`docs/references/README.md`](docs/references/README.md)\n  and [`docs/documentation-audit/README.md`](docs/documentation-audit/README.md).\n\n## Engineering guardrails\n\n- Use Effect-native Schema, branded identities, Config, services, Layers,\n  tagged errors, collections, Command, and runtime primitives when they own the\n  semantics. Decode unknown/representation ingress once and encode egress at\n  explicit boundaries.\n- Reuse owning Schemas and schema-derived types. Do not mirror raw `id: string`,\n  DTOs, provider types, primitive semantic config, or unchecked SDK output.\n- Keep primary Effects flat, sequential, and pipe-first where that clarifies\n  data flow. Keep one-use mapping/decoding/error logic inline; reject\n  helper/common/utils sprawl and generic SDK callback wrappers.\n- Keep service contracts, live Layers, test Layers, and executable composition\n  separate. Do not run Effects or build live Layers inside domain logic.\n- Provider clients expose named Effect operations, `Config.schema` with\n  redacted secrets, immediate Schema decoding, safe tagged errors without\n  `instanceof`, and live/mock Layers.\n- React composition flows route → policy-owning container → focused leaf.\n  Routes own transport restoration/outcome matching, containers own commands\n  and coordination, and leaves render readonly values/local interaction state.\n- Admit an abstraction only with semantic weight, an owner, a real reuse or\n  substitution point, a simpler call graph, and focused proof.\n\n## Authority and proof\n\nTool access is capability, not authority. Provider, registry, publication,\nrelease, deployment, credential, and destructive operations require a named\nprincipal, operation, resource, environment, approval boundary, receipt,\nrollback/revocation, and readback. Local gates do not prove publication,\nproduction, or external consumer behavior.\n\nUse `bun run check:repository-paths` for checkout portability and\n`bun run verification` for repository closeout. Use `bun run release:check`\nonly for its documented local release-evidence graph; it does not authorize or\nprove publication.\n\n\u003c/INSTRUCTIONS\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003cenvironment_context\u003e\n  \u003ccwd\u003e/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit\u003c/cwd\u003e\n  \u003cshell\u003ezsh\u003c/shell\u003e\n  \u003ccurrent_date\u003e2026-10-05\u003c/current_date\u003e\n  \u003ctimezone\u003eAustralia/Melbourne\u003c/timezone\u003e\n  \u003cfilesystem\u003e\u003cworkspace_roots\u003e\u003croot\u003e/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit\u003c/root\u003e\u003croot\u003e/Users/cooper/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/04/01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159\u003c/root\u003e\u003c/workspace_roots\u003e\u003cpermission_profile type=\"managed\"\u003e\u003cfile_system type=\"restricted\"\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cspecial\u003e:root\u003c/special\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"write\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"write\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/Users/cooper/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/04/01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"write\"\u003e\u003cspecial\u003e:slash_tmp\u003c/special\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"write\"\u003e\u003cspecial\u003e:tmpdir\u003c/special\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/.git\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/Users/cooper/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/04/01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159/.git\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/.agents\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/Users/cooper/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/04/01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159/.agents\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/.codex\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/Users/cooper/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/04/01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159/.codex\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/.aws\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/Users/cooper/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/04/01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159/.aws\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003c/file_system\u003e\u003c/permission_profile\u003e\u003c/filesystem\u003e\n\u003c/environment_context\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a10791-c238-7b41-9384-e075507f67fd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["agents_md.instructions","environments.environment_context"],"turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Continue","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a106da-6a9d-7e63-a676-d613ca83284b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1791116339.869503,"turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},"role":"user","type":"message"}],"replacement_history_metadata":[{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a1055e-500d-7de0-b833-96db813b1de3","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},"revision":"retained_01a1055e-500d-7de0-b833-96f424cd39df"},"user_input_order":0},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_issue"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.list_comments"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_workspace"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_status_updates"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_project"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.save_comment"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","plugin_id":"codex-app-tools@openai-bundled","server_name":"codex_app","tool_name":"attach_artifact"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.save_status_update"}],"status":"complete"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a106da-6a9d-7e63-a676-d613ca83284b","role":"user","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},"revision":"retained_01a106da-6a9d-7e63-a676-d63d307e199e"},"user_input_order":162},{"client_authored":false,"compaction_model_hash":"3000","mcp_attribution":{"sources":[{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_issue"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.list_comments"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_workspace"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_status_updates"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.get_project"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.save_comment"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","plugin_id":"codex-app-tools@openai-bundled","server_name":"codex_app","tool_name":"attach_artifact"},{"connector_id":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","first_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"linear.save_status_update"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":null,"multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","cyber_access_program":"standard","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","realtime_active":false}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_06b7a884f26959d3016ac26dff136c87d0b80bcf04c64c20ac","order":235,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1077d-b0d2-7750-b35f-53473a80cd97","text":"The full test log shows a separate failure in the CommonJS example: its ES-module imports stopped the parser before the strict rules could run. I’m replacing it with valid CommonJS examples so the test proves the intended rule checks.","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_06b7a884f26959d3016ac26ed6bd3087d085a4a96420964061","order":236,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10780-fca4-7cf2-81d0-b8b20ccf229a","text":"All 401 lint tests now pass, including valid CommonJS and checks beside every excluded fixture. Root lint also passes on 397 owned files. I’ve added two temporary-copy checks that must fail when someone removes full source coverage or changes the five exact fixture exclusions into a wildcard.","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_06b7a884f26959d3016ac26f7cb0f087d0a5ec8901b24d38c2","order":237,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10783-835f-7062-adaf-3f2ba57eb19b","text":"All package tests and builds passed. The canonical lint scan now admits all 397 owned source files and reports zero findings, with the five fixture exclusions kept exact. The full closeout run is checking the two new deliberate regressions alongside the existing checks.","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_06b7a884f26959d3016ac27014839487d0809e205bf768575e","order":238,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10785-d555-7d10-8d74-8a14d5f9f419","text":"The broader review is checking where services are created and how work is stopped, beyond what lint can prove. The slower temporary-copy checks are still running. I’m preserving the distinction between DEV-73’s enforcement work and the calculator/interface rebuild already assigned to the next tasks.","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_06b7a884f26959d3016ac270b2502c87d0ba85ccdc913e7f14","order":239,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10788-40a5-7270-9d3d-38327bcf131d","text":"GitHub Quality passed for draft #125 at its exact pushed commit. The next slice’s local tests and builds have passed; its full closeout run is still checking the copied-repository failures. The review is also keeping intentionally bad test input separate from code used by the app.","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_06b7a884f26959d3016ac27119a23487d09c1c34b10cdf8467","order":240,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a10789-d076-7093-9e89-5366f0f523f5","text":"The expanded closeout passed all 32 Quality tests. That includes 13 isolated checks, with both new cases failing for the intended reasons. Both unused-code checks, compiler tasks and browser checks also passed. I’m recording the results and preparing the next draft PR.","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_06b7a884f26959d3016ac271d8559c87d0a6e79ae21889f55a","order":241,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1078c-b944-7673-a7da-7bab3761943f","text":"[Draft PR #126](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/126) is pushed with the tested source-coverage changes. Its GitHub check is running. I’m continuing the final DEV-73 review, with the native API and website work next in the accepted order.","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_06b7a884f26959d3016ac272314fcc87d08830732af08c7804","order":242,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1078e-14a3-7852-a262-bebc305e016a","text":"The review found older Effect examples in the architecture guides, including the old service and configuration syntax. I’m updating those examples from the current source so the guides match the version we’ve tested.","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":243,"user_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a1055e-500d-7de0-b833-96db813b1de3","order":0,"revision":"retained_01a1055e-500d-7de0-b833-96f424cd39df","text":"\n# Files pasted by the user:\n\n## \"--- document_type: execution-plan lifecycle: current authority: supporting owne…\": /Users/cooper/.codex/attachments/f82088a9-b579-462a-9bee-4d3685805660/Pasted text.txt\n\nPasted text contains the user's request.\n\n## My request:\n\n","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a106da-6a9d-7e63-a676-d613ca83284b","order":162,"revision":"retained_01a106da-6a9d-7e63-a676-d63d307e199e","text":"Continue","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"}],"user_messages_incomplete":false,"verified_answers":[]},"window_id":"01a10791-c231-71c2-8abe-8358a180938e","window_number":18}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:39:15.385Z","ordinal":13612,"type":"world_state","payload":{"full":true,"state":{"agents_md":{"directory":"/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","text":"## Strict communication requirement\n\nAlways respond in plain, simple Australian English. Use an ELI5 style and avoid jargon, buzzwords, and unexplained technical terms.\n\nThis rule applies especially when discussing codebases or software engineering. Explain those topics in simple English for a beginner unless the user asks for more detail. Use concrete words and examples. Avoid specialist shorthand and vague terms such as “seams” and “gates” unless the user asks for them or the term is essential and clearly explained.\n\n--- project-doc ---\n\n---\ndocument_type: agent-router\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: repository-maintainers\nlast_reviewed: 2026-07-21\n---\n\n# TaxKit repository guide\n\nTaxKit is the public monorepo for the open-source tax engine, API, SDK, and\ndocumentation site. Start with [`docs/README.md`](docs/README.md), the sole\nmaintainer-document lifecycle and truth-layer router. `CLAUDE.md` points to this\nfile; edit `AGENTS.md` only.\n\n## Operating loop\n\n1. Read `docs/README.md`, then only the semantic owner for the task.\n2. Confirm the claim against code, configuration, Schemas, exports, generated\n   owners, or external readback at the boundary it describes.\n3. Put current implementation intent in a SPEC/task and active execution plan;\n   never reopen completed work as policy.\n4. Update the earliest durable owner and required pointers in the same slice.\n5. Run `bun run check:docs`, `bun run check:runbooks` when operations changed,\n   focused checks, and `bun run verification`;\n   package-facing changes also need an appropriate Changeset.\n6. Retain artifact identity, authority, postconditions, limitations,\n   non-claims, and rollback.\n\nFor any material calculator/rule/schema, SDK/export/example, HTTP/OpenAPI,\npublic MDX/navigation/runtime, package/app, command/CI/versioning/release-proof,\nlifecycle, SPEC, plan, runbook, or skill change, invoke the repository-local\n`$docs-maintainer` route before accepting the slice. Record `Change required`,\n`Preserve`, or evidenced `N/A` for its documentation impact. Scheduled or\nbackground freshness work is report-only candidate output unless a separately\nattached implementation authority names the reviewer and publisher.\n\n## Task routes\n\n- Repository and package topology:\n  [`docs/architecture/README.md`](docs/architecture/README.md), then\n  [`docs/architecture/package-ownership.md`](docs/architecture/package-ownership.md).\n- Effect services and boundaries:\n  [`docs/architecture/effect-services.md`](docs/architecture/effect-services.md)\n  and the applicable package README.\n- API/SDK: [`docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`](docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md),\n  [`apps/api/README.md`](apps/api/README.md), and\n  [`packages/sdk/typescript/README.md`](packages/sdk/typescript/README.md).\n- Calculators/rules/facts: the focused owner under `docs/architecture/` and the\n  owning package README.\n- Frontend/public docs:\n  [`docs/architecture/frontend.md`](docs/architecture/frontend.md),\n  [`docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md`](docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md),\n  and [`apps/docs/README.md`](apps/docs/README.md).\n- Current work: [`docs/product-specs/index.md`](docs/product-specs/index.md) and\n  [`docs/exec-plans/active/README.md`](docs/exec-plans/active/README.md).\n- Standards, tests, and release checks:\n  [`docs/standards/README.md`](docs/standards/README.md) and\n  [`docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md`](docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md).\n- Repeatable release, versioning, packed-consumer and recovery operations:\n  [`docs/runbooks/README.md`](docs/runbooks/README.md) and\n  [`docs/operations/authority-model.md`](docs/operations/authority-model.md).\n- References and audits: [`docs/references/README.md`](docs/references/README.md)\n  and [`docs/documentation-audit/README.md`](docs/documentation-audit/README.md).\n\n## Engineering guardrails\n\n- Use Effect-native Schema, branded identities, Config, services, Layers,\n  tagged errors, collections, Command, and runtime primitives when they own the\n  semantics. Decode unknown/representation ingress once and encode egress at\n  explicit boundaries.\n- Reuse owning Schemas and schema-derived types. Do not mirror raw `id: string`,\n  DTOs, provider types, primitive semantic config, or unchecked SDK output.\n- Keep primary Effects flat, sequential, and pipe-first where that clarifies\n  data flow. Keep one-use mapping/decoding/error logic inline; reject\n  helper/common/utils sprawl and generic SDK callback wrappers.\n- Keep service contracts, live Layers, test Layers, and executable composition\n  separate. Do not run Effects or build live Layers inside domain logic.\n- Provider clients expose named Effect operations, `Config.schema` with\n  redacted secrets, immediate Schema decoding, safe tagged errors without\n  `instanceof`, and live/mock Layers.\n- React composition flows route → policy-owning container → focused leaf.\n  Routes own transport restoration/outcome matching, containers own commands\n  and coordination, and leaves render readonly values/local interaction state.\n- Admit an abstraction only with semantic weight, an owner, a real reuse or\n  substitution point, a simpler call graph, and focused proof.\n\n## Authority and proof\n\nTool access is capability, not authority. Provider, registry, publication,\nrelease, deployment, credential, and destructive operations require a named\nprincipal, operation, resource, environment, approval boundary, receipt,\nrollback/revocation, and readback. Local gates do not prove publication,\nproduction, or external consumer behavior.\n\nUse `bun run check:repository-paths` for checkout portability and\n`bun run verification` for repository closeout. Use `bun run release:check`\nonly for its documented local release-evidence graph; it does not authorize or\nprove publication.\n"},"apps_instructions":false,"collaboration_mode":{"mode":"default","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","instructions":"0a11049b0421e1e86f1e129af8d547a89548a0c3"},"context_window_guidance":"","environments":{"environments":{"local":{"cwd":"/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","status":"available","shell":"zsh"}},"current_date":"2026-10-05","timezone":"Australia/Melbourne","filesystem":"<filesystem><workspace_roots><root>/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit</root><root>/Users/cooper/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/04/01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"managed\"><file_system type=\"restricted\"><entry access=\"read\"><special>:root</special></entry><entry access=\"write\"><path>/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit</path></entry><entry access=\"write\"><path>/Users/cooper/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/04/01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159</path></entry><entry access=\"write\"><special>:slash_tmp</special></entry><entry access=\"write\"><special>:tmpdir</special></entry><entry access=\"read\"><path>/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/.git</path></entry><entry access=\"read\"><path>/Users/cooper/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/04/01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159/.git</path></entry><entry access=\"read\"><path>/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/.agents</path></entry><entry access=\"read\"><path>/Users/cooper/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/04/01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159/.agents</path></entry><entry access=\"read\"><path>/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/.codex</path></entry><entry access=\"read\"><path>/Users/cooper/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/04/01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159/.codex</path></entry><entry access=\"read\"><path>/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/.aws</path></entry><entry access=\"read\"><path>/Users/cooper/.codex/visualizations/2026/10/04/01a1055e-4560-7b33-8