{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:39:45.624Z","ordinal":13649,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c69d1af7-3ec3-4460-8de0-7094ce8a568a","process_id":"28056","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","gh run view 37213423930 --repo crcorbett/taxkit --json databaseId,headSha,status,conclusion,url"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh run view 37213423930 --repo crcorbett/taxkit --json databaseId,headSha,status,conclusion,url"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"databaseId\":37213423930,\"headSha\":\"d9abbb374cec0232636d5eb82696ab1548c6189b\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/actions/runs/37213423930\"}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"databaseId\":37213423930,\"headSha\":\"d9abbb374cec0232636d5eb82696ab1548c6189b\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/actions/runs/37213423930\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":734102292},"formatted_output":"{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"databaseId\":37213423930,\"headSha\":\"d9abbb374cec0232636d5eb82696ab1548c6189b\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/actions/runs/37213423930\"}\n"},"started_at_ms":1791128384890,"completed_at_ms":1791128385624}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:39:45.687Z","ordinal":13650,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10792-3896-7652-8e92-46a74155fa4a","call_id":"call_zgTIFd0kJ9QXUslHOKPMluz7","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":0,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"73b0f4\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.734130875,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":47,\"output\":\"{\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"databaseId\\\":37213423930,\\\"headSha\\\":\\\"d9abbb374cec0232636d5eb82696ab1548c6189b\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/actions/runs/37213423930\\\"}\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"edbb76\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000005417,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1844,\"output\":\"# TaxKit documentation profile\\n\\nRead this profile after `AGENTS.md` and `docs/README.md`. Paths and commands\\nbelow are repository-local; resolve the checkout with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`.\\n\\n## Owner map\\n\\n| Change class                                        | Earliest owner and required pointers                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| Maintainer lifecycle, truth layers, archive routing | `docs/README.md`; architecture, standards, audit and active intent only when affected                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\\n| Calculator rules, facts and schemas                 | owning `packages/calculators` or `packages/rules/**` source/README; relevant `docs/architecture/**`, SDK/API/public docs only when consumers change                                                                                                                                                                             |\\n| SDK exports and examples                            | `packages/sdk/typescript` source/export map and README; packed-consumer/downstream proof; `docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\\n| HTTP/OpenAPI                                        | `packages/api/http/src/**` schemas and `src/openapi.ts`; generated snapshot `packages/api/http/__snapshots__/openapi.json` through `test:openapi`; `packages/api/http/README.md`, `apps/api/README.md`, and API/SDK architecture only when their contracts change                                                               |\\n| Public MDX/navigation/lifecycle                     | `packages/docs-content/content/**`, `packages/docs-content/navigation.json`, and `tools/documentation/owner-policy.json`; `published` requires one exact `public.statusDecision.acceptanceRecords` binding to a strict addressable record, with the durable lifecycle decision routed from `docs/documentation-audit/hgi-207/public-mdx-lifecycle.json` |\\n| Public docs runtime/generated Fumadocs              | `apps/docs/README.md`, `packages/docs-content/source.config.ts`, `packages/docs-content/.source`, and `packages/docs-fumadocs`; regenerate/check through the owning commands and never hand-edit generated output                                                                                                               |\\n| Package/app roots                                   | owning package/app README, package ownership architecture, root routes only when discoverability changes                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\\n| Commands, CI, versioning and release readiness      | `package.json`, workflow/command owner, `docs/standards/versioning.md`, `docs/runbooks/README.md`, testing-quality architecture and proof owner                                                                                                                                                                                 |\\n| Runbooks, authority, proof and history              | exactly five target-owned procedures routed by `docs/runbooks/README.md`; `docs/operations/authority-model.md`; `tools/documentation/runbook-contract.json`; sanitized `docs/evidence/releases/**`, `docs/evidence/deployments/**`, or dated `docs/documentation-audit/**`; preserve provenance and non-claims                             |\\n| PRD and implementation                              | target SPEC, sibling tasks and active plan; local `prd-writer`, `prd-review`, `prd-implementer` invoke this skill                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\\n\\nPublic `published` needs an exact accepted record and one-to-one binding in\\n`tools/documentation/owner-policy.json`; its `targetPath` must equal the public\\npath. Navigation remains independently draft unless it receives its own exact\\nrecord and binding.\\nGenerated source is authoritative over checked output. Repository evidence is\\nnot provider, registry, deployment, public-site or consumer proof.\\n\\n## Commands and boundaries\\n\\n- Baseline documentation/path/skill checks: `bun run test:skills`, `bun run\\ncheck:docs`, `bun run check:runbooks`, `bun run check:repository-paths`.\\n- Harness foundation checks: `bun run check:harness-governance:types`, `bun run\\n  test:harness-governance`, and `bun run check:harness-governance`. The runtime\\n  gate reads only repository-local profile, audit, receipt, skill, link, and\\n  critical-journey owners.\\n- Full local closeout: `bun run verification` and `git diff --check`.\\n- Public content/runtime: `bun run docs:validate`, `bun run docs:build`,\\n  `bun run --filter=docs test:browser` when applicable.\\n- SDK package boundary: `bun run --filter=@taxkit/sdk check-packed-artifact`\\n  and `bun run --filter=@taxkit/sdk validate:downstream` when applicable.\\n- Release evidence: `bun run release:check` is local proof only; versioning,\\n  publication and deployment remain separately authorized operations.\\n- Runbook contract: `bun run check:runbooks` is inspect-only and writes the\\n  bounded ignored `tmp/runbook-validation-report.json`; it never runs a\\n  documented procedure or establishes external state.\\n\\nFor each check, state its observable postcondition and what it does not prove.\\nKeep background freshness reports as candidates until an attached implementation\\nauthority, responsible reviewer and separately named publisher accept them.\\n\\n## Clean-slate compatibility and implementation\\n\\nThe local root manifest and lockfile select stable Effect 4.0.0 and TypeScript\\n7.0.2. Canonical skill templates may retain their upstream rc.117 qualification;\\nthat reference snapshot does not downgrade TaxKit or prove an app/provider\\nmigration. Check installed exports and the active clean-slate plan before use.\\n\\nThe complete local skill collection is pinned by\\n`tools/skills/canonical-skill-baseline.json` to Commonplace development-workflows\\n0.6.1. It includes `linear`, `strict-effect-ts` and `alchemy-iac`, with relative\\nClaude links. Use the Linear skill for tracked task status/evidence. The active\\n`docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md` distinguishes skill adoption\\nfrom pending full strict enforcement, Atom integration and application work.\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":2,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"436471\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007792,\"exit_code\":1,\"original_token_count\":3675,\"output\":\"      ],\\n      \\\"dependsOn\\\": [],\\n      \\\"goal\\\": \\\"Every planned removal has an addressable retained source/evidence/rollback owner.\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": [\\n        \\\"Confirm the exact branch/source and incorporate the completed Alchemy/Doppler work without overwriting another chat's changes.\\\",\\n        \\\"Inventory retained tax packages, authored content, historical/binary evidence, deployment IDs, existing public URLs and rollback artifacts. Record each removal/replacement disposition before deleting wiring.\\\",\\n        \\\"Create the active execution plan only after final shared understanding. Record current golden outputs, supported scope and the failed offline frozen-install proof; establish its actual diagnostic and recovery.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"outputs\\\": [\\n        \\\"docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md and its active index entry\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/retention-manifest.json and baseline receipt\\\",\\n        \\\"Updated SPEC/task status and explicit infrastructure handover identity\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"implementationPrompt\\\": \\\"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\\\",\\n      \\\"mandatoryVerification\\\": [\\n        \\\"bun run check:docs\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run check:runbooks\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run --filter=@taxkit/core test\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run --filter=@taxkit/calculators test\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run test:quality-workflow\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run verification\\\",\\n        \\\"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"browserVerification\\\": [],\\n      \\\"qualityAudits\\\": [\\n        \\\"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\\\",\\n        \\\"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\\\",\\n        \\\"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\\\",\\n        \\\"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"parentAudit\\\": {\\n        \\\"required\\\": true,\\n        \\\"basis\\\": \\\"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\\\",\\n        \\\"recovery\\\": \\\"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"completionCriteria\\\": [\\n        \\\"Every planned removal has an addressable retained source/evidence/rollback owner.\\\",\\n        \\\"Other work is integrated or explicitly outside the write scope; cloud ownership is not inferred from local Git.\\\",\\n        \\\"The previous install failure is diagnosed or remains a named prerequisite; no green closeout claim hides it.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"commitAfterPassing\\\": true,\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": [\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/retention-manifest.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-baseline.json\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CSF-T002\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Qualify current versions, exports and strict enforcement\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"in_progress\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"foundation\\\",\\n      \\\"acceptedFindingIds\\\": [],\\n      \\\"requirementIds\\\": [\\n        \\\"CSF-001\\\",\\n        \\\"CSF-002\\\",\\n        \\\"CSF-010\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"dependsOn\\\": [\\n        \\\"CSF-T001\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"goal\\\": \\\"The selected graph is actually installed and built; provisional research is not presented as compatibility proof.\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": [\\n        \\\"Resolve current official releases, including stable Effect module paths, then qualify one exact Bun/TypeScript/React/Atom/Alchemy/tooling graph in a fresh scratch fixture before integrating it.\\\",\\n        \\\"Qualify the proposed exact Scheduler peer-metadata correction, or use a newer upstream fix. Preserve valid tax outputs; update package exports/types/imports and versioning consequences deliberately.\\\",\\n        \\\"Adopt the complete canonical current repository skills (0.6.1 successor of the designed 0.6.0 baseline) and declared TaxKit profiles/receipts, including the required Linear skill folder and Claude link without creating provider projects/issues. Merge all eleven portable strict Effect rules, including no-imperative-collections, and workspace-export direction into the actual lint config across source/tests/tools/config/infrastructure. Reuse baseline mutation/loop/collection checks; add only evidenced gaps and readonly-value checks. Exact Promise-returning/runtime host exceptions do not exempt other constructs.\\\",\\n        \\\"Extend actual-command positive/negative fixtures under moved paths; assert admitted file counts, exit codes and expected rules. Prove removing/disabling required rules or broadening exact assignment/method exceptions fails the verifier. Refresh Turbo read/input/cache ownership, Knip inventories and CI commands; keep explicit generated/vendor exclusions.\\\",\\n        \\\"Qualify canonical rejection of let/var, assignments/writes/delete/updates, loops, native array traversal including forEach and mutators/constructors, transient Effect collection modes, switch and manual tag checks. Use existing restrictions and focused corrections for Object/Reflect writes, mutable class/contract values, WeakMap/WeakSet and demonstrated destructured/local aliases. Computed member access is already rejected by no-unchecked-index. Accept persistent collections, pure immutable Effect-managed state and qualified Alchemy Output operations. Preserve/qualify stronger lexical runtime callback/reference checks outside exact hosts. Review helper purpose, Schema ownership and pipe/flat-program call graphs separately; lint alone is not semantic proof.\\\",\\n        \\\"Cover owned .ts/.tsx/.js/.jsx/.mjs/.cjs files, including retained JavaScript policy tools, in actual lint scope; convert to checked TypeScript where necessary instead of treating the scaffold TypeScript-only override as complete. Executable MDX expressions/imports remain with the existing content-policy owner.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"outputs\\\": [\\n        \\\"package.json, bun.lock, turbo.json, tsconfig*, oxlint.config.ts, oxfmt.config.ts, Knip config and .github/workflows/quality.yml\\\",\\n        \\\"tools/oxlint/** policy/fixtures, tools/effect-language-service/** and tools/skills/canonical-skill-baseline.json\\\",\\n        \\\"Canonical .agents/skills/** copies with explicit local profiles; AGENTS.md, README.md and affected package READMEs\\\",\\n        \\\"Qualified version receipt, any exact-version patches/**, applicable .changeset/*.md and owning standards/architecture\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"implementationPrompt\\\": \\\"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\\\",\\n      \\\"mandatoryVerification\\\": [\\n        \\\"bun install --frozen-lockfile\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run format:check\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run lint\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run test:oxlint\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run check:effect-language-service\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run test:skills\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run check:harness-governance\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run check-types\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run test\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run build\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run verification\\\",\\n        \\\"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"browserVerification\\\": [\\n        \\\"Qualify Atom server rendering/hydration, scheduled/cancelled updates, rapid input changes, strict-mode remount and final disposal on the selected React/Scheduler graph.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"qualityAudits\\\": [\\n        \\\"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\\\",\\n        \\\"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\\\",\\n        \\\"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\\\",\\n        \\\"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"parentAudit\\\": {\\n        \\\"required\\\": true,\\n        \\\"basis\\\": \\\"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\\\",\\n        \\\"recovery\\\": \\\"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"completionCriteria\\\": [\\n        \\\"The selected graph is actually installed and built; provisional research is not presented as compatibility proof.\\\",\\n        \\\"Deliberate bad fixtures fail with the expected rule in every owned path group, and documented valid adapters pass.\\\",\\n        \\\"Retained valid calculations produce unchanged golden results; breaking interfaces have an appropriate Changeset.\\\",\\n        \\\"No owned application, domain, test, script or infrastructure workflow retains forbidden mutation or imperative loops. Every necessary host construct has an exact owner/containment/test/removal record; copied reference templates do not provide an escape for executable owned code.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"commitAfterPassing\\\": true,\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": [\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-stable-dependency-qualification.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-version-observations.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-medicare-scope-conflict.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-canonical-skills.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-atom-qualification.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-quality-workflow-boundaries.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lint-binding-policies.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lint-route-policy.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-enforcement-canaries.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lexical-policy-gaps.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-documentation-tools.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-evaluation-tools.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-artifacts.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-credentials.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-workflow-checks.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-receipt-policies.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lint-file-deadlines.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-retained-deployment-proof.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-inventory-checks.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-typed-lint-policies.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-release-script-boundaries.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-client-lifetime.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-checking-scripts.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-api-app-boundaries.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-docs-import-checker.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-docs-runtime-tests.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-quality-fixture-deadlines.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-docs-app-hosts.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-infrastructure-native-tests.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-web-app-hosts.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-hosted-docs-native-proof.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-built-worker-proof.json\\\",\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-owned-source-coverage.json\\\"\\n      ]\\ncat: packages/core/src/scenario.ts: No such file or directory\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":3,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"81c099\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000005875,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2874,\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"taxkit\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"workspaces\\\": {\\n    \\\"packages\\\": [\\n      \\\"apps/*\\\",\\n      \\\"packages/*\\\",\\n      \\\"packages/api/*\\\",\\n      \\\"packages/sdk/*\\\",\\n      \\\"packages/rules/au/*\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"catalog\\\": {\\n      \\\"@effect/platform-bun\\\": \\\"4.0.0\\\",\\n      \\\"@effect/platform-node\\\": \\\"4.0.0\\\",\\n      \\\"@effect/vitest\\\": \\\"4.0.0\\\",\\n      \\\"@cloudflare/vite-plugin\\\": \\\"1.62.5\\\",\\n      \\\"@tanstack/react-router\\\": \\\"1.170.41\\\",\\n      \\\"@tanstack/react-start\\\": \\\"1.168.60\\\",\\n      \\\"@types/bun\\\": \\\"1.4.2\\\",\\n      \\\"@types/node\\\": \\\"26.6.4\\\",\\n      \\\"@types/react\\\": \\\"19.3.0\\\",\\n      \\\"@types/react-dom\\\": \\\"19.3.0\\\",\\n      \\\"@vitejs/plugin-react\\\": \\\"6.1.1\\\",\\n      \\\"alchemy\\\": \\\"2.0.0-beta.80\\\",\\n      \\\"effect\\\": \\\"4.0.0\\\",\\n      \\\"nitro\\\": \\\"3.0.260903-beta\\\",\\n      \\\"react\\\": \\\"19.3.0\\\",\\n      \\\"react-dom\\\": \\\"19.3.0\\\",\\n      \\\"typescript\\\": \\\"7.0.2\\\",\\n      \\\"vite\\\": \\\"8.3.2\\\",\\n      \\\"vitest\\\": \\\"5.0.3\\\",\\n      \\\"wrangler\\\": \\\"4.147.0\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\",\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"turbo run build\\\",\\n    \\\"changeset\\\": \\\"changeset\\\",\\n    \\\"check\\\": \\\"ultracite check --type-aware\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:docs:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs:task\\\": \\\"bun run tools/documentation/check.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:docs-deployment:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment:task\\\": \\\"bun --conditions=source run tools/docs-deployment/check.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-automation\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:docs-deployment-automation:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-automation:task\\\": \\\"bun --conditions=source run tools/docs-deployment/automation.check.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-inventory\\\": \\\"CI=1 turbo run //#check:docs-deployment-inventory:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-inventory:task\\\": \\\"bun --conditions=source run tools/docs-deployment/inventory.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-workflow-proof\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:docs-deployment-workflow-proof:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-workflow-proof:task\\\": \\\"bun --conditions=source run tools/docs-deployment/workflow-proof-check.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-workflow-input\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:docs-deployment-workflow-input:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-workflow-input:task\\\": \\\"bun --conditions=source run tools/docs-deployment/workflow-input-check.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-workflow-run\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:docs-deployment-workflow-run:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-workflow-run:task\\\": \\\"bun --conditions=source run tools/docs-deployment/workflow-run-check.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-workflow-plan\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:docs-deployment-workflow-plan:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-workflow-plan:task\\\": \\\"bun --conditions=source run tools/docs-deployment/workflow-plan-check.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-workflow-teardown-proof\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:docs-deployment-workflow-teardown-proof:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-workflow-teardown-proof:task\\\": \\\"bun --conditions=source run tools/docs-deployment/workflow-teardown-proof-check.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment:types\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:docs-deployment:types:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment:types:task\\\": \\\"tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.alchemy.json\\\",\\n    \\\"check:doppler-custody\\\": \\\"bun --no-env-file run tools/docs-deployment/doppler-custody.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-tools:types\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:docs-deployment-tools:types:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs-deployment-tools:types:task\\\": \\\"tsc --noEmit -p tools/docs-deployment/tsconfig.json\\\",\\n    \\\"check:skills:types\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:skills:types:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:skills:types:task\\\": \\\"tsc --noEmit -p tools/skills/tsconfig.json\\\",\\n    \\\"check:oxlint:types\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:oxlint:types:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:oxlint:types:task\\\": \\\"tsc --noEmit -p tools/oxlint/tsconfig.json\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs:types\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:docs:types:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:docs:types:task\\\": \\\"tsc --noEmit -p tools/documentation/tsconfig.json\\\",\\n    \\\"check:effect-language-service\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:effect-language-service:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:effect-language-service:task\\\": \\\"effect-tsgo diagnostics --project tools/effect-language-service/tsconfig.json && tsc --noEmit -p tools/effect-language-service/tsconfig.json\\\",\\n    \\\"check:harness-governance\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:harness-governance:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:harness-governance:task\\\": \\\"bun --conditions=source run tools/governance/check.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check:harness-governance:types\\\": \\\"tsc --noEmit -p tools/governance/tsconfig.json\\\",\\n    \\\"check:harness-foundation-epoch\\\": \\\"bun --conditions=source run tools/evals/harness-foundation/check.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check:harness-foundation-epoch:types\\\": \\\"tsc --noEmit -p tools/evals/tsconfig.json\\\",\\n    \\\"check:hgi-206\\\": \\\"bun --conditions=source run tools/evals/hgi-206/check.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check:runbooks\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:runbooks:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:runbooks:task\\\": \\\"bun --conditions=source run tools/documentation/runbook-check.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check-types\\\": \\\"turbo run check-types\\\",\\n    \\\"check:repository-paths\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:repository-paths:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:repository-paths:task\\\": \\\"bun run tools/repository-paths/check.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check:repository-paths:types\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:repository-paths:types:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:repository-paths:types:task\\\": \\\"tsc --noEmit -p tools/repository-paths/tsconfig.json\\\",\\n    \\\"check:quality-workflow\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:quality-workflow:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:quality-workflow:task\\\": \\\"bun run tools/quality-workflow/check.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"check:quality-workflow:types\\\": \\\"turbo run //#check:quality-workflow:types:task\\\",\\n    \\\"check:quality-workflow:types:task\\\": \\\"tsc --noEmit -p tools/quality-workflow/tsconfig.json\\\",\\n    \\\"clean\\\": \\\"turbo run clean\\\",\\n    \\\"dev\\\": \\\"portless proxy start --https && turbo run dev --filter=api --filter=web\\\",\\n    \\\"docs:build\\\": \\\"turbo run build --filter=docs\\\",\\n    \\\"docs:dev:cloudflare\\\": \\\"bun --no-env-file run tools/docs-deployment/local-doppler.runtime.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"docs:dev:cloudflare:internal\\\": \\\"alchemy dev --env-file tools/docs-deployment/no-local-env\\\",\\n    \\\"docs:dev:vite\\\": \\\"bun run --filter=docs dev:vite\\\",\\n    \\\"docs:validate\\\": \\\"turbo run validate --filter=@taxkit/docs-content\\\",\\n    \\\"fix\\\": \\\"ultracite fix --type-aware\\\",\\n    \\\"format\\\": \\\"oxfmt -c oxfmt.config.ts --write . --no-error-on-unmatched-pattern\\\",\\n    \\\"format:check\\\": \\\"turbo run //#format:check:task\\\",\\n    \\\"format:check:task\\\": \\\"oxfmt -c oxfmt.config.ts --check . --no-error-on-unmatched-pattern\\\",\\n    \\\"knip\\\": \\\"turbo run //#knip:task\\\",\\n    \\\"knip:task\\\": \\\"knip --no-progress --no-config-hints\\\",\\n    \\\"knip:production\\\": \\\"turbo run //#knip:production:task\\\",\\n    \\\"knip:production:task\\\": \\\"knip --production --config knip.production.json --no-gitignore --no-progress --no-config-hints\\\",\\n    \\\"lint\\\": \\\"turbo run //#lint:task\\\",\\n    \\\"lint:task\\\": \\\"bun run lint:boundary-directives && oxlint -c oxlint.config.ts . --disable-nested-config --no-error-on-unmatched-pattern\\\",\\n    \\\"lint:boundary-directives\\\": \\\"oxlint -c oxlint.config.ts . --allow=taxkit/no-decoding-outside-boundaries --allow=taxkit/no-route-transport-restore-outside-consumers --report-unused-disable-directives-severity=error --disable-nested-config --no-error-on-unmatched-pattern\\\",\\n    \\\"prepare\\\": \\\"effect-tsgo patch\\\",\\n    \\\"release:check\\\": \\\"bun run --filter=@taxkit/scripts release:check\\\",\\n    \\\"release:present\\\": \\\"bun run --filter=@taxkit/scripts release:present\\\",\\n    \\\"test\\\": \\\"bun run test:documentation && bun run test:repository-paths && bun run test:docs-boundaries && bun run test:oxlint && turbo run test\\\",\\n    \\\"test:documentation\\\": \\\"turbo run //#test:documentation:task\\\",\\n    \\\"test:documentation:task\\\": \\\"bun --bun vitest run --config tools/vitest.config.ts tools/documentation\\\",\\n    \\\"test:docs-deployment\\\": \\\"turbo run //#test:docs-deployment:task\\\",\\n    \\\"test:docs-deployment:task\\\": \\\"bun --conditions=source node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run --config tools/vitest.config.ts tools/docs-deployment\\\",\\n    \\\"test:docs-boundaries\\\": \\\"turbo run //#test:docs-