{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:40:41.200Z","ordinal":13661,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_06b7a884f26959d3016ac2734aec7087d097e73d05f7163914","status":"completed","call_id":"call_IXo4pFn9JbAyYM2coU8jKpF6","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat > /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/update-foundation-guides.py <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nroot=Path.cwd()\\ndef write(path,text):\\n    (root/path).write_text(text)\\ndef metadata(owner,trigger):\\n    return f'---\\\\ndocument_type: architecture\\\\nlifecycle: current\\\\nauthority: canonical\\\\nowner: {owner}\\\\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-05\\\\nreview_trigger: {trigger}\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n'\\nwrite('docs/architecture/facts.md', metadata('taxkit-facts-owner','fact Schema, identity, descriptor, authority or question metadata change')+'''# Facts\\n\\nA fact is a named value required or produced by a calculation. Its owning rule\\npackage defines the value Schema, the Effect service identity and the descriptor\\nused to check the calculation graph. Consumers reuse those definitions.\\n\\n## Fact pattern\\n\\nThe current [pay facts](../../packages/rules/au/pay/src/facts/pay.ts) define\\n`GrossPay`, `PayPeriod`, `GrossPayFact` and `GrossPayDescriptor` together.\\n`GrossPay` contains canonical `Money` and a checked pay period. The service\\nuses the installed Effect 4 form:\\n\\n```ts\\nexport class GrossPayFact extends Context.Service<GrossPayFact, GrossPay>()(\\n  \\\"taxkit/rules-au-pay/fact/GrossPay\\\"\\n) {}\\n```\\n\\nThis is an excerpt from the owning module; its imports and value Schema belong\\nthere. Keep the service identity stable. Another value with similar fields\\ncannot supply a different fact service.\\n\\n## Descriptors and authority\\n\\nImport `FactDescriptor` and `makeFactDescriptor` from `@taxkit/core`; do not\\ncopy their fields into a second interface. The [descriptor owner](../../packages/core/src/facts/descriptor.ts)\\nkeeps the value Schema and `Context.Key<Self, Value>` tied to the same value\\ntype. Its readonly fields include a branded fact ID, title, authority and\\noptional `FactQuestion`. This generic relation supports graph tools while\\nEffect's dependency type still decides what execution needs.\\n\\n`FactAuthority` admits three values:\\n\\n- `input`: the caller supplies a typed input accepted by the calculator.\\n- `derived`: a rule produces the fact from other facts or parameters.\\n- `parameter`: a service supplies a tax-year table, rate or constant.\\n\\nCallers must construct the selected calculator's canonical input facts before\\nrunning it. Metadata does not supply missing values.\\n\\n## Dates, money and rounding\\n\\nReuse the [core date primitives](../../packages/core/src/primitives/date.ts)\\nand the selected calculator's input Schema. Keep calculation dates, payment\\ndates and tax years distinct where that calculator supports them. FBT and\\nother proposed date dimensions do not establish an implemented calculator\\ncontract; add them at their owning Schema when that work is accepted.\\n\\n[Money](../../packages/core/src/primitives/money.ts) uses integer cents. Its\\nnumber representation is checked by the owning Schema; a bare number is not\\ncanonical money. Keep final amounts in that representation rather than using\\nfloating-point dollar arithmetic.\\n\\nReuse [RoundingMode](../../packages/core/src/primitives/rounding.ts) and the\\nowning rounding operations. The closed modes are `none`,\\n`round-to-nearest-cent`, `floor-cent`, `ceil-cent`, `floor-dollar`,\\n`ceil-dollar` and `ato-withholding-rounding`, defined by `Schema.Literals`.\\nRecord the chosen policy in calculation trace output.\\n\\nDo not invent defaults that materially change tax results, such as whether a\\nperson has study debt, claims the tax-free threshold or has health insurance.\\nA supported default must belong to the input Schema or an explicit rule.\\n\\n## Question metadata\\n\\n`FactQuestion` is the [core-owned Schema class](../../packages/core/src/facts/descriptor.ts).\\nIt carries a branded `FactQuestionId`, `prompt`, optional `helpText` and an\\n`inputKind` of `money`, `boolean` or `selection`. Reuse this class and the\\nfact descriptor's question rather than introducing a competing question type.\\n\\nQuestion metadata describes supported input collection. It does not prove that\\na UI or CLI can automatically collect every missing fact; that behaviour needs\\nits own application implementation and tests.\\n''')\\nwrite('docs/architecture/rules-and-parameters.md', metadata('taxkit-rules-and-parameters-owner','rule Layer, descriptor, parameter or rule-pack composition change')+'''# Rules and parameters\\n\\nRules are Effect Layers that produce named facts from other facts and parameter\\nservices. Descriptors explain that graph; the typed dependencies drive execution.\\n\\n## Rule pattern\\n\\nThe current [TaxablePayLive](../../packages/rules/au/pay/src/rules/taxable-pay.ts)\\nuses `Layer.effect(TaxablePayFact)(...)` and reads `GrossPayFact` inside its\\nEffect. It produces canonical `TaxablePay` with a `TraceNode`. In the retained\\nimplementation taxable pay equals gross pay: salary sacrifice is not yet part\\nof this rule. Do not describe a proposed input as an existing dependency.\\n\\nAfter the rule pack and scenario Layers are supplied, a calculator must have no\\nremaining dependencies. A missing fact or parameter remains visible in Effect's\\nrequired service type.\\n\\n## Rule descriptors\\n\\nReuse `RuleDescriptor` and `makeRuleDescriptor` from `@taxkit/core`.\\nThe [descriptor owner](../../packages/core/src/rules/descriptor.ts) ties the\\nLayer's output, errors and required services to readonly fact/parameter\\ndescriptors. It owns branded rule IDs, titles, source references and the\\n`required` or `not-required` source policy. Do not maintain a second descriptor\\ninterface or add fields that the owning contract does not expose.\\n\\nDescriptors must match the actual Layer. The core graph validator and owning\\nrule-pack tests check missing dependencies, competing providers and source\\nrequirements; static descriptor metadata alone is not execution proof.\\n\\n## Parameter services\\n\\nA parameter table belongs to its own service, separate from the algorithm that\\nuses it. The current [Schedule 1 owner](../../packages/rules/au/pay/src/parameters/schedule1.ts)\\ndefines checked rows, a table Schema and the service:\\n\\n```ts\\nexport class AtoSchedule1Table extends Context.Service<\\n  AtoSchedule1Table,\\n  Schedule1Table\\n>()(\\\"taxkit/rules-au-pay/parameter/AtoSchedule1Table\\\") {}\\n```\\n\\nThis is an excerpt from the owning module. Its `AtoSchedule1_2025_26_Live`\\nLayer supplies the canonical table. PAYG algorithms require the service rather\\nthan reading a year-specific table from a global variable.\\n\\nParameter descriptors include source references and the table's effective\\ntax-year period. Graph validation reports overlapping periods for different\\ndescriptors with the same parameter ID, preventing two competing tables from\\nsilently supplying the same service and year.\\n\\n## Rule packs\\n\\nA rule pack composes existing Layers and keeps descriptors, sources and golden\\nexamples with their owning modules. Reuse the actual public exports; a pack\\ndoes not require a namespace containing duplicate metadata or a made-up graph\\nbuilder.\\n\\nThe current [take-home-pay pack](../../packages/rules/au/pay/src/rule-pack/au-take-home-pay-2025-26.ts)\\ncomposes:\\n\\n```ts\\nexport const AuTakeHomePay2025_26_Live = NetPayLive.pipe(\\n  Layer.provideMerge(PayWithholdingsLedgerLive),\\n  Layer.provideMerge(PaygWithholdingLive),\\n  Layer.provideMerge(TaxablePayLive),\\n  Layer.provideMerge(AtoSchedule1_2025_26_Live)\\n);\\n```\\n\\nThis excerpt uses the owning module's imports. The caller supplies\\n`GrossPayFact` and `TaxFreeThresholdClaimedFact` through its scenario Layer.\\nThe base withholding ledger includes PAYG only; a pack adding STSL replaces\\nthat ledger with the owner that requires both components. Compose typed Layers\\nrather than using untyped plugin arrays.\\n\\n## Algorithm and data separation\\n\\nKeep a year's checked parameter data separate from the reusable algorithm.\\nA yearly change can then update that data and its source references while\\nfocused tests check the resulting calculation. Changes to formulas, thresholds,\\nrounding or supported inputs still require rule review and golden-result proof.\\n\\nUse schema-checked data tables where they express the actual rule, including\\nmarginal rates, coefficient formulas, caps and ledger components. Add a shared\\nrule builder only when it owns repeated policy and makes the call graph simpler;\\nthe [abstraction admission owner](../design-docs/abstraction-admission.md)\\ndefines that review.\\n''')\\np=root/'docs/architecture/effect-services.md'\\ns=p.read_text().replace('last_reviewed: 2026-10-04','last_reviewed: 2026-10-05').replace('`Context.Tag` services','`Context.Service` services').replace('`Schema.make` is valid construction','The owning Schema’s `make` is valid construction').replace('`Schema.TaggedErrorClass`','`Schema.TaggedError`')\\ns=s.replace('repository tools; website applications remain outside this rollout.','repository tools and both website applications. The strict override covers all\\\\nowned TypeScript and JavaScript extensions. Five unexecuted upstream lint-input\\\\nfixtures have exact strict-only exclusions; their neighbouring files still\\\\nreceive the full policy. The [testing owner](testing-and-quality.md) records\\\\nthe coverage and actual-command rejection proof.')\\ns=s.replace('''program.pipe(\\n  Effect.mapError(\\n    (cause) =>\\n      new BoundaryError({\\n        cause,\\n        message: `Failed to load boundary config: ${cause.message}`,\\n      })\\n  )\\n);''','''program.pipe(\\n  Effect.mapError(\\n    () => new BoundaryError({ message: \\\"Boundary settings are invalid\\\" })\\n  )\\n);''')\\ns=s.replace('''Use `@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain(...)`''','''The web scaffold owns its server and browser health-client runtimes in the\\n[web runtime module](../../apps/web/src/lib/runtime.ts). Its public facade\\nexposes the named health operation and disposal, while route cancellation\\nreaches the HTTP request through Effect interruption. Browser configuration\\nreceives only the checked public input selected by the build configuration.\\nThe SDK owns one runtime per client, with caller disposal and bounded one-shot\\nhelpers; see the [SDK lifetime owner](api-and-sdk.md#typescript-sdk-facade).\\n\\nUse `@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain(...)`''')\\ns=s.replace('- Use `Effect.Schema` for boundary and persisted values.','- Use `Schema` from `effect` for boundary and persisted values.')\\np.write_text(s)\\nfor rel in ['docs/architecture/README.md','docs/architecture/package-boundaries.md']:\\n    p=root/rel;s=p.read_text().replace('Context.Tag','Context.Service')\\n    if 'status: canonical' in s:\\n        s=metadata('taxkit-package-boundaries-owner','package responsibility, dependency direction or public export change')+s.split('---\\\\n',2)[2].lstrip()\\n    else:s=s.replace('last_reviewed: 2026-07-20','last_reviewed: 2026-10-05')\\n    p.write_text(s)\\nPY\\npython3 /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/update-foundation-guides.py\",max_output_tokens:2000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","create_time":1791128392.111371}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:40:41.204Z","ordinal":13662,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","session_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","root_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","response_id":"resp_06b7a884f26959d3016ac27347fe1487d09d5a9f4afc7c5898","usage":{"input_tokens":84370,"cached_input_tokens":80384,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2574,"reasoning_output_tokens":29,"total_tokens":86944},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":262216290,"cached_input_tokens":257089152,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1362990,"reasoning_output_tokens":547050,"total_tokens":263579280},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":262216290,"cached_input_tokens":257089152,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1362990,"reasoning_output_tokens":547050,"total_tokens":263579280}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:40:41.321Z","ordinal":13663,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3e823ee9-2f04-490e-9776-f026dae29024","process_id":"43490","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat > /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/update-foundation-guides.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot=Path.cwd()\ndef write(path,text):\n    (root/path).write_text(text)\ndef metadata(owner,trigger):\n    return f'---\\ndocument_type: architecture\\nlifecycle: current\\nauthority: canonical\\nowner: {owner}\\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-05\\nreview_trigger: {trigger}\\n---\\n\\n'\nwrite('docs/architecture/facts.md', metadata('taxkit-facts-owner','fact Schema, identity, descriptor, authority or question metadata change')+'''# Facts\n\nA fact is a named value required or produced by a calculation. Its owning rule\npackage defines the value Schema, the Effect service identity and the descriptor\nused to check the calculation graph. Consumers reuse those definitions.\n\n## Fact pattern\n\nThe current [pay facts](../../packages/rules/au/pay/src/facts/pay.ts) define\n`GrossPay`, `PayPeriod`, `GrossPayFact` and `GrossPayDescriptor` together.\n`GrossPay` contains canonical `Money` and a checked pay period. The service\nuses the installed Effect 4 form:\n\n```ts\nexport class GrossPayFact extends Context.Service<GrossPayFact, GrossPay>()(\n  \"taxkit/rules-au-pay/fact/GrossPay\"\n) {}\n```\n\nThis is an excerpt from the owning module; its imports and value Schema belong\nthere. Keep the service identity stable. Another value with similar fields\ncannot supply a different fact service.\n\n## Descriptors and authority\n\nImport `FactDescriptor` and `makeFactDescriptor` from `@taxkit/core`; do not\ncopy their fields into a second interface. The [descriptor owner](../../packages/core/src/facts/descriptor.ts)\nkeeps the value Schema and `Context.Key<Self, Value>` tied to the same value\ntype. Its readonly fields include a branded fact ID, title, authority and\noptional `FactQuestion`. This generic relation supports graph tools while\nEffect's dependency type still decides what execution needs.\n\n`FactAuthority` admits three values:\n\n- `input`: the caller supplies a typed input accepted by the calculator.\n- `derived`: a rule produces the fact from other facts or parameters.\n- `parameter`: a service supplies a tax-year table, rate or constant.\n\nCallers must construct the selected calculator's canonical input facts before\nrunning it. Metadata does not supply missing values.\n\n## Dates, money and rounding\n\nReuse the [core date primitives](../../packages/core/src/primitives/date.ts)\nand the selected calculator's input Schema. Keep calculation dates, payment\ndates and tax years distinct where that calculator supports them. FBT and\nother proposed date dimensions do not establish an implemented calculator\ncontract; add them at their owning Schema when that work is accepted.\n\n[Money](../../packages/core/src/primitives/money.ts) uses integer cents. Its\nnumber representation is checked by the owning Schema; a bare number is not\ncanonical money. Keep final amounts in that representation rather than using\nfloating-point dollar arithmetic.\n\nReuse [RoundingMode](../../packages/core/src/primitives/rounding.ts) and the\nowning rounding operations. The closed modes are `none`,\n`round-to-nearest-cent`, `floor-cent`, `ceil-cent`, `floor-dollar`,\n`ceil-dollar` and `ato-withholding-rounding`, defined by `Schema.Literals`.\nRecord the chosen policy in calculation trace output.\n\nDo not invent defaults that materially change tax results, such as whether a\nperson has study debt, claims the tax-free threshold or has health insurance.\nA supported default must belong to the input Schema or an explicit rule.\n\n## Question metadata\n\n`FactQuestion` is the [core-owned Schema class](../../packages/core/src/facts/descriptor.ts).\nIt carries a branded `FactQuestionId`, `prompt`, optional `helpText` and an\n`inputKind` of `money`, `boolean` or `selection`. Reuse this class and the\nfact descriptor's question rather than introducing a competing question type.\n\nQuestion metadata describes supported input collection. It does not prove that\na UI or CLI can automatically collect every missing fact; that behaviour needs\nits own application implementation and tests.\n''')\nwrite('docs/architecture/rules-and-parameters.md', metadata('taxkit-rules-and-parameters-owner','rule Layer, descriptor, parameter or rule-pack composition change')+'''# Rules and parameters\n\nRules are Effect Layers that produce named facts from other facts and parameter\nservices. Descriptors explain that graph; the typed dependencies drive execution.\n\n## Rule pattern\n\nThe current [TaxablePayLive](../../packages/rules/au/pay/src/rules/taxable-pay.ts)\nuses `Layer.effect(TaxablePayFact)(...)` and reads `GrossPayFact` inside its\nEffect. It produces canonical `TaxablePay` with a `TraceNode`. In the retained\nimplementation taxable pay equals gross pay: salary sacrifice is not yet part\nof this rule. Do not describe a proposed input as an existing dependency.\n\nAfter the rule pack and scenario Layers are supplied, a calculator must have no\nremaining dependencies. A missing fact or parameter remains visible in Effect's\nrequired service type.\n\n## Rule descriptors\n\nReuse `RuleDescriptor` and `makeRuleDescriptor` from `@taxkit/core`.\nThe [descriptor owner](../../packages/core/src/rules/descriptor.ts) ties the\nLayer's output, errors and required services to readonly fact/parameter\ndescriptors. It owns branded rule IDs, titles, source references and the\n`required` or `not-required` source policy. Do not maintain a second descriptor\ninterface or add fields that the owning contract does not expose.\n\nDescriptors must match the actual Layer. The core graph validator and owning\nrule-pack tests check missing dependencies, competing providers and source\nrequirements; static descriptor metadata alone is not execution proof.\n\n## Parameter services\n\nA parameter table belongs to its own service, separate from the algorithm that\nuses it. The current [Schedule 1 owner](../../packages/rules/au/pay/src/parameters/schedule1.ts)\ndefines checked rows, a table Schema and the service:\n\n```ts\nexport class AtoSchedule1Table extends Context.Service<\n  AtoSchedule1Table,\n  Schedule1Table\n>()(\"taxkit/rules-au-pay/parameter/AtoSchedule1Table\") {}\n```\n\nThis is an excerpt from the owning module. Its `AtoSchedule1_2025_26_Live`\nLayer supplies the canonical table. PAYG algorithms require the service rather\nthan reading a year-specific table from a global variable.\n\nParameter descriptors include source references and the table's effective\ntax-year period. Graph validation reports overlapping periods for different\ndescriptors with the same parameter ID, preventing two competing tables from\nsilently supplying the same service and year.\n\n## Rule packs\n\nA rule pack composes existing Layers and keeps descriptors, sources and golden\nexamples with their owning modules. Reuse the actual public exports; a pack\ndoes not require a namespace containing duplicate metadata or a made-up graph\nbuilder.\n\nThe current [take-home-pay pack](../../packages/rules/au/pay/src/rule-pack/au-take-home-pay-2025-26.ts)\ncomposes:\n\n```ts\nexport const AuTakeHomePay2025_26_Live = NetPayLive.pipe(\n  Layer.provideMerge(PayWithholdingsLedgerLive),\n  Layer.provideMerge(PaygWithholdingLive),\n  Layer.provideMerge(TaxablePayLive),\n  Layer.provideMerge(AtoSchedule1_2025_26_Live)\n);\n```\n\nThis excerpt uses the owning module's imports. The caller supplies\n`GrossPayFact` and `TaxFreeThresholdClaimedFact` through its scenario Layer.\nThe base withholding ledger includes PAYG only; a pack adding STSL replaces\nthat ledger with the owner that requires both components. Compose typed Layers\nrather than using untyped plugin arrays.\n\n## Algorithm and data separation\n\nKeep a year's checked parameter data separate from the reusable algorithm.\nA yearly change can then update that data and its source references while\nfocused tests check the resulting calculation. Changes to formulas, thresholds,\nrounding or supported inputs still require rule review and golden-result proof.\n\nUse schema-checked data tables where they express the actual rule, including\nmarginal rates, coefficient formulas, caps and ledger components. Add a shared\nrule builder only when it owns repeated policy and makes the call graph simpler;\nthe [abstraction admission owner](../design-docs/abstraction-admission.md)\ndefines that review.\n''')\np=root/'docs/architecture/effect-services.md'\ns=p.read_text().replace('last_reviewed: 2026-10-04','last_reviewed: 2026-10-05').replace('`Context.Tag` services','`Context.Service` services').replace('`Schema.make` is valid construction','The owning Schema’s `make` is valid construction').replace('`Schema.TaggedErrorClass`','`Schema.TaggedError`')\ns=s.replace('repository tools; website applications remain outside this rollout.','repository tools and both website applications. The strict override covers all\\nowned TypeScript and JavaScript extensions. Five unexecuted upstream lint-input\\nfixtures have exact strict-only exclusions; their neighbouring files still\\nreceive the full policy. The [testing owner](testing-and-quality.md) records\\nthe coverage and actual-command rejection proof.')\ns=s.replace('''program.pipe(\n  Effect.mapError(\n    (cause) =>\n      new BoundaryError({\n        cause,\n        message: `Failed to load boundary config: ${cause.message}`,\n      })\n  )\n);''','''program.pipe(\n  Effect.mapError(\n    () => new BoundaryError({ message: \"Boundary settings are invalid\" })\n  )\n);''')\ns=s.replace('''Use `@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain(...)`''','''The web scaffold owns its server and browser health-client runtimes in the\n[web runtime module](../../apps/web/src/lib/runtime.ts). Its public facade\nexposes the named health operation and disposal, while route cancellation\nreaches the HTTP request through Effect interruption. Browser configuration\nreceives only the checked public input selected by the build configuration.\nThe SDK owns one runtime per client, with caller disposal and bounded one-shot\nhelpers; see the [SDK lifetime owner](api-and-sdk.md#typescript-sdk-facade).\n\nUse `@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain(...)`''')\ns=s.replace('- Use `Effect.Schema` for boundary and persisted values.','- Use `Schema` from `effect` for boundary and persisted values.')\np.write_text(s)\nfor rel in ['docs/architecture/README.md','docs/architecture/package-boundaries.md']:\n    p=root/rel;s=p.read_text().replace('Context.Tag','Context.Service')\n    if 'status: canonical' in s:\n        s=metadata('taxkit-package-boundaries-owner','package responsibility, dependency direction or public export change')+s.split('---\\n',2)[2].lstrip()\n    else:s=s.replace('last_reviewed: 2026-07-20','last_reviewed: 2026-10-05')\n    p.write_text(s)\nPY\npython3 /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/update-foundation-guides.py"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cat > /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/update-foundation-guides.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot=Path.cwd()\ndef write(path,text):\n    (root/path).write_text(text)\ndef metadata(owner,trigger):\n    return f'---\\ndocument_type: architecture\\nlifecycle: current\\nauthority: canonical\\nowner: {owner}\\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-05\\nreview_trigger: {trigger}\\n---\\n\\n'\nwrite('docs/architecture/facts.md', metadata('taxkit-facts-owner','fact Schema, identity, descriptor, authority or question metadata change')+'''# Facts\n\nA fact is a named value required or produced by a calculation. Its owning rule\npackage defines the value Schema, the Effect service identity and the descriptor\nused to check the calculation graph. Consumers reuse those definitions.\n\n## Fact pattern\n\nThe current [pay facts](../../packages/rules/au/pay/src/facts/pay.ts) define\n`GrossPay`, `PayPeriod`, `GrossPayFact` and `GrossPayDescriptor` together.\n`GrossPay` contains canonical `Money` and a checked pay period. The service\nuses the installed Effect 4 form:\n\n```ts\nexport class GrossPayFact extends Context.Service<GrossPayFact, GrossPay>()(\n  \"taxkit/rules-au-pay/fact/GrossPay\"\n) {}\n```\n\nThis is an excerpt from the owning module; its imports and value Schema belong\nthere. Keep the service identity stable. Another value with similar fields\ncannot supply a different fact service.\n\n## Descriptors and authority\n\nImport `FactDescriptor` and `makeFactDescriptor` from `@taxkit/core`; do not\ncopy their fields into a second interface. The [descriptor owner](../../packages/core/src/facts/descriptor.ts)\nkeeps the value Schema and `Context.Key<Self, Value>` tied to the same value\ntype. Its readonly fields include a branded fact ID, title, authority and\noptional `FactQuestion`. This generic relation supports graph tools while\nEffect's dependency type still decides what execution needs.\n\n`FactAuthority` admits three values:\n\n- `input`: the caller supplies a typed input accepted by the calculator.\n- `derived`: a rule produces the fact from other facts or parameters.\n- `parameter`: a service supplies a tax-year table, rate or constant.\n\nCallers must construct the selected calculator's canonical input facts before\nrunning it. Metadata does not supply missing values.\n\n## Dates, money and rounding\n\nReuse the [core date primitives](../../packages/core/src/primitives/date.ts)\nand the selected calculator's input Schema. Keep calculation dates, payment\ndates and tax years distinct where that calculator supports them. FBT and\nother proposed date dimensions do not establish an implemented calculator\ncontract; add them at their owning Schema when that work is accepted.\n\n[Money](../../packages/core/src/primitives/money.ts) uses integer cents. Its\nnumber representation is checked by the owning Schema; a bare number is not\ncanonical money. Keep final amounts in that representation rather than using\nfloating-point dollar arithmetic.\n\nReuse [RoundingMode](../../packages/core/src/primitives/rounding.ts) and the\nowning rounding operations. The closed modes are `none`,\n`round-to-nearest-cent`, `floor-cent`, `ceil-cent`, `floor-dollar`,\n`ceil-dollar` and `ato-withholding-rounding`, defined by `Schema.Literals`.\nRecord the chosen policy in calculation trace output.\n\nDo not invent defaults that materially change tax results, such as whether a\nperson has study debt, claims the tax-free threshold or has health insurance.\nA supported default must belong to the input Schema or an explicit rule.\n\n## Question metadata\n\n`FactQuestion` is the [core-owned Schema class](../../packages/core/src/facts/descriptor.ts).\nIt carries a branded `FactQuestionId`, `prompt`, optional `helpText` and an\n`inputKind` of `money`, `boolean` or `selection`. Reuse this class and the\nfact descriptor's question rather than introducing a competing question type.\n\nQuestion metadata describes supported input collection. It does not prove that\na UI or CLI can automatically collect every missing fact; that behaviour needs\nits own application implementation and tests.\n''')\nwrite('docs/architecture/rules-and-parameters.md', metadata('taxkit-rules-and-parameters-owner','rule Layer, descriptor, parameter or rule-pack composition change')+'''# Rules and parameters\n\nRules are Effect Layers that produce named facts from other facts and parameter\nservices. Descriptors explain that graph; the typed dependencies drive execution.\n\n## Rule pattern\n\nThe current [TaxablePayLive](../../packages/rules/au/pay/src/rules/taxable-pay.ts)\nuses `Layer.effect(TaxablePayFact)(...)` and reads `GrossPayFact` inside its\nEffect. It produces canonical `TaxablePay` with a `TraceNode`. In the retained\nimplementation taxable pay equals gross pay: salary sacrifice is not yet part\nof this rule. Do not describe a proposed input as an existing dependency.\n\nAfter the rule pack and scenario Layers are supplied, a calculator must have no\nremaining dependencies. A missing fact or parameter remains visible in Effect's\nrequired service type.\n\n## Rule descriptors\n\nReuse `RuleDescriptor` and `makeRuleDescriptor` from `@taxkit/core`.\nThe [descriptor owner](../../packages/core/src/rules/descriptor.ts) ties the\nLayer's output, errors and required services to readonly fact/parameter\ndescriptors. It owns branded rule IDs, titles, source references and the\n`required` or `not-required` source policy. Do not maintain a second descriptor\ninterface or add fields that the owning contract does not expose.\n\nDescriptors must match the actual Layer. The core graph validator and owning\nrule-pack tests check missing dependencies, competing providers and source\nrequirements; static descriptor metadata alone is not execution proof.\n\n## Parameter services\n\nA parameter table belongs to its own service, separate from the algorithm that\nuses it. The current [Schedule 1 owner](../../packages/rules/au/pay/src/parameters/schedule1.ts)\ndefines checked rows, a table Schema and the service:\n\n```ts\nexport class AtoSchedule1Table extends Context.Service<\n  AtoSchedule1Table,\n  Schedule1Table\n>()(\"taxkit/rules-au-pay/parameter/AtoSchedule1Table\") {}\n```\n\nThis is an excerpt from the owning module. Its `AtoSchedule1_2025_26_Live`\nLayer supplies the canonical table. PAYG algorithms require the service rather\nthan reading a year-specific table from a global variable.\n\nParameter descriptors include source references and the table's effective\ntax-year period. Graph validation reports overlapping periods for different\ndescriptors with the same parameter ID, preventing two competing tables from\nsilently supplying the same service and year.\n\n## Rule packs\n\nA rule pack composes existing Layers and keeps descriptors, sources and golden\nexamples with their owning modules. Reuse the actual public exports; a pack\ndoes not require a namespace containing duplicate metadata or a made-up graph\nbuilder.\n\nThe current [take-home-pay pack](../../packages/rules/au/pay/src/rule-pack/au-take-home-pay-2025-26.ts)\ncomposes:\n\n```ts\nexport const AuTakeHomePay2025_26_Live = NetPayLive.pipe(\n  Layer.provideMerge(PayWithholdingsLedgerLive),\n  Layer.provideMerge(PaygWithholdingLive),\n  Layer.provideMerge(TaxablePayLive),\n  Layer.provideMerge(AtoSchedule1_2025_26_Live)\n);\n```\n\nThis excerpt uses the owning module's imports. The caller supplies\n`GrossPayFact` and `TaxFreeThresholdClaimedFact` through its scenario Layer.\nThe base withholding ledger includes PAYG only; a pack adding STSL replaces\nthat ledger with the owner that requires both components. Compose typed Layers\nrather than using untyped plugin arrays.\n\n## Algorithm and data separation\n\nKeep a year's checked parameter data separate from the reusable algorithm.\nA yearly change can then update that data and its source references while\nfocused tests check the resulting calculation. Changes to formulas, thresholds,\nrounding or supported inputs still require rule review and golden-result proof.\n\nUse schema-checked data tables where they express the actual rule, including\nmarginal rates, coefficient formulas, caps and ledger components. Add a shared\nrule builder only when it owns repeated policy and makes the call graph simpler;\nthe [abstraction admission owner](../design-docs/abstraction-admission.md)\ndefines that review.\n''')\np=root/'docs/architecture/effect-services.md'\ns=p.read_text().replace('last_reviewed: 2026-10-04','last_reviewed: 2026-10-05').replace('`Context.Tag` services','`Context.Service` services').replace('`Schema.make` is valid construction','The owning Schema’s `make` is