{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:40:48.775Z","ordinal":13675,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_06b7a884f26959d3016ac2737fc6a087d0a68b597f109480f9","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The guides also described features the retained rules do not yet support, such as salary sacrifice in taxable pay. I’m replacing those examples with links to the real rules and keeping proposed features clearly labelled.\n"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1791128447781,"completed_at_ms":1791128448775}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:40:48.778Z","ordinal":13676,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_06b7a884f26959d3016ac2737fc6a087d0a68b597f109480f9","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The guides also described features the retained rules do not yet support, such as salary sacrifice in taxable pay. I’m replacing those examples with links to the real rules and keeping proposed features clearly labelled.\n"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_06b7a884f26959d3016ac2737fc6a087d0a68b597f109480f9","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a10793-2f0a-7e03-ba75-ea36cddd5ddb","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":244}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:41:11.612Z","ordinal":13677,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_06b7a884f26959d3016ac27380c41087d0b53191ef419b21e1","status":"completed","call_id":"call_UDsmW41GQO9oQueah0QCOlnw","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat apps/web/src/lib/runtime.server.ts apps/web/src/lib/runtime.client.ts apps/web/src/lib/runtime-selection.ts; cat > /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/update-config-guide.py <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\np=Path('docs/architecture/configuration.md')\\ns=p.read_text();s='''---\\ndocument_type: architecture\\nlifecycle: current\\nauthority: canonical\\nowner: taxkit-configuration-owner\\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-05\\nreview_trigger: config Schema, namespace, source selection or secret custody change\\n---\\n\\n'''+s.split('---\\\\n',2)[2].lstrip()\\ns=s.replace('The current environment map is:', 'The repository-defined environment map is:')\\ns=s.replace('''The TaxKit Doppler project/configs and three GitHub bridges are established.\\nDirect Turbo and Cloudflare GitHub entries have been removed after merged-main\\nreplacement proof. No implemented workflow or supported recovery path falls\\nback to a direct value.''','''The earlier Doppler implementation recorded establishment of the project,\\nconfigs and GitHub bridges, and removal of direct Turbo/Cloudflare entries after\\nreplacement proof. That is historical provider evidence, not a fresh readback\\nfrom this checkout. Current source has no supported direct-value fallback;\\nprovider custody and availability require the separate operational readback\\nowned by the [authority model](../operations/authority-model.md).''')\\na=s.index('## Pattern\\\\n');b=s.index('## Guardrails\\\\n')\\ns=s[:a]+'''## Current package and app pattern\\n\\nThe [HTTP package config owner](../../packages/api/http/src/config.ts) exports\\n`TaxKitHttpApiClientConfigSchema`, its derived type and the keyed server/browser\\nconfig fragments. Its Schema uses `Schema.URLFromString`, so the encoded base\\nURL is a string and the canonical value is a `URL`. The fragment reads the\\nnamed URL through native `Config.URL` and constructs the owning Schema value.\\nIts `Config.nested` namespaces are `TAXKIT_API` and `VITE_TAXKIT_API`.\\n\\nThe [server app config](../../apps/web/src/lib/config.server.ts) composes the\\npackage fragment rather than defining the HTTP setting again:\\n\\n```ts\\nexport const TaxKitWebServerConfig = Config.all({\\n  ...TaxKitHttpApiServerEnvConfig,\\n});\\n```\\n\\nThis excerpt describes package composition; the owning module also maps config\\nfailure inline to the safe app error. Its native `ConfigProvider.fromEnv()` and\\n`ConfigProvider.constantCase` read `TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` at server runtime.\\n`Config.nested`, `Config.Wrap` and `Config.URL` are supported by the installed\\nEffect 4 version. Use `typeof ConfigSchema.Type` for new schema-derived type\\nexamples; the package's existing `Schema.Schema.Type` form remains supported.\\n\\n## Browser configuration boundary\\n\\nThe [client config module](../../apps/web/src/lib/config.client.ts) composes\\n`TaxKitHttpApiViteEnvConfig`. Its provider receives only the build-selected\\npublic input:\\n\\n```ts\\nexport const TaxKitWebClientConfigProviderLive = ConfigProvider.layer(\\n  ConfigProvider.fromEnv({ env: __TAXKIT_WEB_CLIENT_INPUT__ }).pipe(\\n    ConfigProvider.constantCase\\n  )\\n);\\n```\\n\\nThe [input owner](../../apps/web/src/lib/config.client-input.ts) defines and\\nconstructs the checked input containing only optional `VITE_TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL`.\\nThe [Vite config](../../apps/web/vite.config.ts) loads that input with native\\n`Config.schema` and replaces the typed constant during the build. It sets\\n`envPrefix: []` so Vite cannot automatically copy other prefixed environment\\nvalues into browser code. The URL is then read through the package-owned config\\nfragment. Do not pass the whole `import.meta.env` or process environment to the\\nbrowser provider.\\n\\nThe browser config test and built-bundle sentinel check prove that unrelated\\ncredential markers do not reach the qualified browser bundle. This is local\\nbuild proof, separate from any hosted environment or provider configuration.\\n\\n## Schema-owned settings\\n\\nUse `Config.schema` with the owning Schema when loading semantic settings,\\nincluding provider identities, credentials, stages and checked command inputs.\\n[API app config](../../apps/api/src/config.ts) is another current example: the\\nhost and port are checked by their owners; optional `API_PORT` falls back to\\n`PORT` only when absent. An invalid supplied primary value remains an error.\\n\\nConfiguration modules own defaults and selection. Service contracts receive\\ncanonical checked values. Raw credentials use `Schema.RedactedFromValue` at\\nstring ingress; unwrap only at final construction of the private provider\\nclient, never merely for a brand or diagnostic.\\n\\n'''+s[b:]\\ns=s.replace('''- Use Effect `Config`, `ConfigProvider`, `Schema`, `Layer` and platform\\n  runtime primitives for configuration. Do not parse `process.env` or\\n  `import.meta.env` by hand when an Effect config/schema composition can own\\n  the shape.''','''- Use Effect `Config`, `ConfigProvider`, `Schema`, `Layer` and platform\\n  runtime primitives for configuration. Keep representation ingress at its\\n  exact config owner, and select only explicitly public keys for browser builds.''')\\np.write_text(s)\\np=Path('docs/architecture/effect-services.md');s=p.read_text().replace('[web runtime module](../../apps/web/src/lib/runtime.ts)','[web runtime selection](../../apps/web/src/lib/runtime-selection.ts)');p.write_text(s)\\nPY\\npython3 /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/update-config-guide.py\",max_output_tokens:3000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","create_time":1791128446.19684}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:41:11.659Z","ordinal":13678,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","session_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","root_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","response_id":"resp_06b7a884f26959d3016ac2737e09fc87d0b811a5b068291f56","usage":{"input_tokens":88487,"cached_input_tokens":86784,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1314,"reasoning_output_tokens":14,"total_tokens":89801},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":262391778,"cached_input_tokens":257260160,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1364394,"reasoning_output_tokens":547073,"total_tokens":263756172},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":262391778,"cached_input_tokens":257260160,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1364394,"reasoning_output_tokens":547073,"total_tokens":263756172}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:41:11.732Z","ordinal":13679,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b8abf814-f9a3-4d93-b3d1-a76dad0d4bc2","process_id":"23458","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat apps/web/src/lib/runtime.server.ts apps/web/src/lib/runtime.client.ts apps/web/src/lib/runtime-selection.ts; cat > /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/update-config-guide.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('docs/architecture/configuration.md')\ns=p.read_text();s='''---\ndocument_type: architecture\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: taxkit-configuration-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-05\nreview_trigger: config Schema, namespace, source selection or secret custody change\n---\n\n'''+s.split('---\\n',2)[2].lstrip()\ns=s.replace('The current environment map is:', 'The repository-defined environment map is:')\ns=s.replace('''The TaxKit Doppler project/configs and three GitHub bridges are established.\nDirect Turbo and Cloudflare GitHub entries have been removed after merged-main\nreplacement proof. No implemented workflow or supported recovery path falls\nback to a direct value.''','''The earlier Doppler implementation recorded establishment of the project,\nconfigs and GitHub bridges, and removal of direct Turbo/Cloudflare entries after\nreplacement proof. That is historical provider evidence, not a fresh readback\nfrom this checkout. Current source has no supported direct-value fallback;\nprovider custody and availability require the separate operational readback\nowned by the [authority model](../operations/authority-model.md).''')\na=s.index('## Pattern\\n');b=s.index('## Guardrails\\n')\ns=s[:a]+'''## Current package and app pattern\n\nThe [HTTP package config owner](../../packages/api/http/src/config.ts) exports\n`TaxKitHttpApiClientConfigSchema`, its derived type and the keyed server/browser\nconfig fragments. Its Schema uses `Schema.URLFromString`, so the encoded base\nURL is a string and the canonical value is a `URL`. The fragment reads the\nnamed URL through native `Config.URL` and constructs the owning Schema value.\nIts `Config.nested` namespaces are `TAXKIT_API` and `VITE_TAXKIT_API`.\n\nThe [server app config](../../apps/web/src/lib/config.server.ts) composes the\npackage fragment rather than defining the HTTP setting again:\n\n```ts\nexport const TaxKitWebServerConfig = Config.all({\n  ...TaxKitHttpApiServerEnvConfig,\n});\n```\n\nThis excerpt describes package composition; the owning module also maps config\nfailure inline to the safe app error. Its native `ConfigProvider.fromEnv()` and\n`ConfigProvider.constantCase` read `TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` at server runtime.\n`Config.nested`, `Config.Wrap` and `Config.URL` are supported by the installed\nEffect 4 version. Use `typeof ConfigSchema.Type` for new schema-derived type\nexamples; the package's existing `Schema.Schema.Type` form remains supported.\n\n## Browser configuration boundary\n\nThe [client config module](../../apps/web/src/lib/config.client.ts) composes\n`TaxKitHttpApiViteEnvConfig`. Its provider receives only the build-selected\npublic input:\n\n```ts\nexport const TaxKitWebClientConfigProviderLive = ConfigProvider.layer(\n  ConfigProvider.fromEnv({ env: __TAXKIT_WEB_CLIENT_INPUT__ }).pipe(\n    ConfigProvider.constantCase\n  )\n);\n```\n\nThe [input owner](../../apps/web/src/lib/config.client-input.ts) defines and\nconstructs the checked input containing only optional `VITE_TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL`.\nThe [Vite config](../../apps/web/vite.config.ts) loads that input with native\n`Config.schema` and replaces the typed constant during the build. It sets\n`envPrefix: []` so Vite cannot automatically copy other prefixed environment\nvalues into browser code. The URL is then read through the package-owned config\nfragment. Do not pass the whole `import.meta.env` or process environment to the\nbrowser provider.\n\nThe browser config test and built-bundle sentinel check prove that unrelated\ncredential markers do not reach the qualified browser bundle. This is local\nbuild proof, separate from any hosted environment or provider configuration.\n\n## Schema-owned settings\n\nUse `Config.schema` with the owning Schema when loading semantic settings,\nincluding provider identities, credentials, stages and checked command inputs.\n[API app config](../../apps/api/src/config.ts) is another current example: the\nhost and port are checked by their owners; optional `API_PORT` falls back to\n`PORT` only when absent. An invalid supplied primary value remains an error.\n\nConfiguration modules own defaults and selection. Service contracts receive\ncanonical checked values. Raw credentials use `Schema.RedactedFromValue` at\nstring ingress; unwrap only at final construction of the private provider\nclient, never merely for a brand or diagnostic.\n\n'''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('''- Use Effect `Config`, `ConfigProvider`, `Schema`, `Layer` and platform\n  runtime primitives for configuration. Do not parse `process.env` or\n  `import.meta.env` by hand when an Effect config/schema composition can own\n  the shape.''','''- Use Effect `Config`, `ConfigProvider`, `Schema`, `Layer` and platform\n  runtime primitives for configuration. Keep representation ingress at its\n  exact config owner, and select only explicitly public keys for browser builds.''')\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/architecture/effect-services.md');s=p.read_text().replace('[web runtime module](../../apps/web/src/lib/runtime.ts)','[web runtime selection](../../apps/web/src/lib/runtime-selection.ts)');p.write_text(s)\nPY\npython3 /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/update-config-guide.py"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cat apps/web/src/lib/runtime.server.ts apps/web/src/lib/runtime.client.ts apps/web/src/lib/runtime-selection.ts; cat > /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/update-config-guide.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('docs/architecture/configuration.md')\ns=p.read_text();s='''---\ndocument_type: architecture\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: taxkit-configuration-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-05\nreview_trigger: config Schema, namespace, source selection or secret custody change\n---\n\n'''+s.split('---\\n',2)[2].lstrip()\ns=s.replace('The current environment map is:', 'The repository-defined environment map is:')\ns=s.replace('''The TaxKit Doppler project/configs and three GitHub bridges are established.\nDirect Turbo and Cloudflare GitHub entries have been removed after merged-main\nreplacement proof. No implemented workflow or supported recovery path falls\nback to a direct value.''','''The earlier Doppler implementation recorded establishment of the project,\nconfigs and GitHub bridges, and removal of direct Turbo/Cloudflare entries after\nreplacement proof. That is historical provider evidence, not a fresh readback\nfrom this checkout. Current source has no supported direct-value fallback;\nprovider custody and availability require the separate operational readback\nowned by the [authority model](../operations/authority-model.md).''')\na=s.index('## Pattern\\n');b=s.index('## Guardrails\\n')\ns=s[:a]+'''## Current package and app pattern\n\nThe [HTTP package config owner](../../packages/api/http/src/config.ts) exports\n`TaxKitHttpApiClientConfigSchema`, its derived type and the keyed server/browser\nconfig fragments. Its Schema uses `Schema.URLFromString`, so the encoded base\nURL is a string and the canonical value is a `URL`. The fragment reads the\nnamed URL through native `Config.URL` and constructs the owning Schema value.\nIts `Config.nested` namespaces are `TAXKIT_API` and `VITE_TAXKIT_API`.\n\nThe [server app config](../../apps/web/src/lib/config.server.ts) composes the\npackage fragment rather than defining the HTTP setting again:\n\n```ts\nexport const TaxKitWebServerConfig = Config.all({\n  ...TaxKitHttpApiServerEnvConfig,\n});\n```\n\nThis excerpt describes package composition; the owning module also maps config\nfailure inline to the safe app error. Its native `ConfigProvider.fromEnv()` and\n`ConfigProvider.constantCase` read `TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` at server runtime.\n`Config.nested`, `Config.Wrap` and `Config.URL` are supported by the installed\nEffect 4 version. Use `typeof ConfigSchema.Type` for new schema-derived type\nexamples; the package's existing `Schema.Schema.Type` form remains supported.\n\n## Browser configuration boundary\n\nThe [client config module](../../apps/web/src/lib/config.client.ts) composes\n`TaxKitHttpApiViteEnvConfig`. Its provider receives only the build-selected\npublic input:\n\n```ts\nexport const TaxKitWebClientConfigProviderLive = ConfigProvider.layer(\n  ConfigProvider.fromEnv({ env: __TAXKIT_WEB_CLIENT_INPUT__ }).pipe(\n    ConfigProvider.constantCase\n  )\n);\n```\n\nThe [input owner](../../apps/web/src/lib/config.client-input.ts) defines and\nconstructs the checked input containing only optional `VITE_TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL`.\nThe [Vite config](../../apps/web/vite.config.ts) loads that input with native\n`Config.schema` and replaces the typed constant during the build. It sets\n`envPrefix: []` so Vite cannot automatically copy other prefixed environment\nvalues into browser code. The URL is then read through the package-owned config\nfragment. Do not pass the whole `import.meta.env` or process environment to the\nbrowser provider.\n\nThe browser config test and built-bundle sentinel check prove that unrelated\ncredential markers do not reach the qualified browser bundle. This is local\nbuild proof, separate from any hosted environment or provider configuration.\n\n## Schema-owned settings\n\nUse `Config.schema` with the owning Schema when loading semantic settings,\nincluding provider identities, credentials, stages and checked command inputs.\n[API app config](../../apps/api/src/config.ts) is another current example: the\nhost and port are checked by their owners; optional `API_PORT` falls back to\n`PORT` only when absent. An invalid supplied primary value remains an error.\n\nConfiguration modules own defaults and selection. Service contracts receive\ncanonical checked values. Raw credentials use `Schema.RedactedFromValue` at\nstring ingress; unwrap only at final construction of the private provider\nclient, never merely for a brand or diagnostic.\n\n'''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('''- Use Effect `Config`, `ConfigProvider`, `Schema`, `Layer` and platform\n  runtime primitives for configuration. Do not parse `process.env` or\n  `import.meta.env` by hand when an Effect config/schema composition can own\n  the shape.''','''- Use Effect `Config`, `ConfigProvider`, `Schema`, `Layer` and platform\n  runtime primitives for configuration. Keep representation ingress at its\n  exact config owner, and select only explicitly public keys for browser builds.''')\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/architecture/effect-services.md');s=p.read_text().replace('[web runtime module](../../apps/web/src/lib/runtime.ts)','[web runtime selection](../../apps/web/src/lib/runtime-selection.ts)');p.write_text(s)\nPY\npython3 /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/update-config-guide.py"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"import \"@tanstack/react-start/server-only\";\nimport { createTaxKitApiClientLayer } from \"@taxkit/api-http/client/live\";\nimport { Effect, Layer, ManagedRuntime } from \"effect\";\nimport * as FetchHttpClient from \"effect/http/FetchHttpClient\";\n\nimport {\n  TaxKitWebServerConfig,\n  TaxKitWebServerConfigProviderLive,\n} from \"./config.server\";\n\nconst TaxKitApiClientLive = Layer.unwrap(\n  Effect.gen(function* makeTaxKitApiClientLive() {\n    const config = yield* TaxKitWebServerConfig;\n    return createTaxKitApiClientLayer({ baseUrl: config.httpApi.baseUrl });\n  })\n).pipe(\n  Layer.provide(FetchHttpClient.layer),\n  Layer.provide(TaxKitWebServerConfigProviderLive)\n);\n\nexport const appRuntime = ManagedRuntime.make(TaxKitApiClientLive);\nimport { createTaxKitApiClientLayer } from \"@taxkit/api-http/client/live\";\nimport { Effect, Layer, ManagedRuntime } from \"effect\";\nimport * as FetchHttpClient from \"effect/http/FetchHttpClient\";\n\nimport {\n  TaxKitWebClientConfig,\n  TaxKitWebClientConfigProviderLive,\n} from \"./config.client\";\n\nconst TaxKitApiClientLive = Layer.unwrap(\n  Effect.gen(function* makeTaxKitApiClientLive() {\n    const config = yield* TaxKitWebClientConfig;\n    return createTaxKitApiClientLayer({ baseUrl: config.httpApi.baseUrl });\n  })\n).pipe(\n  Layer.provide(FetchHttpClient.layer),\n  Layer.provide(TaxKitWebClientConfigProviderLive)\n);\n\nexport const appRuntime = ManagedRuntime.make(TaxKitApiClientLive);\nimport { createIsomorphicFn } from \"@tanstack/react-start\";\n\nimport { appRuntime as appRuntimeClient } from \"./runtime.client\";\nimport { appRuntime as appRuntimeServer } from \"./runtime.server\";\n\nexport const getAppRuntime = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server(() => appRuntimeServer)\n  .client(() => appRuntimeClient);\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"import \"@tanstack/react-start/server-only\";\nimport { createTaxKitApiClientLayer } from \"@taxkit/api-http/client/live\";\nimport { Effect, Layer, ManagedRuntime } from \"effect\";\nimport * as FetchHttpClient from \"effect/http/FetchHttpClient\";\n\nimport {\n  TaxKitWebServerConfig,\n  TaxKitWebServerConfigProviderLive,\n} from \"./config.server\";\n\nconst TaxKitApiClientLive = Layer.unwrap(\n  Effect.gen(function* makeTaxKitApiClientLive() {\n    const config = yield* TaxKitWebServerConfig;\n    return createTaxKitApiClientLayer({ baseUrl: config.httpApi.baseUrl });\n  })\n).pipe(\n  Layer.provide(FetchHttpClient.layer),\n  Layer.provide(TaxKitWebServerConfigProviderLive)\n);\n\nexport const appRuntime = ManagedRuntime.make(TaxKitApiClientLive);\nimport { createTaxKitApiClientLayer } from \"@taxkit/api-http/client/live\";\nimport { Effect, Layer, ManagedRuntime } from \"effect\";\nimport * as FetchHttpClient from \"effect/http/FetchHttpClient\";\n\nimport {\n  TaxKitWebClientConfig,\n  TaxKitWebClientConfigProviderLive,\n} from \"./config.client\";\n\nconst TaxKitApiClientLive = Layer.unwrap(\n  Effect.gen(function* makeTaxKitApiClientLive() {\n    const config = yield* TaxKitWebClientConfig;\n    return createTaxKitApiClientLayer({ baseUrl: config.httpApi.baseUrl });\n  })\n).pipe(\n  Layer.provide(FetchHttpClient.layer),\n  Layer.provide(TaxKitWebClientConfigProviderLive)\n);\n\nexport const appRuntime = ManagedRuntime.make(TaxKitApiClientLive);\nimport { createIsomorphicFn } from \"@tanstack/react-start\";\n\nimport { appRuntime as appRuntimeClient } from \"./runtime.client\";\nimport { appRuntime as appRuntimeServer } from \"./runtime.server\";\n\nexport const getAppRuntime = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server(() => appRuntimeServer)\n  .client(() => appRuntimeClient);\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":6000},"formatted_output":"import \"@tanstack/react-start/server-only\";\nimport { createTaxKitApiClientLayer } from \"@taxkit/api-http/client/live\";\nimport { Effect, Layer, ManagedRuntime } from \"effect\";\nimport * as FetchHttpClient from \"effect/http/FetchHttpClient\";\n\nimport {\n  TaxKitWebServerConfig,\n  TaxKitWebServerConfigProviderLive,\n} from \"./config.server\";\n\nconst TaxKitApiClientLive = Layer.unwrap(\n  Effect.gen(function* makeTaxKitApiClientLive() {\n    const config = yield* TaxKitWebServerConfig;\n    return createTaxKitApiClientLayer({ baseUrl: config.httpApi.baseUrl });\n  })\n).pipe(\n  Layer.provide(FetchHttpClient.layer),\n  Layer.provide(TaxKitWebServerConfigProviderLive)\n);\n\nexport const appRuntime = ManagedRuntime.make(TaxKitApiClientLive);\nimport { createTaxKitApiClientLayer } from \"@taxkit/api-http/client/live\";\nimport { Effect, Layer, ManagedRuntime } from \"effect\";\nimport * as FetchHttpClient from \"effect/http/FetchHttpClient\";\n\nimport {\n  TaxKitWebClientConfig,\n  TaxKitWebClientConfigProviderLive,\n} from \"./config.client\";\n\nconst TaxKitApiClientLive = Layer.unwrap(\n  Effect.gen(function* makeTaxKitApiClientLive() {\n    const config = yield* TaxKitWebClientConfig;\n    return createTaxKitApiClientLayer({ baseUrl: config.httpApi.baseUrl });\n  })\n).pipe(\n  Layer.provide(FetchHttpClient.layer),\n  Layer.provide(TaxKitWebClientConfigProviderLive)\n);\n\nexport const appRuntime = ManagedRuntime.make(TaxKitApiClientLive);\nimport { createIsomorphicFn } from \"@tanstack/react-start\";\n\nimport { appRuntime as appRuntimeClient } from \"./runtime.client\";\nimport { appRuntime as appRuntimeServer } from \"./runtime.server\";\n\nexport const getAppRuntime = createIsomorphicFn()\n  .server(() => appRuntimeServer)\n  .client(() => appRuntimeClient);\n"},"started_at_ms":1791128471732,"completed_at_ms":1791128471732}}
