{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:41:17.784Z","ordinal":13686,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-742ce9fa-6b2c-424b-ad8d-24d0e737b81b","process_id":"65729","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat apps/web/src/lib/route-context.ts apps/web/src/lib/config.server.ts apps/web/src/lib/config.client.ts; sed -n '1,110p' docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-owned-source-coverage.json; rg -n 'qualification|review|exception|T002|host' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md | head -65; git diff --stat"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cat apps/web/src/lib/route-context.ts apps/web/src/lib/config.server.ts apps/web/src/lib/config.client.ts; sed -n '1,110p' docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-owned-source-coverage.json; rg -n 'qualification|review|exception|T002|host' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md | head -65; git diff --stat"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"import type { TaxKitHttpApiService } from \"@taxkit/api-http/client\";\nimport type { ManagedRuntime } from \"effect\";\n\nimport type { TaxKitWebConfigError } from \"./config\";\n\nexport interface RouterContext {\n  readonly api: Pick<\n    ManagedRuntime.ManagedRuntime<TaxKitHttpApiService, TaxKitWebConfigError>,\n    \"runPromise\" | \"runPromiseExit\"\n  >;\n}\nimport \"@tanstack/react-start/server-only\";\nimport { TaxKitHttpApiServerEnvConfig } from \"@taxkit/api-http/config\";\nimport { Config, ConfigProvider, Effect } from \"effect\";\n\nimport { TaxKitWebConfigError } from \"./config\";\n\nexport const TaxKitWebServerConfig = Config.all({\n  ...TaxKitHttpApiServerEnvConfig,\n}).pipe(\n  Effect.mapError(\n    () =>\n      new TaxKitWebConfigError({\n        message: \"TaxKit web settings are missing or invalid.\",\n        operation: \"settings\",\n        runtime: \"server\",\n      })\n  )\n);\n\nexport const TaxKitWebServerConfigProviderLive = ConfigProvider.layer(\n  ConfigProvider.fromEnv().pipe(ConfigProvider.constantCase)\n);\nimport { TaxKitHttpApiViteEnvConfig } from \"@taxkit/api-http/config\";\nimport { Config, ConfigProvider, Effect } from \"effect\";\n\nimport { TaxKitWebConfigError } from \"./config\";\n\nexport const TaxKitWebClientConfig = Config.all({\n  ...TaxKitHttpApiViteEnvConfig,\n}).pipe(\n  Effect.mapError(\n    () =>\n      new TaxKitWebConfigError({\n        message: \"TaxKit web settings are missing or invalid.\",\n        operation: \"settings\",\n        runtime: \"client\",\n      })\n  )\n);\n\nexport const TaxKitWebClientConfigProviderLive = ConfigProvider.layer(\n  ConfigProvider.fromEnv({ env: __TAXKIT_WEB_CLIENT_INPUT__ }).pipe(\n    ConfigProvider.constantCase\n  )\n);\n{\n  \"document_type\": \"migration-receipt\",\n  \"date\": \"2026-10-05\",\n  \"issue\": \"DEV-73\",\n  \"parent_revision\": \"cd5b2a8dec1fdd53375486852485a898215d9ede\",\n  \"status\": \"locally-qualified\",\n  \"authority\": {\n    \"principal\": \"Cooper Corbett\",\n    \"operation\": \"local implementation, tested commits, pushes and draft PRs\",\n    \"repository\": \"crcorbett/taxkit\",\n    \"environment\": \"local pinned macOS/Bun/Chromium; no provider operation\"\n  },\n  \"implemented\": [\n    \"Canonical whole-source selector covers six extensions across current/future owned root/app/tool/config files\",\n    \"Five exact unexecuted lint-only inputs preserve isolated host/binding-rule contexts; neighbouring files remain strict\",\n    \"Actual six-extension and five-neighbour admission/rejection controls with exact file count and expected rules\",\n    \"Valid CommonJS positive/negative fixtures, separately from ESM syntax\",\n    \"Two new isolated real-verifier mutations reject removed whole-source coverage and broadened fixture exclusions; existing controls/deadlines preserved\"\n  ],\n  \"checks\": [\n    {\n      \"command\": \"native lint/Quality compiler projects\",\n      \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n      \"logs\": [\n        \"owned-source-qualified-lint-types.log\",\n        \"owned-source-qualified-quality-types.log\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"bun run lint / explicit Git-owned canonical CLI inventory\",\n      \"outcome\": \"pass: 397 admitted owned source paths, zero warnings/errors or inventory diagnostics; all staged additions included\",\n      \"logs\": [\n        \"owned-source-root-lint.log\",\n        \"2026-10-05-canonical-owned-source-inventory.json\",\n        \"2026-10-05-canonical-owned-source-inventory.stderr\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"bun run test:oxlint / bun run test\",\n      \"outcome\": \"401 actual CLI lint cases pass; all 24 package tasks, 23 matching caches; unchanged docs script/server cases 53/19 rerun\",\n      \"logs\": [\n        \"owned-source-cli-tests-qualified.log\",\n        \"owned-source-root-tests.log\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"bun run build\",\n      \"outcome\": \"all 15 tasks pass, matching caches; no app/package implementation change\",\n      \"logs\": [\n        \"owned-source-root-build.log\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"bun run verification\",\n      \"outcome\": \"32 Quality cases pass, including 13 isolated checks in 360.78 seconds; new source/exclusion regressions fail the real verifier with exact intended messages; 206 deployment-tool, 21 skill and 16 evaluation cases; both Knip profiles and all 24 compiler tasks pass; unchanged SDK/browser 24 and web/browser four matching caches\",\n      \"logs\": [\n        \"owned-source-full-verification.log\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"command\": \"bun install --frozen-lockfile\",\n      \"outcome\": \"pass: unchanged 792 installs/1020 packages; native compiler replacement hash matches\",\n      \"logs\": [\n        \"owned-source-frozen-install.log\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"documentation_impact\": {\n    \"Change required\": [\n      \"oxlint.config.ts\",\n      \"tools/oxlint/portable-rules.test.ts\",\n      \"tools/quality-workflow/schemas.ts\",\n      \"tools/quality-workflow/release-boundary.test.ts\",\n      \"tools/quality-workflow/fixtures/strict-enforcement-defects.json\",\n      \"docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md\",\n      \"docs/standards/controls.md\",\n      \"docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md\",\n      \"docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json\"\n    ],\n    \"Preserve\": [\n      \"All canonical rule severities and narrow runtime/codec/assignment/method admissions\",\n      \"Explicit generated/vendor exclusions and MDX expression owner\",\n      \"Canonical skills/digests, installed dependencies, public content, historical evidence, provider state and retained tax results\"\n    ],\n    \"N/A\": {\n      \"Changeset\": \"repository tooling only; no package contract change\",\n      \"runbook/provider operation\": \"same local verification commands; no consequential operation\",\n      \"new public/generated output\": \"unchanged\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"fixture_containment\": {\n    \"paths\": [\n      \"tools/oxlint/fixtures/bun-accepted.ts\",\n      \"tools/oxlint/fixtures/bun-global-non-host-accepted.ts\",\n      \"tools/oxlint/fixtures/bun-unrelated-accepted.ts\",\n      \"tools/oxlint/fixtures/effect-accepted.ts\",\n      \"tools/oxlint/fixtures/effect-unrelated-accepted.ts\"\n    ],\n    \"purpose\": \"unexecuted source inputs read by the actual lint corpus to isolate separate binding/host rules\",\n    \"owner\": \"tools/oxlint/portable-rules.test.ts\",\n    \"compiler_boundary\": \"tools/oxlint/tsconfig.json includes only ./*.ts, outside fixtures directory\",\n    \"removal\": \"retire exact exclusions when their isolated rule fixtures are retired; no workflow host admission\"\n  },\n  \"recovery\": {\n    \"failed_observations\": [\n      \"Initial new test object was unsorted, corrected\",\n      \"Initial CommonJS corpus used ESM imports and failed the strict diagnostic Schema before rule assertions; replaced with valid CommonJS fixtures\",\n      \"Initial corpus extension edit duplicated two expected IDs; corrected before isolated verification\"\n    ],\n    \"rollback\": \"revert this complete slice to parent revision\",\n6:last_reviewed: 2026-10-04\n7:review_trigger: rebuild scope, interview answer, version selection, or implementation admission\n17:This authority includes reviewable commits and draft PRs, but no merge, deploy,\n89:successful hosted calculation -> API application event owner -> PostHog capture\n98:Generated clients remain private. Preview uses its own backend. Runtime secrets\n113:controlled Preview journeys -> exact Website/API artifacts -> independent readback\n158:request cleanup and are released at their actual host/browser lifetime. Native\n167:envelopes, unknown procedure tags and request IDs also need qualification;\n174:checked ingress treatment or an exact reviewed native correction for uncovered\n198:| Documentation launch | Agreed in Q6: review and publish finished pages | Update and review pages; publish accepted pages and keep unfinished drafts out of public search | Publication records, search, sitemap, Markdown and agent indexes |\n201:| Functional Effect policy | Required by Cooper's follow-up | Immutable values, declarative workflows, services/Layers and piping across all owned code; current portable rules plus proved corrections for remaining gaps | Mutation/loop restrictions, state ownership and precise host exceptions |\n221:carry the rebuild through integration, local checks, reviewed provider plans,\n251:| CSF-002 | Qualify current dependencies and strict repository structure | Root manifest, lock, runtime, exports, TypeScript, formatting, lint, tests, Turbo, Knip and CI select one exact qualified graph. Update canonical repository skill copies and their local profiles together. Enforce immutable/declarative owned code as well as the portable Effect baseline. No silent version downgrade or blanket exception. |\n256:| CSF-007 | Let Alchemy own infrastructure, domains and secret inputs | One native graph pairs Website/API for each stage. Production uses taxkit.dev/api.taxkit.dev; Previews never call Production. Each host binds its own origin from native Cloudflare.Worker.URL and receives another host's address through native resource Outputs. No duplicated hard-coded app origin. DNS/zone ownership, retained resources, Doppler stage selection and secret precedence are explicit before apply. |\n259:| CSF-010 | Complete a qualified replacement and operational handover | Inventory retained source, history and deployed identities before removing wiring. Keep release/consumer proof, stage isolation, approvals and rollback intent. Replace obsolete commands, docs, skills, lint scopes and CI in the owning slice. Distinguish local, Preview, provider and Production proof. |\n332:There is no claim that React, Effect, the host or a vendor SDK has no internal\n339:host requirements, and no longer treats a total leaf as permission for local\n340:mutation. TaxKit's stronger requirement admits only a host-imposed primitive\n343:construct that the host needs; a Promise-returning adapter exception does not\n364:across owned source, tests, tools, infrastructure and configuration. Exact host\n365:adapters get only their necessary exception; generated/vendor exclusions are\n399:no parent path, glob or whole-file exception. Prove nearby mutations remain\n400:rejected and that removing/disabling a required rule or broadening an exception\n402:the type side; structural review covers helper purpose, Schema ownership and\n407:passing `Effect.runPromise` to a pipe, must be rejected outside the exact host\n410:is insufficient. Primitive host adapters cannot become a generic `run`\n440:| `calculator_used` | A supported hosted calculation completes successfully | Catalogue calculator ID/name only. No inputs, year selection, amounts, facts, report or result fields. |\n455:Manage retained TaxKit Production and one shared Preview PostHog project through\n457:actual organisation/credentials in the reviewed provider plan. Local analytics\n458:is disabled. Ordinary Previews are disabled; an explicit controlled Preview\n459:proof can enable its Preview project. Production capture tokens are public\n479:analytics exception to separate machine routes. Fix its regional upstream,\n499:`deployment.environment.name=production|preview|development`. Bind repository,\n509:metrics and flush through bounded host background work with explicit cleanup.\n537:bodies, values, results, raw exceptions/Schema issues, secrets or raw headers.\n548:Resolve that observed constraint through a reviewed design change before\n554:on ordinary Preview teardown. Dashboards, tokens and destinations must have\n563:redirect and `api.taxkit.dev`. Preview uses its own temporary native addresses\n568:public DNS or DNSSEC has converged. Recheck current Alchemy domain and Preview\n572:`Cloudflare.Worker.URL`. Another host's address comes from that resource's native\n576:infrastructure inputs. Qualify local, Preview and custom-domain address behaviour\n588:Before each provider mutation, the reviewed version-matched plan must identify\n598:qualification, then prove one native two-app calculator. Expand calculators and\n606:| Tax rules/core/calculator owners and READMEs under `packages/core`, `packages/calculators`, `packages/rules/au/*` | Change required | Compatibility/type/input/interface corrections in T002/T004; preserve valid known results and rate tables. Owning package tests, whole test run, reviewed Changesets. |\n610:| Root manifests/lock/runtime, `turbo.json`, TypeScript, `oxlint.config.ts`, `oxfmt.config.ts`, `knip*.json`, `tools/oxlint/**`, language-service config, `tools/quality-workflow/**` and quality workflow | Change required | Exact qualifie