{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:47:36.467Z","ordinal":13899,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_06b7a884f26959d3016ac2751434c087d0b1265b7ed718505a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_dXG0Cp588yEMYmhISu90r9bJ","name":"exec","input":"const r=await Promise.allSettled([tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '335,405p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json; sed -n '135,178p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md; cat alchemy.run.ts packages/infrastructure/README.md\",max_output_tokens:6000}),tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,150p' .agents/skills/alchemy-iac/SKILL.md; sed -n '1,180p' docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md; cat packages/calculators/src/service.ts\",max_output_tokens:6500}),tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg --files node_modules/effect/src | rg '/rpc/|Rpc'; rg --files packages/infrastructure/src | head -35; rg -n 'httpWebApp|layerProtocolHttp|layerProtocolHttp|toHttpApp|makeProtocolHttp|layerJson|HttpServerRequest' node_modules/effect/src/rpc/*.ts\",max_output_tokens:6000})]);r.forEach((v,i)=>text({i,...v}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","create_time":1791128842.101295}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:47:36.468Z","ordinal":13900,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","session_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","root_turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","response_id":"resp_06b7a884f26959d3016ac27509fcb087d0ab7612f03d02f3b5","usage":{"input_tokens":150082,"cached_input_tokens":149120,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":465,"reasoning_output_tokens":219,"total_tokens":150547},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":266251214,"cached_input_tokens":261052544,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1377607,"reasoning_output_tokens":550578,"total_tokens":267628821},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":266251214,"cached_input_tokens":261052544,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1377607,"reasoning_output_tokens":550578,"total_tokens":267628821}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:47:36.546Z","ordinal":13901,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5e64d428-fde0-4768-807b-64b506dd55a9","process_id":"29525","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '335,405p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json; sed -n '135,178p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md; cat alchemy.run.ts packages/infrastructure/README.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '335,405p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json; sed -n '135,178p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md; cat alchemy.run.ts packages/infrastructure/README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-foundation-acceptance-review.json\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CSF-T003\",\n      \"title\": \"Prove one native API and Website path\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-003\",\n        \"CSF-004\",\n        \"CSF-007\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T002\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Rebuild apps/api as a native Alchemy Worker and apps/web as a standard TanStack Website using one real existing calculator.\",\n        \"Implement the Q9-agreed native Effect RPC in packages/api/rpc with shared calculator/content Schemas, thin handlers and private generated client Layers. Use native JSON serialisation and explicitly select HTTP POST rather than the native server WebSocket default. Keep the public HTTP adapter separate and call the same named application operation.\",\n        \"Qualify checked semantic client errors, malformed-reply handling, safe RPC expected/defect/protocol replies, contract version agreement, credential/redirect/origin policy, one whole-response deadline and earlier caller interruption. Recheck every native fatal/global defect path and unknown-tag/invalid-envelope bypass as well as per-procedure encoding; an outer HTTP reporter, custom procedure defect Schema or codecFor hook alone is insufficient privacy proof. Qualify supported ingress treatment or an exact reviewed native correction where required.\",\n        \"Use native instance/request lifetimes, matching-stage service binding/public address, one Website server runner and a React-owned browser Atom graph; no extra backend runner or Effect Context through TanStack. Bind each host's own origin from native Cloudflare.Worker.URL and cross-host addresses from native resource Outputs, decoded once at application ingress. Missing Outputs fail checked configuration without guessed or concatenated addresses.\",\n        \"Select native Stack.secrets/Doppler at the infrastructure root with explicit stage/precedence; qualify bindings without applying a cloud plan.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"apps/api/src/**, apps/web/src/**, packages/api/rpc/**, packages/api/http/src/** and packages/infrastructure/src/** native composition\",\n        \"alchemy.run.ts and exact stage/secret configuration owners\",\n        \"apps/api/README.md, apps/web/README.md, packages/api/rpc/README.md, packages/api/http/README.md, packages/infrastructure/README.md and affected architecture\",\n        \"Focused client/Worker/lifetime tests and a local two-app receipt\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/api-http test\",\n        \"bun run api:smoke\",\n        \"bun run check-types\",\n        \"bun run build\",\n        \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Exercise initial render and client navigation against the matching local API.\",\n        \"Check actual post-initialisation Worker startup, browser CORS, full response decoding, slow headers/stalled bodies, abort, route change and unmount.\",\n        \"Inspect the production browser bundle for server/Alchemy/provider credentials or live domain implementations.\",\n        \"Use the actual generated RPC client and native POST/JSON server through browser URL and private server binding. Prove expected error/hydration round-trip, bad valid-JSON reply, unrelated adapter defect, version skew, malformed envelopes/unknown tags/invalid IDs, sensitive sentinels in all native reply/log/trace paths, and abort during complete body decoding.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n        \"No package/app domain code constructs a runtime or builds a live Layer mid-operation.\",\n        \"The same-stage origin/binding and deadline/cancellation claims have runtime evidence.\",\n        \"Website RPC, HTTP and later MCP reuse one checked application operation. Native RPC wire privacy and failure classification have source/version-matched proof, not assumed defaults or handwritten protocol framing.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CSF-T004\",\n      \"title\": \"Finish calculator pages and the fresh package interface\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\nanalytics or calculation Schemas. Browser WebMCP calls the visible page\ncommands, then the same website client.\n\nThe Website server runner supplies a private same-stage service-binding\ntransport; browser Atom supplies the checked public API URL from the root\nloader. Both implement the same named checked client contract and keep the\nnative generated client private. The Website has no live rule engine, authored\nsource loader, RPC server or backend fallback. Calculator facts go only in\nbounded bodies; reports live only in the current calculation/page state.\nCredentials are omitted and unexpected redirects rejected for public browser\ncalls. Actual native request headers determine the tested CORS allowlist.\n\nVersion the RPC contract and qualify a checked compatibility boundary so\nindependently activated Website/API Workers fail safely during version skew.\nA single Alchemy plan does not make activation atomic. Keep public HTTP/OpenAPI\nversioning and package Changesets explicit; a fresh SDK interface is not\npermission to silently repurpose an already published wire contract. T001\nestablishes any existing public consumer/version before selecting its successor.\n\nPrivate client Layers distinguish expected calculation errors, unavailable\ntransport, incompatible contract and malformed replies. Keep one total budget\nthrough headers and decoded body; preserve earlier caller interruption and\nclose abandoned bodies. Root-owned RPC/client resources survive individual\nrequest cleanup and are released at their actual host/browser lifetime. Native\nAPI handlers run in the incoming Effect fibre with no extra ManagedRuntime.\n\nExact Effect 4.0.0 exports RPC at `effect/rpc`, while the RPC source still marks\nthe APIs unstable. Requalify the older skill's invalid-reply decoder workaround,\nnative error/defect encoders, JSON codec and Alchemy integration against this\nselected source; copy no RC-specific workaround without evidence. A safe outer\nHTTP reporter alone does not prove that native RPC replies omit raw Causes,\nSchema inputs or stack details. Native global/fatal defect paths, malformed\nenvelopes, unknown procedure tags and request IDs also need qualification;\nper-procedure defect encoding alone does not cover them. Test actual wire\nreplies, request/response payloads and native logs with sensitive sentinels,\nincluding malformed valid-JSON responses and an unrelated adapter defect.\nThe public serialisation `codecFor` hook is a candidate supported adapter,\nnot yet proof that every native path is safe: an unknown-procedure response\nuses an identity encoder and can reflect its supplied tag. Qualify a supported\nchecked ingress treatment or an exact reviewed native correction for uncovered\npaths. No complete redaction capability has been established. Do not replace\nthe native protocol\nwith handwritten framing or broadly convert every defect to an expected error.\n\nimport {\n  declareDocsStack,\n  docsCloudflareStackName,\n} from \"@taxkit/infrastructure/stack\";\nimport { decodeDocsCloudflareStackStage } from \"@taxkit/infrastructure/website\";\nimport * as Alchemy from \"alchemy\";\nimport * as Cloudflare from \"alchemy/Cloudflare\";\nimport { Stack } from \"alchemy/Stack\";\nimport { Stage } from \"alchemy/Stage\";\nimport * as Effect from \"effect/Effect\";\n\nexport default Alchemy.Stack(\n  docsCloudflareStackName,\n  {\n    providers: Cloudflare.providers(),\n    state: Cloudflare.state(),\n  },\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\n    const stack = yield* Stack;\n    const stage = yield* Stage.pipe(\n      Effect.flatMap(decodeDocsCloudflareStackStage)\n    );\n    return yield* declareDocsStack({ stackName: stack.name, stage });\n  })\n);\n---\ndocument_type: package-guide\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: supporting\nowner: taxkit-infrastructure-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-04\nreview_trigger: Alchemy resource, stage, provider, state, or package-export change\n---\n\n# TaxKit infrastructure\n\nThis private source-only package owns the docs Alchemy stage and one Website\nresource declaration. Root `alchemy.run.ts` selects the Cloudflare provider\nand state store, decodes the stage, and calls `declareDocsStack`. The docs app\nowns Vite and the Worker code; it does not depend on this package.\n\nIts explicit `./stage`, `./website` and `./stack` exports remain source-only:\ncallers need the repository's TypeScript-aware Alchemy/Bun toolchain. Shared\nmemo settings are readonly, including nested workspace arrays. The stack gives\nAlchemy fresh arrays at the provider input because its current types require\nwritable arrays; callers must also copy these arrays before using a writable\nprovider input. Values, source selection and cache invalidation are preserved.\n\nThe stack keeps `TaxKitDocsCloudflare`, `DocsWebsite`, `dev_<user>`,\n`pr-N` and `prod` stable. It has no runtime binding, custom domain,\ndatabase or Axiom resource. Deployment admission, state/provider readback and\nreceipts live in `tools/docs-deployment`.\n\nRun `bun run --filter=@taxkit/infrastructure check-types` and\n`bun run --filter=@taxkit/infrastructure test` for local declaration proof.\nThe test command uses Bun-hosted Vitest and the native Effect runner. It checks\nstage acceptance/rejection, bounded log settings and the actual app-owned asset\nheader file through native file/path services. Compiler controls require both\ntop-level and nested memo arrays to remain readonly. Canonical strict rules\ncover all package source/tests, with no test runtime execution permission.\nThese commands do not plan, deploy or prove provider state. See\n[`docs/architecture/deployment.md`](../../docs/architecture/deployment.md)\nand [the deployment runbook](../../docs/runbooks/docs-deployment.md).\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-foundation-acceptance-review.json\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CSF-T003\",\n      \"title\": \"Prove one native API and Website path\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-003\",\n        \"CSF-004\",\n        \"CSF-007\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T002\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Rebuild apps/api as a native Alchemy Worker and apps/web as a standard TanStack Website using one real existing calculator.\",\n        \"Implement the Q9-agreed native Effect RPC in packages/api/rpc with shared calculator/content Schemas, thin handlers and private generated client Layers. Use native JSON serialisation and explicitly select HTTP POST rather than the native server WebSocket default. Keep the public HTTP adapter separate and call the same named application operation.\",\n        \"Qualify checked semantic client errors, malformed-reply handling, safe RPC expected/defect/protocol replies, contract version agreement, credential/redirect/origin policy, one whole-response deadline and earlier caller interruption. Recheck every native fatal/global defect path and unknown-tag/invalid-envelope bypass as well as per-procedure encoding; an outer HTTP reporter, custom procedure defect Schema or codecFor hook alone is insufficient privacy proof. Qualify supported ingress treatment or an exact reviewed native correction where required.\",\n        \"Use native instance/request lifetimes, matching-stage service binding/public address, one Website server runner and a React-owned browser Atom graph; no extra backend runner or Effect Context through TanStack. Bind each host's own origin from native Cloudflare.Worker.URL and cross-host addresses from native resource Outputs, decoded once at application ingress. Missing Outputs fail checked configuration without guessed or concatenated addresses.\",\n        \"Select native Stack.secrets/Doppler at the infrastructure root with explicit stage/precedence; qualify bindings without applying a cloud plan.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"apps/api/src/**, apps/web/src/**, packages/api/rpc/**, packages/api/http/src/** and packages/infrastructure/src/** native composition\",\n        \"alchemy.run.ts and exact stage/secret configuration owners\",\n        \"apps/api/README.md, apps/web/README.md, packages/api/rpc/README.md, packages/api/http/README.md, packages/infrastructure/README.md and affected architecture\",\n        \"Focused client/Worker/lifetime tests and a local two-app receipt\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/api-http test\",\n        \"bun run api:smoke\",\n        \"bun run check-types\",\n        \"bun run build\",\n        \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Exercise initial render and client navigation against the matching local API.\",\n        \"Check actual post-initialisation Worker startup, browser CORS, full response decoding, slow headers/stalled bodies, abort, route change and unmount.\",\n        \"Inspect the production browser bundle for server/Alchemy/provider credentials or live domain implementations.\",\n        \"Use the actual generated RPC client and native POST/JSON server through browser URL and private server binding. Prove expected error/hydration round-trip, bad valid-JSON reply, unrelated adapter defect, version skew, malformed envelopes/unknown tags/invalid IDs, sensitive sentinels in all native reply/log/trace paths, and abort during complete body decoding.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n        \"No package/app domain code constructs a runtime or builds a live Layer mid-operation.\",\n        \"The same-stage origin/binding and deadline/cancellation claims have runtime evidence.\",\n        \"Website RPC, HTTP and later MCP reuse one checked application operation. Native RPC wire privacy and failure classification have source/version-matched proof, not assumed defaults or handwritten protocol framing.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CSF-T004\",\n      \"title\": \"Finish calculator pages and the fresh package interface\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\nanalytics or calculation Schemas. Browser WebMCP calls the visible page\ncommands, then the same website client.\n\nThe Website server runner supplies a private same-stage service-binding\ntransport; browser Atom supplies the checked public API URL from the root\nloader. Both implement the same named checked client contract and keep the\nnative generated client private. The Website has no live rule engine, authored\nsource loader, RPC server or backend fallback. Calculator facts go only in\nbounded bodies; reports live only in the current calculation/page state.\nCredentials are omitted and unexpected redirects rejected for public browser\ncalls. Actual native request headers determine the tested CORS allowlist.\n\nVersion the RPC contract and qualify a checked compatibility boundary so\nindependently activated Website/API Workers fail safely during version skew.\nA single Alchemy plan does not make activation atomic. Keep public HTTP/OpenAPI\nversioning and package Changesets explicit; a fresh SDK interface is not\npermission to silently repurpose an already published wire contract. T001\nestablishes any existing public consumer/version before selecting its successor.\n\nPrivate client Layers distinguish expected calculation errors, unavailable\ntransport, incompatible contract and malformed replies. Keep one total budget\nthrough headers and decoded body; preserve earlier caller interruption and\nclose abandoned bodies. Root-owned RPC/client resources survive individual\nrequest cleanup and are released at their actual host/browser lifetime. Native\nAPI handlers run in the incoming Effect fibre with no extra ManagedRuntime.\n\nExact Effect 4.0.0 exports RPC at `effect/rpc`, while the RPC source still marks\nthe APIs unstable. Requalify the older skill's invalid-reply decoder workaround,\nnative error/defect encoders, JSON codec and Alchemy integration against this\nselected source; copy no RC-specific workaround without evidence. A safe outer\nHTTP reporter alone does not prove that native RPC replies omit raw Causes,\nSchema inputs or stack details. Native global/fatal defect paths, malformed\nenvelopes, unknown procedure tags and request IDs also need qualification;\nper-procedure defect encoding alone does not cover them. Test actual wire\nreplies, request/response payloads and native logs with sensitive sentinels,\nincluding malformed valid-JSON responses and an unrelated adapter defect.\nThe public serialisation `codecFor` hook is a candidate supported adapter,\nnot yet proof that every native path is safe: an unknown-procedure response\nuses an identity encoder and can reflect its supplied tag. Qualify a supported\nchecked ingress treatment or an exact reviewed native correction for uncovered\npaths. No complete redaction capability has been established. Do not replace\nthe native protocol\nwith handwritten framing or broadly convert every defect to an expected error.\n\nimport {\n  declareDocsStack,\n  docsCloudflareStackName,\n} from \"@taxkit/infrastructure/stack\";\nimport { decodeDocsCloudflareStackStage } from \"@taxkit/infrastructure/website\";\nimport * as Alchemy from \"alchemy\";\nimport * as Cloudflare from \"alchemy/Cloudflare\";\nimport { Stack } from \"alchemy/Stack\";\nimport { Stage } from \"alchemy/Stage\";\nimport * as Effect from \"effect/Effect\";\n\nexport default Alchemy.Stack(\n  docsCloudflareStackName,\n  {\n    providers: Cloudflare.providers(),\n    state: Cloudflare.state(),\n  },\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\n    const stack = yield* Stack;\n    const stage = yield* Stage.pipe(\n      Effect.flatMap(decodeDocsCloudflareStackStage)\n    );\n    return yield* declareDocsStack({ stackName: stack.name, stage });\n  })\n);\n---\ndocument_type: package-guide\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: supporting\nowner: taxkit-infrastructure-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-04\nreview_trigger: Alchemy resource, stage, provider, state, or package-export change\n---\n\n# TaxKit infrastructure\n\nThis private source-only package owns the docs Alchemy stage and one Website\nresource declaration. Root `alchemy.run.ts` selects the Cloudflare provider\nand state store, decodes the stage, and calls `declareDocsStack`. The docs app\nowns Vite and the Worker code; it does not depend on this package.\n\nIts explicit `./stage`, `./website` and `./stack` exports remain source-only:\ncallers need the repository's TypeScript-aware Alchemy/Bun toolchain. Shared\nmemo settings are readonly, including nested workspace arrays. The stack gives\nAlchemy fresh arrays at the provider input because its current types require\nwritable arrays; callers must also copy these arrays before using a writable\nprovider input. Values, source selection and cache invalidation are preserved.\n\nThe stack keeps `TaxKitDocsCloudflare`, `DocsWebsite`, `dev_<user>`,\n`pr-N` and `prod` stable. It has no runtime binding, custom domain,\ndatabase or Axiom resource. Deployment admission, state/provider readback and\nreceipts live in `tools/docs-deployment`.\n\nRun `bun run --filter=@taxkit/infrastructure check-types` and\n`bun run --filter=@taxkit/infrastructure test` for local declaration proof.\nThe test command uses Bun-hosted Vitest and the native Effect runner. It checks\nstage acceptance/rejection, bounded log settings and the actual app-owned asset\nheader file t