ting span statuses)\n *\n * ```ts import.meta.vitest\n * import { Exit } from \"effect\"\n * import type { Tracer } from \"effect\"\n *\n * const startTime = 1_000_000_000n\n * const endTime = 1_500_000_000n\n516: * Use to prevent spans in a scope from propagating tracing context.\n520: * When enabled on fiber or span annotations, new spans are created as\n521: * non-propagating no-op spans and disabled spans are skipped when deriving a\n522: * parent span.\n524: * **Example** (Disabling span propagation)\n529: * // Disable span propagation for a specific effect\n550: * Use to set the default trace level for spans in a scope when span options do\n558: * @see {@link MinimumTraceLevel} for the threshold that decides whether spans at that level are sampled\n575: * Use to set the trace-level threshold that controls whether spans are sampled\n580: * The default value is `\"All\"`. Span creation compares the span level from\n587: * @see {@link CurrentTraceLevel} for the default span level used when options do not specify one\n645: * observe, such as recording span attributes.\n651:  span: (options) => new NativeSpan(options)\n656: * generates span and trace identifiers, stores attributes, events, and links,\n661: * The constructor initializes the span with `Started` status. Trace and span\n663: * first access, so spans that are never inspected allocate as little as\n667: * @see {@link Span} for the interface implemented by native spans\n685:  _spanId: string | undefined = undefined\n715:  get spanId(): string {\n716:    return this._spanId ??= Hex.random(16)\n"},"started_at_ms":1791131069375,"completed_at_ms":1791131069375}}
