{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T16:29:06.488Z","ordinal":14864,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_06b7a884f26959d3016ac27eb72d5887d0aa43f482739bdf19","status":"completed","call_id":"call_a6cFPfnPFvCoRZETT13usyB3","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfor f in ('packages/core/src/engine/calculation-engine.ts','packages/rules/au/pay/src/calculator/take-home-pay.ts','packages/rules/au/income-tax/src/calculator/annual-tax.ts'):\\n p=Path(f);s=p.read_text().replace('from \\\"./schemas.js\\\";\\\\nexport','from \\\"./schemas.js\\\";\\\\n\\\\nexport');p.write_text(s)\\np=Path('packages/rules/au/pay/src/calculator/take-home-pay.ts');s=p.read_text();a=s.index('/**\\\\n * Calculates the pay-period withholding ledger');b=s.index('/**\\\\n * Builds the typed scenario layer',a);s=s[:a]+s[b:];p.write_text(s)\\np=Path('docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md');s=p.read_text().replace('last_reviewed: 2026-10-04','last_reviewed: 2026-10-05',1);anchor='## Export boundaries';section='''## Native website RPC (T003 in progress)\\n\\n`@taxkit/api-rpc` now owns one versioned `Calculate` procedure over canonical\\ncalculator request/result Schemas. Its native server explicitly mounts POST\\n`/rpc` with JSON; its handler delegates to `PublicCalculatorService.calculate`.\\nThe private generated client lives in the caller's Layer scope. Expected\\ncalculator failures project to fixed reasons, while version disagreement,\\nunavailable transport, invalid replies and a complete-response deadline remain\\nseparate checked failures. Independent adapter defects remain defects.\\n\\nNative parser ingress checks procedure tags, bounded identities/batches/headers\\nand a one-MiB UTF-8 input before dispatch. Native per-procedure and global defect\\nencoding use a fixed value. The client marks only the native exit reply decoder;\\nit does not classify every SchemaError as an invalid response. Installed Effect\\n4.0.0 source and actual wire tests qualify these hooks. RPC APIs remain unstable.\\n\\nThe [package README](../../packages/api/rpc/README.md) owns its explicit exports\\nand current proof limits. The existing apps do not consume it yet; T003's real\\nWorker/Website binding, browser CORS, origin and tracing qualification remain\\nin progress. Public HTTP/OpenAPI still has its existing contract and runtime.\\n\\nCalculator Schemas use narrow core/rule Schema entrypoints. Diagnostics and\\nreport/input definitions have separate canonical modules; old entrypoints\\nre-export the same definitions. Browser transport imports therefore avoid live\\nengine/calculator/rule-pack modules. This changes export ownership, not tax\\nrules or retained report values. It does not change the SDK's deliberate local\\ncalculation composition.\\n\\n''';s=s.replace(anchor,section+anchor);p.write_text(s)\\np=Path('docs/architecture/package-ownership.md');s=p.read_text();anchor='`packages/sdk/typescript`';s=s.replace(anchor,'''`packages/api/rpc`\\n: Private compiled native Effect RPC transport. It owns one versioned calculation\\n  procedure, thin calculator-service handler, checked POST/JSON ingress and\\n  caller-scoped private client Layers. Calculator/content Schemas remain with\\n  their existing owners. Explicit test-only composition is separate; no app\\n  runtime or backend fallback belongs here. T003 app-host composition is pending.\\n\\n'''+anchor,1).replace('while a future product workflow is still unscoped.','while the accepted T003 calculator workflow is being implemented.');p.write_text(s)\\np=Path('docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md');s=p.read_text();s+='''\\n## Native RPC contract proof\\n\\nThe private `@taxkit/api-rpc` test command uses the actual Effect 4 generated\\nclient, JSON parser and POST server. Its corpus checks the real retained\\ncalculator, expected error classes, global/per-procedure native defects, bounded\\nand malformed envelopes, unknown tags/IDs, version skew, broken JSON and invalid\\nsuccess replies. Private sentinels must be absent from actual native reply bytes\\nand captured logs. An independent adapter SchemaError keeps its exact defect\\nidentity. Deterministic clock/body fixtures prove one deadline through headers\\nand complete decoding, earlier interruption and scope cleanup. Operation-policy\\nproof observes credential omission and redirect rejection at HttpClient ingress.\\n\\nThis corpus does not prove browser CORS, service binding, Worker origin,\\nproduction app startup or safe exported traces. Those are remaining T003 host\\nchecks. A browser build of the private client exposed live calculation modules\\nthrough broad Schema imports; narrow canonical diagnostics/report/input exports\\nremove those modules. Real Website bundle proof remains required after app\\ncomposition. Existing golden calculator and packed SDK checks protect the old\\nexports and report values when these Schema owners move.\\n''';p.write_text(s)\\nfor loc,title,owner,section in [\\n ('packages/core','TaxKit Core','taxkit-core-owner','The browser-safe `@taxkit/core/engine/schemas` entrypoint owns `CalculationDiagnostics` without importing the live engine. Existing core/engine/root exports re-export the same class.'),\\n ('packages/rules/au/pay','Australian pay rules','taxkit-au-pay-owner','Use `@taxkit/rules-au-pay/schemas` for canonical calculator metadata, `TakeHomePayReport`, `PayWithholdingsLedger` and `TakeHomeScenarioInputSchema` without live calculator or rule-pack imports. Existing root/calculator exports retain the same definitions and calculation behaviour.'),\\n ('packages/rules/au/income-tax','Australian income tax rules','taxkit-au-income-tax-owner','Use `@taxkit/rules-au-income-tax/schemas` for canonical calculator metadata, `AnnualTaxReport` and `AnnualTaxScenarioInputSchema` without live calculator or rule-pack imports. Existing root/calculator exports retain the same definitions and calculation behaviour.'),\\n ('packages/calculators','Calculators','taxkit-calculators-owner','`@taxkit/calculators/schemas` consumes narrow core/rule Schema entrypoints and owns no live runtime or rule pack. The RPC contract reuses its existing request and report Schemas; calculation remains with `PublicCalculatorService.calculate`.')]:\\n p=Path(loc)/'README.md';s=p.read_text();s+='\\\\n## Browser Schema entrypoints\\\\n\\\\n'+section+'\\\\n\\\\nThe [transport architecture](%sdocs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md) and active clean-slate plan own application use and proof limits.\\\\n'%('../'* (len(Path(loc).parts)));p.write_text(s)\\np=Path('.changeset/native-calculator-rpc.md');s=p.read_text().replace('\\\"@taxkit/api-rpc\\\": minor','\\\"@taxkit/api-rpc\\\": minor\\\\n\\\"@taxkit/core\\\": minor\\\\n\\\"@taxkit/rules-au-pay\\\": minor\\\\n\\\"@taxkit/rules-au-income-tax\\\": minor\\\\n\\\"@taxkit/calculators\\\": patch');s+='\\\\nSeparate canonical diagnostics and calculator report/input Schemas from live\\\\ncalculation imports, and add narrow public Schema exports. Existing exports\\\\nretain the same class identities and calculation values.\\\\n';p.write_text(s)\\nPY\",max_output_tokens:1500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","create_time":1791131300.449118}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T16:29:06.611Z","ordinal":14865,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2e8a24fa-9f33-4d0f-a84c-a22a3f5b08c3","process_id":"56053","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor f in ('packages/core/src/engine/calculation-engine.ts','packages/rules/au/pay/src/calculator/take-home-pay.ts','packages/rules/au/income-tax/src/calculator/annual-tax.ts'):\n p=Path(f);s=p.read_text().replace('from \"./schemas.js\";\\nexport','from \"./schemas.js\";\\n\\nexport');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('packages/rules/au/pay/src/calculator/take-home-pay.ts');s=p.read_text();a=s.index('/**\\n * Calculates the pay-period withholding ledger');b=s.index('/**\\n * Builds the typed scenario layer',a);s=s[:a]+s[b:];p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md');s=p.read_text().replace('last_reviewed: 2026-10-04','last_reviewed: 2026-10-05',1);anchor='## Export boundaries';section='''## Native website RPC (T003 in progress)\n\n`@taxkit/api-rpc` now owns one versioned `Calculate` procedure over canonical\ncalculator request/result Schemas. Its native server explicitly mounts POST\n`/rpc` with JSON; its handler delegates to `PublicCalculatorService.calculate`.\nThe private generated client lives in the caller's Layer scope. Expected\ncalculator failures project to fixed reasons, while version disagreement,\nunavailable transport, invalid replies and a complete-response deadline remain\nseparate checked failures. Independent adapter defects remain defects.\n\nNative parser ingress checks procedure tags, bounded identities/batches/headers\nand a one-MiB UTF-8 input before dispatch. Native per-procedure and global defect\nencoding use a fixed value. The client marks only the native exit reply decoder;\nit does not classify every SchemaError as an invalid response. Installed Effect\n4.0.0 source and actual wire tests qualify these hooks. RPC APIs remain unstable.\n\nThe [package README](../../packages/api/rpc/README.md) owns its explicit exports\nand current proof limits. The existing apps do not consume it yet; T003's real\nWorker/Website binding, browser CORS, origin and tracing qualification remain\nin progress. Public HTTP/OpenAPI still has its existing contract and runtime.\n\nCalculator Schemas use narrow core/rule Schema entrypoints. Diagnostics and\nreport/input definitions have separate canonical modules; old entrypoints\nre-export the same definitions. Browser transport imports therefore avoid live\nengine/calculator/rule-pack modules. This changes export ownership, not tax\nrules or retained report values. It does not change the SDK's deliberate local\ncalculation composition.\n\n''';s=s.replace(anchor,section+anchor);p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/architecture/package-ownership.md');s=p.read_text();anchor='`packages/sdk/typescript`';s=s.replace(anchor,'''`packages/api/rpc`\n: Private compiled native Effect RPC transport. It owns one versioned calculation\n  procedure, thin calculator-service handler, checked POST/JSON ingress and\n  caller-scoped private client Layers. Calculator/content Schemas remain with\n  their existing owners. Explicit test-only composition is separate; no app\n  runtime or backend fallback belongs here. T003 app-host composition is pending.\n\n'''+anchor,1).replace('while a future product workflow is still unscoped.','while the accepted T003 calculator workflow is being implemented.');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md');s=p.read_text();s+='''\n## Native RPC contract proof\n\nThe private `@taxkit/api-rpc` test command uses the actual Effect 4 generated\nclient, JSON parser and POST server. Its corpus checks the real retained\ncalculator, expected error classes, global/per-procedure native defects, bounded\nand malformed envelopes, unknown tags/IDs, version skew, broken JSON and invalid\nsuccess replies. Private sentinels must be absent from actual native reply bytes\nand captured logs. An independent adapter SchemaError keeps its exact defect\nidentity. Deterministic clock/body fixtures prove one deadline through headers\nand complete decoding, earlier interruption and scope cleanup. Operation-policy\nproof observes credential omission and redirect rejection at HttpClient ingress.\n\nThis corpus does not prove browser CORS, service binding, Worker origin,\nproduction app startup or safe exported traces. Those are remaining T003 host\nchecks. A browser build of the private client exposed live calculation modules\nthrough broad Schema imports; narrow canonical diagnostics/report/input exports\nremove those modules. Real Website bundle proof remains required after app\ncomposition. Existing golden calculator and packed SDK checks protect the old\nexports and report values when these Schema owners move.\n''';p.write_text(s)\nfor loc,title,owner,section in [\n ('packages/core','TaxKit Core','taxkit-core-owner','The browser-safe `@taxkit/core/engine/schemas` entrypoint owns `CalculationDiagnostics` without importing the live engine. Existing core/engine/root exports re-export the same class.'),\n ('packages/rules/au/pay','Australian pay rules','taxkit-au-pay-owner','Use `@taxkit/rules-au-pay/schemas` for canonical calculator metadata, `TakeHomePayReport`, `PayWithholdingsLedger` and `TakeHomeScenarioInputSchema` without live calculator or rule-pack imports. Existing root/calculator exports retain the same definitions and calculation behaviour.'),\n ('packages/rules/au/income-tax','Australian income tax rules','taxkit-au-income-tax-owner','Use `@taxkit/rules-au-income-tax/schemas` for canonical calculator metadata, `AnnualTaxReport` and `AnnualTaxScenarioInputSchema` without live calculator or rule-pack imports. Existing root/calculator exports retain the same definitions and calculation behaviour.'),\n ('packages/calculators','Calculators','taxkit-calculators-owner','`@taxkit/calculators/schemas` consumes narrow core/rule Schema entrypoints and owns no live runtime or rule pack. The RPC contract reuses its existing request and report Schemas; calculation remains with `PublicCalculatorService.calculate`.')]:\n p=Path(loc)/'README.md';s=p.read_text();s+='\\n## Browser Schema entrypoints\\n\\n'+section+'\\n\\nThe [transport architecture](%sdocs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md) and active clean-slate plan own application use and proof limits.\\n'%('../'* (len(Path(loc).parts)));p.write_text(s)\np=Path('.changeset/native-calculator-rpc.md');s=p.read_text().replace('\"@taxkit/api-rpc\": minor','\"@taxkit/api-rpc\": minor\\n\"@taxkit/core\": minor\\n\"@taxkit/rules-au-pay\": minor\\n\"@taxkit/rules-au-income-tax\": minor\\n\"@taxkit/calculators\": patch');s+='\\nSeparate canonical diagnostics and calculator report/input Schemas from live\\ncalculation imports, and add narrow public Schema exports. Existing exports\\nretain the same class identities and calculation values.\\n';p.write_text(s)\nPY"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor f in ('packages/core/src/engine/calculation-engine.ts','packages/rules/au/pay/src/calculator/take-home-pay.ts','packages/rules/au/income-tax/src/calculator/annual-tax.ts'):\n p=Path(f);s=p.read_text().replace('from \"./schemas.js\";\\nexport','from \"./schemas.js\";\\n\\nexport');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('packages/rules/au/pay/src/calculator/take-home-pay.ts');s=p.read_text();a=s.index('/**\\n * Calculates the pay-period withholding ledger');b=s.index('/**\\n * Builds the typed scenario layer',a);s=s[:a]+s[b:];p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md');s=p.read_text().replace('last_reviewed: 2026-10-04','last_reviewed: 2026-10-05',1);anchor='## Export boundaries';section='''## Native website RPC (T003 in progress)\n\n`@taxkit/api-rpc` now owns one versioned `Calculate` procedure over canonical\ncalculator request/result Schemas. Its native server explicitly mounts POST\n`/rpc` with JSON; its handler delegates to `PublicCalculatorService.calculate`.\nThe private generated client lives in the caller's Layer scope. Expected\ncalculator failures project to fixed reasons, while version disagreement,\nunavailable transport, invalid replies and a complete-response deadline remain\nseparate checked failures. Independent adapter defects remain defects.\n\nNative parser ingress checks procedure tags, bounded identities/batches/headers\nand a one-MiB UTF-8 input before dispatch. Native per-procedure and global defect\nencoding use a fixed value. The client marks only the native exit reply decoder;\nit does not classify every SchemaError as an invalid response. Installed Effect\n4.0.0 source and actual wire tests qualify these hooks. RPC APIs remain unstable.\n\nThe [package README](../../packages/api/rpc/README.md) owns its explicit exports\nand current proof limits. The existing apps do not consume it yet; T003's real\nWorker/Website binding, browser CORS, origin and tracing qualification remain\nin progress. Public HTTP/OpenAPI still has its existing contract and runtime.\n\nCalculator Schemas use narrow core/rule Schema entrypoints. Diagnostics and\nreport/input definitions have separate canonical modules; old entrypoints\nre-export the same definitions. Browser transport imports therefore avoid live\nengine/calculator/rule-pack modules. This changes export ownership, not tax\nrules or retained report values. It does not change the SDK's deliberate local\ncalculation composition.\n\n''';s=s.replace(anchor,section+anchor);p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/architecture/package-ownership.md');s=p.read_text();anchor='`packages/sdk/typescript`';s=s.replace(anchor,'''`packages/api/rpc`\n: Private compiled native Effect RPC transport. It owns one versioned calculation\n  procedure, thin calculator-service handler, checked POST/JSON ingress and\n