{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T16:38:00.289Z","ordinal":15020,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-dbcabc12-a22b-470d-8035-c5fbf2b64035","process_id":"27058","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '339,410p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json; cat apps/api/README.md; cat apps/web/README.md; cat alchemy.run.ts; cat packages/infrastructure/src/stack.ts; rg --files apps/api apps/web packages/infrastructure/src | head -90; tail -12 /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/dev74-rpc-verification.log"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '339,410p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json; cat apps/api/README.md; cat apps/web/README.md; cat alchemy.run.ts; cat packages/infrastructure/src/stack.ts; rg --files apps/api apps/web packages/infrastructure/src | head -90; tail -12 /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/dev74-rpc-verification.log"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"      \"id\": \"CSF-T003\",\n      \"title\": \"Prove one native API and Website path\",\n      \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-003\",\n        \"CSF-004\",\n        \"CSF-007\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T002\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Rebuild apps/api as a native Alchemy Worker and apps/web as a standard TanStack Website using one real existing calculator.\",\n        \"Implement the Q9-agreed native Effect RPC in packages/api/rpc with shared calculator/content Schemas, thin handlers and private generated client Layers. Use native JSON serialisation and explicitly select HTTP POST rather than the native server WebSocket default. Keep the public HTTP adapter separate and call the same named application operation.\",\n        \"Qualify checked semantic client errors, malformed-reply handling, safe RPC expected/defect/protocol replies, contract version agreement, credential/redirect/origin policy, one whole-response deadline and earlier caller interruption. Recheck every native fatal/global defect path and unknown-tag/invalid-envelope bypass as well as per-procedure encoding; an outer HTTP reporter, custom procedure defect Schema or codecFor hook alone is insufficient privacy proof. Qualify supported ingress treatment or an exact reviewed native correction where required.\",\n        \"Use native instance/request lifetimes, matching-stage service binding/public address, one Website server runner and a React-owned browser Atom graph; no extra backend runner or Effect Context through TanStack. Bind each host's own origin from native Cloudflare.Worker.URL and cross-host addresses from native resource Outputs, decoded once at application ingress. Missing Outputs fail checked configuration without guessed or concatenated addresses.\",\n        \"Select native Stack.secrets/Doppler at the infrastructure root with explicit stage/precedence; qualify bindings without applying a cloud plan.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"apps/api/src/**, apps/web/src/**, packages/api/rpc/**, packages/api/http/src/** and packages/infrastructure/src/** native composition\",\n        \"alchemy.run.ts and exact stage/secret configuration owners\",\n        \"apps/api/README.md, apps/web/README.md, packages/api/rpc/README.md, packages/api/http/README.md, packages/infrastructure/README.md and affected architecture\",\n        \"Focused client/Worker/lifetime tests and a local two-app receipt\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/api-http test\",\n        \"bun run api:smoke\",\n        \"bun run check-types\",\n        \"bun run build\",\n        \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Exercise initial render and client navigation against the matching local API.\",\n        \"Check actual post-initialisation Worker startup, browser CORS, full response decoding, slow headers/stalled bodies, abort, route change and unmount.\",\n        \"Inspect the production browser bundle for server/Alchemy/provider credentials or live domain implementations.\",\n        \"Use the actual generated RPC client and native POST/JSON server through browser URL and private server binding. Prove expected error/hydration round-trip, bad valid-JSON reply, unrelated adapter defect, version skew, malformed envelopes/unknown tags/invalid IDs, sensitive sentinels in all native reply/log/trace paths, and abort during complete body decoding.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n        \"No package/app domain code constructs a runtime or builds a live Layer mid-operation.\",\n        \"The same-stage origin/binding and deadline/cancellation claims have runtime evidence.\",\n        \"Website RPC, HTTP and later MCP reuse one checked application operation. Native RPC wire privacy and failure classification have source/version-matched proof, not assumed defaults or handwritten protocol framing.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-rpc-contract.json\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CSF-T004\",\n      \"title\": \"Finish calculator pages and the fresh package interface\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n---\ndocument_type: app-readme\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: taxkit-api-app-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-04\nreview_trigger: API app settings, startup, smoke command or shutdown change\n---\n\n# API App\n\nStandalone Bun process for the TaxKit Effect HTTP API.\n\n## Scope\n\n`apps/api` owns process config, Bun server startup, request dispatch to\n`@taxkit/api-http/server` and graceful shutdown. API contracts, handlers,\nschemas, generated OpenAPI and docs routes stay in `packages/api/http`.\n\n## Runtime Shape\n\nThe process entrypoint is an Effect program run with\n`@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain`. Startup reads `ApiServerConfig` from\n`ApiAppLayer`, requests are served by the Bun-backed `HttpServer` layer, and\n`SIGINT` or `SIGTERM` interrupts the root Effect fiber so scoped finalizers stop\nthe Bun server.\n\nLocal defaults:\n\n- host: `127.0.0.1`\n- port: `4000`\n\nEnvironment overrides:\n\n- `API_HOST`\n- `API_PORT`\n- `PORT` as the fallback port supplied by portless\n\n`API_PORT` takes priority. A present, invalid value fails startup rather than\nusing `PORT`; missing values use the fallback and then port 4000. Ports must\nbe whole numbers from 1 to 65535. Host names are trimmed and blank host values\nuse the default. Settings use the caller's Effect ConfigProvider; the live app\nuses the environment and tests supply isolated providers. The safe\n`ApiServerConfigError` does not include the rejected value.\n\n## Routes\n\n- `GET /api/health`\n- `GET /api/docs`\n- `GET /api/docs/openapi.json`\n- `GET /api/v1/jurisdictions`\n- `GET /api/v1/tax-years`\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators`\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId`\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId/schema`\n- `POST /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId/calculate`\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId/graph`\n- `GET /api/v1/facts`\n- `GET /api/v1/rules`\n\nPublic calculation routes are calculator, fact, rule and graph driven.\nJurisdiction and tax year are calculator context, not top-level route families.\nThe initial calculator IDs are `au.pay.take-home`, `au.pay.withholdings` and\n`au.income-tax.annual`.\n\nCalculate payloads use canonical schema values from the rule packages. The\ngenerated OpenAPI request body shows supported fact shapes under `facts.anyOf`;\nfor example, take-home-pay JSON includes tagged `GrossPay` and `Money` values.\nThe calculator service validates facts again against the selected calculator,\nso annual-tax facts sent to `au.pay.take-home` return pay-calculator input help\ninstead of being treated as a valid take-home request.\n\n## Changelog\n\nPublic API contract and deployment-facing changes are tracked in\n[CHANGELOG.md](./CHANGELOG.md). Package-level API contract changes are also\ntracked in [`@taxkit/api-http`](../../packages/api/http/CHANGELOG.md) through\nChangesets.\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api dev\nbun run --filter=api start\nbun run --filter=api smoke:public-routes\nbun run --filter=api check-types\nbun run --filter=api test\nbun run --filter=api build\nbun run --filter=api clean\n```\n\nFor local UI development, run the API and web app in separate terminals:\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api dev\nbun run --filter=web dev\n```\n\n`bun run --filter=api dev` serves this app through portless at\n`https://api.taxkit.localhost`. `bun run --filter=web dev` injects that URL\ninto `TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` for SSR and `VITE_TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` for browser\nnavigation.\n\n## Public-route smoke\n\nUse the app-owned smoke command when you need proof that the standalone Bun\nprocess serves the current public API contract:\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api smoke:public-routes\n```\n\nThe command starts `apps/api` at `http://127.0.0.1:4173` by default, waits for\n`GET /api/health`, calls the public calculator metadata route, posts a\ntake-home-pay calculation and checks the generated OpenAPI document. It then\ncreates a temp consumer workspace outside the repo, writes a dependency-free\n`fetch` consumer and runs that consumer from the temp workspace against the\nsame public HTTP routes:\n\n- `GET /api/health`\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators`\n- `POST /api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate`\n- `POST /api/v1/calculators/au.income-tax.annual/calculate`\n- `GET /api/docs/openapi.json`\n\nThe smoke script owns process lifecycle only. It validates response bodies with\nschemas exported by `@taxkit/api-http` where those schemas are public, and it\nlets the app process stop through Effect-scoped child process cleanup on\nsuccess or failure. The external consumer checks minimal public JSON evidence;\ncanonical route schema validation stays in this repo-owned smoke script. The\ntemp workspace is removed on success and failure. Failed cleanup also fails\nthe command and remains alongside an earlier command failure.\n\nWhen the default loopback port is occupied, set `TAXKIT_API_SMOKE_PORT` to an\navailable port. The isolated release-boundary harness uses this override so a\nneighbouring local development server cannot change its failure oracle.\n\nThe smoke command uses checked Config settings and arguments, named HTTP\noperations and the exported `HealthResponse`, catalog and calculation Schemas.\nThe OpenAPI check requires its calculate path before running the plain external\nconsumer. Health readiness has a 15-second total limit, including retries and\nresponse-body reading; other requests have a five-second limit. The external\nconsumer has a 30-second limit and a 1 MiB stdout limit. Its stderr is drained\nwithout retention. Successful stdout is decoded into the exact expected route\ncoverage; failures report their bounded reason and available exit code.\nCancellation stops both child processes and removes the workspace. The external\nconsumer deliberately uses ordinary JavaScript `fetch` and JSON to check a\ncaller outside the repository.\n\n`check-types` covers source, scripts, test fixtures and test configuration.\n`test` runs native Effect fixtures for settings, stalled headers/bodies,\ninvalid responses, child-process faults, cancellation and cleanup. All API\nsource and test paths receive the canonical strict rules, with execution\nadmitted only at the two existing app/command entrypoints.\n\nUse the failure simulation when you need deterministic cleanup evidence for a\ndownstream consumer failure:\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api smoke:public-routes -- --simulate-downstream-failure\n```\n\nThe simulation exits nonzero after the external consumer has covered the\npublic routes, then removes the temp workspace and stops the API process.\n\nUse the portless URL for local API smoke checks:\n\n```sh\ncurl https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/health\ncurl https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/v1/calculators\ncurl -X POST https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"facts\":{\"grossPay\":{\"_tag\":\"GrossPay\",\"amount\":{\"_tag\":\"Money\",\"cents\":150000,\"currency\":\"AUD\"},\"period\":\"weekly\"},\"taxFreeThresholdClaimed\":true}}'\n```\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Do not define API contracts in this app.\n- Keep app-owned schemas in `schemas.ts` and derive exported types from those\n  schemas. Runtime files should consume canonical schema values and compose\n  layers/startup logic, not redefine reusable shapes inline.\n- Do not manually wire process signal handlers, `process.exit`, mutable\n  shutdown flags or `try/catch` around Effect startup. The process entrypoint\n  should be an Effect program run through `BunRuntime.runMain`.\n- Do not create a runtime inside request handling.\n- Keep process-owned resources in `ApiAppLayer` so root fiber interruption\n  releases them through scoped finalizers.\n- Keep `apps/web` as an HTTP client of this app, not an in-process API mount.\n\n## Related Docs\n\n- `docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`\n- `docs/architecture/effect-services.md`\n- `docs/architecture/package-ownership.md`\n- `docs/product-specs/extract-api-app.md`\n---\nstatus: canonical\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-05\nsource_of_truth: package-readme\nconfidence: high\n---\n\n# Web App\n\nCurrent TanStack Start scaffold for TaxKit.\n\n## Scope\n\n`apps/web` proves the current browser/server runtime split and calls the\nstandalone Effect HTTP API service owned by `apps/api`. It is not the\nlong-term calculation engine and should not own tax-domain contracts or API\nrequest handling.\n\n## Main Areas\n\n- `src/routes/`: TanStack Router routes\n- `src/lib/runtime.server.ts`: server `ManagedRuntime`\n- `src/lib/runtime.client.ts`: client `ManagedRuntime`\n- `src/lib/route-context.ts`: route runtime contract and context selection\n- `src/lib/runtime-selection.ts`: isomorphic selection of the server/client runtime\n- `src/server.ts`: server entrypoint\n\n## Runtime Shape\n\nThe root route loads `@taxkit/api-http/client` through the route runtime and\nrenders API health status from the standalone API service over HTTP.\nServer-only API exports must stay out of browser code. The root loader uses\nthe native runtime contract and passes the Router abort signal to its existing\nHTTP operation. It returns readonly health fields without a hand-written\nPromise interface or a one-use runtime wrapper.\n\nThe web runtime reads the API origin from:\n\n- `TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` on the server\n- `VITE_TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` in the browser\n\nBoth are required runtime config values and are validated with the HTTP\npackage's Effect Config and URL Schema. The exact Vite host reads only the\npublic browser input using Vite's normal file/environment precedence, then\nSchema-encodes it into a typed build constant. Automatic public-prefix\nexposure is disabled; Vite still supplies its standard mode/SSR metadata.\nBrowser modules do not read\n`import.meta.env`. Missing or invalid raw URLs still fail at runtime; the build\ndoes not guess a URL or change that validation timing. Settings failures expose\nonly the client/server identity, settings operation and fixed safe message.\n`bun run --filter=web dev` injects both from\n`portless get api.taxkit`. Do not include `/api` in the base URL; the typed\nAPI client owns route prefixes.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Keep tax rules, facts and calculators in engine packages.\n- Use browser-safe API client exports from routes.\n- Do not import `@taxkit/api-http/server` from browser code.\n- Keep route data acquisition and trust-boundary conversion route-high. Render\n  the page shell and semantic landmarks before passing focused readonly values\n  and callbacks to leaves.\n- Keep local UI commands in leaves; keep remote or domain commands in the route\n  action or nearest policy-owning container.\n- Put loading, empty and recoverable error UI at the smallest owning boundary\n  while preserving a stable footprint and the surrounding page shell.\n- Keep the app README local; route durable architecture to `docs/architecture`.\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\nbun run --filter=api dev\nbun run --filter=web dev\nbun run --filter=web check-types\nbun run --filter=web test\nbun run --filter=web test:browser\nbun run --filter=web build\n```\n\nRun `apps/api` before loading the web root locally. Without the API process,\nthe root route should fail with an attributable HTTP transport error rather\nthan silently falling back to an in-process API.\n\nUse the portless URLs for local browser and app-to-app checks:\n\n- API: `https://api.taxkit.localhost`\n- Web: `https://taxkit.localhost`\n\n## Related Docs\n\n- `docs/architecture/frontend.md`\n- `docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`\n- `docs/architecture/deployment.md`\n- `docs/design-docs/abstraction-admission.md`\n\n## Atom compatibility proof\n\n`bun run web:test:browser` builds the web app and runs the Chromium qualification\nin `src/lib/atom-lifecycle.browser.test.tsx`. It is part of root `verification`.\nThe fixture uses Effect test scopes to dispose React roots on failure and proves\nSSR hydration without errors, one registry through StrictMode effect remount,\n50 rapid updates, scheduled/cancelled work and final resource disposal. It does\nnot yet replace the app's existing runtime or qualify RPC cancellation.\n\nThe exact candidate is Atom 4.0.0, React/React DOM 19.3.0 and Scheduler 0.28.0.\nThe root patch changes only Atom's Scheduler peer range to admit exactly 0.28.0;\nremove it when upstream metadata admits that version. One Scheduler version is\npresent in the lockfile. Bun resolves peers from registry metadata before patching\nand may still print the original peer warning; the installed manifest and runtime\nfixture are the qualified correction. Atom/Scheduler are development dependencies\nuntil the application migration adopts their runtime owner.\n\nThe browser test config extends Vite's browser conditions with `source`; replacing\nthe defaults with only `source` selects the Node renderer and is not a valid\nbrowser hydration test. The test imports the actual browser renderer and waits\nfor hydration before issuing updates.\n\n## Strict and route proof\n\nCanonical strict rules cover source, tests and all Vite/Vitest configuration.\nOnly the two existing runtime composition modules, root loader, Vite host and\nfake browser-test runtime have exact execution permissions. They retain all\nother rules; no async workflow or raw settings exception is admitted. The\ncompiler and development Knip graph include both test configurations and Vite.\nThe package test command uses Bun-hosted Vitest and native Effect tests.\n\nSettings tests cover valid, missing and invalid server/browser inputs, exact\nsecret-negative error bytes, public build-input selection and absent compiled\nbrowser settings. The real file-route Chromium tests call the actual generated\nHTTP client through a fake HTTP transport. They prove health decoding and\ninterruption of pending HTTP work when the Router retires its preload. The\nHTTP abort signal is observed as aborted. This proves the tested preload\nretirement, not all navigation/unmount paths or remote provider cancellation.\nBoth retained Atom/Scheduler cases still run. Browser dependencies are listed\nfor optimisation so Vite does not reload tests while they start.\nimport {\n  declareDocsStack,\n  docsCloudflareStackName,\n} from \"@taxkit/infrastructure/stack\";\nimport { decodeDocsCloudflareStackStage } from \"@taxkit/infrastructure/website\";\nimport * as Alchemy from \"alchemy\";\nimport * as Cloudflare from \"alchemy/Cloudflare\";\nimport { Stack } from \"alchemy/Stack\";\nimport { Stage } from \"alchemy/Stage\";\nimport * as Effect from \"effect/Effect\";\n\nexport default Alchemy.Stack(\n  docsCloudflareStackName,\n  {\n    providers: Cloudflare.providers(),\n    state: Cloudflare.state(),\n  },\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\n    const stack = yield* Stack;\n    const stage = yield* Stage.pipe(\n      Effect.flatMap(decodeDocsCloudflareStackStage)\n    );\n    return yield* declareDocsStack({ stackName: stack.name, stage });\n  })\n);\nimport * as Cloudflare from \"alchemy/Cloudflare\";\nimport * as Array from \"effect/Array\";\nimport * as Effect from \"effect/Effect\";\n\nimport {\n  docsWorkerAssetHeaders,\n  docsWorkerCompatibilityDate,\n  docsWorkerCompatibilityFlags,\n  docsWorkerMemo,\n  docsWorkerObservability,\n  docsWorkerResourceId,\n} from \"./cloudflare/website.js\";\nimport type { DocsCloudflareStackStage } from \"./cloudflare/website.js\";\n\nexport { docsCloudflareStackName } from \"./cloudflare/website.js\";\n\nexport const declareDocsStack = ({\n  stackName,\n  stage,\n}: {\n  readonly stackName: string;\n  readonly stage: DocsCloudflareStackStage;\n}) =>\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\n    const worker = yield* Cloudflare.Website.Vite(docsWorkerResourceId, {\n      assets: {\n        // Website.Vite does not infer the app-owned _headers file when its\n        // config is passed through Alchemy.\n        headers: docsWorkerAssetHeaders,\n        runWorkerFirst: false,\n      },\n      compatibility: {\n        date: docsWorkerCompatibilityDate,\n        flags: [...docsWorkerCompatibilityFlags],\n      },\n      // Alchemy's input requires mutable arrays; give it fresh boundary copies.\n      memo: {\n        ...docsWorkerMemo,\n        include: Array.fromIterable(docsWorkerMemo.include),\n        workspaces: Array.map(docsWorkerMemo.workspaces, (workspace) => ({\n          ...workspace,\n          include: Array.fromIterable(workspace.include),\n        })),\n      },\n      observability: docsWorkerObservability,\n      rootDir: \"apps/docs\",\n      workersDev: true,\n    });\n\n    return {\n      logicalResourceId: docsWorkerResourceId,\n      stackName,\n      stage,\n      workerName: worker.workerName,\n      workerUrl: worker.url,\n    };\n  });\npackages/infrastructure/src/stack.ts\napps/api/src/server.ts\napps/api/src/config.ts\napps/api/src/index.ts\napps/api/src/schemas.ts\napps/api/vitest.config.ts\napps/api/tsconfig.json\npackages/infrastructure/src/cloudflare/website.test.ts\npackages/infrastructure/src/cloudflare/website.ts\npackages/infrastructure/src/stage.ts\napps/web/vitest.config.ts\napps/web/vite.config.ts\napps/web/tsconfig.json\napps/web/package.json\napps/web/README.md\napps/web/vitest.browser.config.ts\napps/web/src/routeTree.gen.ts\napps/web/src/router.tsx\napps/web/src/styles.css\napps/api/scripts/schemas.ts\napps/api/scripts/smoke-public-routes.runtime.ts\napps/api/scripts/routes.ts\napps/api/scripts/smoke-boundaries.test.ts\napps/api/tsconfig.scripts.json\napps/api/package.json\napps/api/README.md\napps/api/tsconfig.tests.json\napps/api/CHANGELOG.md\napps/web/src/routes/__root.tsx\napps/web/src/routes/index.tsx\napps/web/src/server.ts\napps/web/src/lib/config.client-input.ts\napps/web/src/lib/runtime.client.ts\napps/web/src/lib/atom-lifecycle.browser.test.tsx\napps/web/src/lib/runtime-selection.ts\napps/web/src/lib/runtime.server.ts\napps/web/src/lib/config.boundary.test.ts\napps/web/src/lib/health-loader.boundary.browser.test.tsx\napps/web/src/lib/config.ts\napps/web/src/lib/config.server.ts\napps/web/src/lib/route-context.ts\napps/web/src/lib/config.client.ts\napps/api/test/config.test.ts\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow-evidence.test.ts (11 tests) 108ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/strict-boundaries.contract.test.ts (40 tests) 55ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/policy.test.ts (20 tests) 25ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow-artifact.test.ts (11 tests) 25ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/alchemy-memo.test.ts (1 test) 24ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/doppler-custody.test.ts (9 tests) 21ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow-plan-projection.test.ts (15 tests) 20ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/automation.check.runtime.test.ts (5 tests) 20ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow.contract.test.ts (18 tests) 19ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/automation.policy.test.ts (8 tests) 18ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/inventory-credentials.boundary.test.ts (10 tests) 16ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/input.boundary.test.ts (9 tests) 15ms\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"      \"id\": \"CSF-T003\",\n      \"title\": \"Prove one native API and Website path\",\n      \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-003\",\n        \"CSF-004\",\n        \"CSF-007\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T002\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Rebuild apps/api as a native Alchemy Worker and apps/web as a standard TanStack Website using one real existing calculator.\",\n        \"Implement the Q9-agreed native Effect RPC in packages/api/rpc with shared calculator/content Schemas, thin handlers and private generated client Layers. Use native JSON serialisation and explicitly select HTTP POST rather than the native server WebSocket default. Keep the public HTTP adapter separate and call the same named application operation.\",\n        \"Qualify checked semantic client errors, malformed-reply handling, safe RPC expected/defect/protocol replies, contract version agreement, credential/redirect/origin policy, one whole-response deadline and earlier caller interruption. Recheck every native fatal/global defect path and unknown-tag/invalid-envelope bypass as well as per-procedure encoding; an outer HTTP reporter, custom procedure defect Schema or codecFor hook alone is insufficient privacy proof. Qualify supported ingress treatment or an exact reviewed native correction where required.\",\n        \"Use native instance/request lifetimes, matching-stage service binding/public address, one Website server runner and a React-owned browser Atom graph; no extra backend runner or Effect Context through TanStack. Bind each host's own origin from native Cloudflare.Worker.URL and cross-host addresses from native resource Outputs, decoded once at application ingress. Missing Outputs fail checked configuration without guessed or concatenated addresses.\",\n        \"Select native Stack.secrets/Doppler at the infrastructure root with explicit stage/precedence; qualify bindings without applying a cloud plan.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"apps/api/src/**, apps/web/src/**, packages/api/rpc/**, packages/api/http/src/** and packages/infrastructure/src/** native composition\",\n        \"alchemy.run.ts and exact stage/secret configuration owners\",\n        \"apps/api/README.md, apps/web/README.md, packages/api/rpc/README.md, packages/api/http/README.md, packages/infrastructure/README.md and affected architecture\",\n        \"Focused client/Worker/lifetime tests and a local two-app receipt\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/api-http test\",\n        \"bun run api:smoke\",\n        \"bun run check-types\",\n        \"bun run build\",\n        \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Exercise initial render and client navigation against the matching local API.\",\n        \"Check actual post-initialisation Worker startup, browser CORS, full response decoding, slow headers/stalled bodies, abort, route change and unmount.\",\n        \"Inspect the production browser bundle for server/Alchemy/provider credentials or live domain implementations.\",\n        \"Use the actual generated RPC client and native POST/JSON server through browser URL and private server binding. Prove expected error/hydration round-trip, bad valid-JSON reply, unrelated adapter defect, version skew, malformed envelopes/unknown tags/invalid IDs, sensitive sentinels in all native reply/log/trace paths, and abort during complete body decoding.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n        \"No package/app domain code constructs a runtime or builds a live Layer mid-operation.\",\n        \"The same-stage origin/binding and deadline/cancellation claims have runtime evidence.\",\n        \"Website RPC, HTTP and later MCP reuse one checked application operation. Native RPC wire privacy and failure classification have source/version-matched proof, not assumed defaults or handwritten protocol framing.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-rpc-contract.json\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CSF-T004\",\n      \"title\": \"Finish calculator pages and the fresh package interface\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n---\ndocument_type: app-readme\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: taxkit-api-app-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-04\nreview_trigger: API app settings, startup, smoke command or shutdown change\n---\n\n# API App\n\nStandalone Bun process for the TaxKit Effect HTTP API.\n\n## Scope\n\n`apps/api` owns process config, Bun server startup, request dispatch to\n`@taxkit/api-http/server` and graceful shutdown. API contracts, handlers,\nschemas, generated OpenAPI and docs routes stay in `packages/api/http`.\n\n## Runtime Shape\n\nThe process entrypoint is an Effect program run with\n`@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain`. Startup reads `ApiServerConfig` from\n`ApiAppLayer`, requests are served by the Bun-backed `HttpServer` layer, and\n`SIGINT` or `SIGTERM` interrupts the root Effect fiber so scoped finalizers stop\nthe Bun server.\n\nLocal defaults:\n\n- host: `127.0.0.1`\n- port: `4000`\n\nEnvironment overrides:\n\n- `API_HOST`\n- `API_PORT`\n- `PORT` as the fallback port supplied by portless\n\n`API_PORT` takes priority. A present, invalid value fails startup rather than\nusing `PORT`; missing values use the fallback and then port 4000. Ports must\nbe whole numbers from 1 to 65535. Host names are trimmed and blank host values\nuse the default. Settings use the caller's Effect ConfigProvider; the live app\nuses the environment and tests supply isolated providers. The safe\n`ApiServerConfigError` does not include the rejected value.\n\n## Routes\n\n- `GET /api/health`\n- `GET /api/docs`\n- `GET /api/docs/openapi.json`\n- `GET /api/v1/jurisdictions`\n- `GET /api/v1/tax-years`\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators`\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId`\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId/schema`\n- `POST /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId/calculate`\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId/graph`\n- `GET /api/v1/facts`\n- `GET /api/v1/rules`\n\nPublic calculation routes are calculator, fact, rule and graph driven.\nJurisdiction and tax year are calculator context, not top-level route families.\nThe initial calculator IDs are `au.pay.take-home`, `au.pay.withholdings` and\n`au.income-tax.annual`.\n\nCalculate payloads use canonical schema values from the rule packages. The\ngenerated OpenAPI request body shows supported fact shapes under `facts.anyOf`;\nfor example, take-home-pay JSON includes tagged `GrossPay` and `Money` values.\nThe calculator service validates facts again against the selected calculator,\nso annual-tax facts sent to `au.pay.take-home` return pay-calculator input help\ninstead of being treated as a valid take-home request.\n\n## Changelog\n\nPublic API contract and deployment-facing changes are tracked in\n[CHANGELOG.md](./CHANGELOG.md). Package-level API contract changes are also\ntracked in [`@taxkit/api-http`](../../packages/api/http/CHANGELOG.md) through\nChangesets.\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api dev\nbun run --filter=api start\nbun run --filter=api smoke:public-routes\nbun run --filter=api check-types\nbun run --filter=api test\nbun run --filter=api build\nbun run --filter=api clean\n```\n\nFor local UI development, run the API and web app in separate terminals:\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api dev\nbun run --filter=web dev\n```\n\n`bun run --filter=api dev` serves this app through portless at\n`https://api.taxkit.localhost`. `bun run --filter=web dev` injects that URL\ninto `TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` for SSR and `VITE_TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` for browser\nnavigation.\n\n## Public-route smoke\n\nUse the app-owned smoke command when you need proof that the standalone Bun\nprocess serves the current public API contract:\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api smoke:public-routes\n```\n\nThe command starts `apps/api` at `http://127.0.0.1:4173` by default, waits for\n`GET /api/health`, calls the public calculator metadata route, posts a\ntake-home-pay calculation and checks the generated OpenAPI document. It then\ncreates a temp consumer workspace outside the repo, writes a dependency-free\n`fetch` consumer and runs that consumer from the temp workspace against the\nsame public HTTP routes:\n\n- `GET /api/health`\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators`\n- `POST /api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate`\n- `POST /api/v1/calculators/au.income-tax.annual/calculate`\n- `GET /api/docs/openapi.json`\n\nThe smoke script owns process lifecycle only. It validates response bodies with\nschemas exported by `@taxkit/api-http` where those schemas are public, and it\nlets the app process stop through Effect-scoped child process cleanup on\nsuccess or failure. The external consumer checks minimal public JSON evidence;\ncanonical route schema validation stays in this repo-owned smoke script. The\ntemp workspace is removed on success and failure. Failed cleanup also fails\nthe command and remains alongside an earlier command failure.\n\nWhen the default loopback port is occupied, set `TAXKIT_API_SMOKE_PORT` to an\navailable port. The isolated release-boundary harness uses this override so a\nneighbouring local development server cannot change its failure oracle.\n\nThe smoke command uses checked Config settings and arguments, named HTTP\noperations and the exported `HealthResponse`, catalog and calculation Schemas.\nThe OpenAPI check requires its calculate path before running the plain external\nconsumer. Health readiness has a 15-second total limit, including retries and\nresponse-body reading; other requests have a five-second limit. The external\nconsumer has a 30-second limit and a 1 MiB stdout limit. Its stderr is drained\nwithout retention. Successful stdout is decoded into the exact expected route\ncoverage; failures report their bounded reason and available exit code.\nCancellation stops both child processes and removes the workspace. The external\nconsumer deliberately uses ordinary JavaScript `fetch` and JSON to check a\ncaller outside the repository.\n\n`check-types` covers source, scripts, test fixtures and test configuration.\n`test` runs native Effect fixtures for settings, stalled headers/bodies,\ninvalid responses, child-process faults, cancellation and cleanup. All API\nsource and test paths receive the canonical strict rules, with execution\nadmitted only at the two existing app/command entrypoints.\n\nUse the failure simulation when you need deterministic cleanup evidence for a\ndownstream consumer failure:\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api smoke:public-routes -- --simulate-downstream-failure\n```\n\nThe simulation exits nonzero after the external consumer has covered the\npublic routes, then removes the temp workspace and stops the API process.\n\nUse the portless URL for local API smoke checks:\n\n```sh\ncurl https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/health\ncurl https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/v1/calculators\ncurl -X POST https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"facts\":{\"grossPay\":{\"_tag\":\"GrossPay\",\"amount\":{\"_tag\":\"Money\",\"cents\":150000,\"currency\":\"AUD\"},\"period\":\"weekly\"},\"taxFreeThresholdClaimed\":true}}'\n```\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Do not define API contracts in this app.\n- Keep app-owned schemas in `schemas.ts` and derive exported types from those\n  schemas. Runtime files should consume canonical schema values and compose\n  layers/startup logic, not redefine reusable shapes inline.\n- Do not manually wire process signal handlers, `process.exit`, mutable\n  shutdown flags or `try/catch` around Effect startup. The process entrypoint\n  should be an Effect program run through `BunRuntime.runMain`.\n- Do not create a runtime inside request handling.\n- Keep process-owned resources in `ApiAppLayer` so root fiber interruption\n  releases them through scoped finalizers.\n- Keep `apps/web` as an HTTP client of this app, not an in-process API mount.\n\n## Related Docs\n\n- `docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`\n- `docs/architecture/effect-services.md`\n- `docs/architecture/package-ownership.md`\n- `docs/product-specs/extract-api-app.md`\n---\nstatus: canonical\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-05\nsource_of_truth: package-readme\nconfidence: high\n---\n\n# Web App\n\nCurrent TanStack Start scaffold for TaxKit.\n\n## Scope\n\n`apps/web` proves the current browser/server runtime split and calls the\nstandalone Effect HTTP API service owned by `apps/api`. It is not the\nlong-term calculation engine and should not own tax-domain contracts or API\nrequest handling.\n\n## Main Areas\n\n- `src/routes/`: TanStack Router routes\n- `src/lib/runtime.server.ts`: server `ManagedRuntime`\n- `src/lib/runtime.client.ts`: client `ManagedRuntime`\n- `src/lib/route-context.ts`: route runtime contract and context selection\n- `src/lib/runtime-selection.ts`: isomorphic selection of the server/client runtime\n- `src/server.ts`: server entrypoint\n\n## Runtime Shape\n\nThe root route loads `@taxkit/api-http/client` through the route runtime and\nrenders API health status from the standalone API service over HTTP.\nServer-only API exports must stay out of browser code. The root loader uses\nthe native runtime contract and passes the Router abort signal to its existing\nHTTP operation. It returns readonly health fields without a hand-written\nPromise interface or a one-use runtime wrapper.\n\nThe web runtime reads the API origin from:\n\n- `TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` on the server\n- `VITE_TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` in the browser\n\nBoth are required runtime config values and are validated with the HTTP\npackage's Effect Config and URL Schema. The exact Vite host reads only the\npublic browser input using Vite's normal file/environment precedence, then\nSchema-encodes it into a typed build constant. Automatic public-prefix\nexposure is disabled; Vite still supplies its standard mode/SSR metadata.\nBrowser modules do not read\n`import.meta.env`. Missing or invalid raw URLs still fail at runtime; the build\ndoes not guess a URL or change that validation timing. Settings failures expose\nonly the client/server identity, settings operation and fixed safe message.\n`bun run --filter=web dev` injects both from\n`portless get api.taxkit`. Do not include `/api` in the base URL; the typed\nAPI client owns route prefixes.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Keep tax rules, facts and calculators in engine packages.\n- Use browser-safe API client exports from routes.\n- Do not import `@taxkit/api-http/server` from browser code.\n- Keep route data acquisition and trust-boundary conversion route-high. Render\n  the page shell and semantic landmarks before passing focused readonly values\n  and callbacks to leaves.\n- Keep local UI commands in leaves; keep remote or domain commands in the route\n  action or nearest policy-owning container.\n- Put loading, empty and recoverable error UI at the smallest owning boundary\n  while preserving a stable footprint and the surrounding page shell.\n- Keep the app README local; route durable architecture to `docs/architecture`.\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\nbun run --filter=api dev\nbun run --filter=web dev\nbun run --filter=web check-types\nbun run --filter=web test\nbun run --filter=web test:browser\nbun run --filter=web build\n```\n\nRun `apps/api` before loading the web root locally. Without the API process,\nthe root route should fail with an attributable HTTP transport error rather\nthan silently falling back to an in-process API.\n\nUse the portless URLs for local browser and app-to-app checks:\n\n- API: `https://api.taxkit.localhost`\n- Web: `https://taxkit.localhost`\n\n## Related Docs\n\n- `docs/architecture/frontend.md`\n- `docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`\n- `docs/architecture/deployment.md`\n- `docs/design-docs/abstraction-admission.md`\n\n## Atom compatibility proof\n\n`bun run web:test:browser` builds the web app and runs the Chromium qualification\nin `src/lib/atom-lifecycle.browser.test.tsx`. It is part of root `verification`.\nThe fixture uses Effect test scopes to dispose React roots on failure and proves\nSSR hydration without errors, one registry through StrictMode effect remount,\n50 rapid updates, scheduled/cancelled work and final resource disposal. It does\nnot yet replace the app's existing runtime or qualify RPC cancellation.\n\nThe exact candidate is Atom 4.0.0, React/React DOM 19.3.0 and Scheduler 0.28.0.\nThe root patch changes only Atom's Scheduler peer range to admit exactly 0.28.0;\nremove it when upstream metadata admits that version. One Scheduler version is\npresent in the lockfile. Bun resolves peers from registry metadata before patching\nand may still print the original peer warning; the installed manifest and runtime\nfixture are the qualified correction. Atom/Scheduler are development dependencies\nuntil the application migration adopts their runtime owner.\n\nThe browser test config extends Vite's browser conditions with `source`; replacing\nthe defaults with only `source` selects the Node renderer and is not a valid\nbrowser hydration test. The test imports the actual browser renderer and waits\nfor hydration before issuing updates.\n\n## Strict and route proof\n\nCanonical strict rules cover source, tests and all Vite/Vitest configuration.\nOnly the two existing runtime composition modules, root loader, Vite host and\nfake browser-test runtime have exact execution permissions. They retain all\nother rules; no async workflow or raw settings exception is admitted. The\ncompiler and development Knip graph include both test configurations and Vite.\nThe package test command uses Bun-hosted Vitest and native Effect tests.\n\nSettings tests cover valid, missing and invalid server/browser inputs, exact\nsecret-negative error bytes, public build-input selection and absent compiled\nbrowser settings. The real file-route Chromium tests call the actual generated\nHTTP client through a fake HTTP transport. They prove health decoding and\ninterruption of pending HTTP work when the Router retires its preload. The\nHTTP abort signal is observed as aborted. This proves the tested preload\nretirement, not all navigation/unmount paths or remote provider cancellation.\nBoth retained Atom/Scheduler cases still run. Browser dependencies are listed\nfor optimisation so Vite does not reload tests while they start.\nimport {\n  declareDocsStack,\n  docsCloudflareStackName,\n} from \"@taxkit/infrastructure/stack\";\nimport { decodeDocsCloudflareStackStage } from \"@taxkit/infrastructure/website\";\nimport * as Alchemy from \"alchemy\";\nimport * as Cloudflare from \"alchemy/Cloudflare\";\nimport { Stack } from \"alchemy/Stack\";\nimport { Stage } from \"alchemy/Stage\";\nimport * as Effect from \"effect/Effect\";\n\nexport default Alchemy.Stack(\n  docsCloudflareStackName,\n  {\n    providers: Cloudflare.providers(),\n    state: Cloudflare.state(),\n  },\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\n    const stack = yield* Stack;\n    const stage = yield* Stage.pipe(\n      Effect.flatMap(decodeDocsCloudflareStackStage)\n    );\n    return yield* declareDocsStack({ stackName: stack.name, stage });\n  })\n);\nimport * as Cloudflare from \"alchemy/Cloudflare\";\nimport * as Array from \"effect/Array\";\nimport * as Effect from \"effect/Effect\";\n\nimport {\n  docsWorkerAssetHeaders,\n  docsWorkerCompatibilityDate,\n  docsWorkerCompatibilityFlags,\n  docsWorkerMemo,\n  docsWorkerObservability,\n  docsWorkerResourceId,\n} from \"./cloudflare/website.js\";\nimport type { DocsCloudflareStackStage } from \"./cloudflare/website.js\";\n\nexport { docsCloudflareStackName } from \"./cloudflare/website.js\";\n\nexport const declareDocsStack = ({\n  stackName,\n  stage,\n}: {\n  readonly stackName: string;\n  readonly stage: DocsCloudflareStackStage;\n}) =>\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\n    const worker = yield* Cloudflare.Website.Vite(docsWorkerResourceId, {\n      assets: {\n        // Website.Vite does not infer the app-owned _headers file when its\n        // config is passed through Alchemy.\n        headers: docsWorkerAssetHeaders,\n        runWorkerFirst: false,\n      },\n      compatibility: {\n        date: docsWorkerCompatibilityDate,\n        flags: [...docsWorkerCompatibilityFlags],\n      },\n      // Alchemy's input requires mutable arrays; give it fresh boundary copies.\n      memo: {\n        ...docsWorkerMemo,\n        include: Array.fromIterable(docsWorkerMemo.include),\n        workspaces: Array.map(docsWorkerMemo.workspaces, (workspace) => ({\n          ...workspace,\n          include: Array.fromIterable(workspace.include),\n        })),\n      },\n      observability: docsWorkerObservability,\n      rootDir: \"apps/docs\",\n      workersDev: true,\n    });\n\n    return {\n      logicalResourceId: docsWorkerResourceId,\n      stackName,\n      stage,\n      workerName: worker.workerName,\n      workerUrl: worker.url,\n    };\n  });\npackages/infrastructure/src/stack.ts\napps/api/src/server.ts\napps/api/src/config.ts\napps/api/src/index.ts\napps/api/src/schemas.ts\napps/api/vitest.config.ts\napps/api/tsconfig.json\npackages/infrastructure/src/cloudflare/website.test.ts\npackages/infrastructure/src/cloudflare/website.ts\npackages/infrastructure/src/stage.ts\napps/web/vitest.config.ts\napps/web/vite.config.ts\napps/web/tsconfig.json\napps/web/package.json\napps/web/README.md\napps/web/vitest.browser.config.ts\napps/web/src/routeTree.gen.ts\napps/web/src/router.tsx\napps/web/src/styles.css\napps/api/scripts/schemas.ts\napps/api/scripts/smoke-public-routes.runtime.ts\napps/api/scripts/routes.ts\napps/api/scripts/smoke-boundaries.test.ts\napps/api/tsconfig.scripts.json\napps/api/package.json\napps/api/README.md\napps/api/tsconfig.tests.json\napps/api/CHANGELOG.md\napps/web/src/routes/__root.tsx\napps/web/src/routes/index.tsx\napps/web/src/server.ts\napps/web/src/lib/config.client-input.ts\napps/web/src/lib/runtime.client.ts\napps/web/src/lib/atom-lifecycle.browser.test.tsx\napps/web/src/lib/runtime-selection.ts\napps/web/src/lib/runtime.server.ts\napps/web/src/lib/config.boundary.test.ts\napps/web/src/lib/health-loader.boundary.browser.test.tsx\napps/web/src/lib/config.ts\napps/web/src/lib/config.server.ts\napps/web/src/lib/route-context.ts\napps/web/src/lib/config.client.ts\napps/api/test/config.test.ts\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow-evidence.test.ts (11 tests) 108ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/strict-boundaries.contract.test.ts (40 tests) 55ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/policy.test.ts (20 tests) 25ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow-artifact.test.ts (11 tests) 25ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/alchemy-memo.test.ts (1 test) 24ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/doppler-custody.test.ts (9 tests) 21ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow-plan-projection.test.ts (15 tests) 20ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/automation.check.runtime.test.ts (5 tests) 20ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow.contract.test.ts (18 tests) 19ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/automation.policy.test.ts (8 tests) 18ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/inventory-credentials.boundary.test.ts (10 tests) 16ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/input.boundary.test.ts (9 tests) 15ms\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":6375},"formatted_output":"      \"id\": \"CSF-T003\",\n      \"title\": \"Prove one native API and Website path\",\n      \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-003\",\n        \"CSF-004\",\n        \"CSF-007\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T002\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Rebuild apps/api as a native Alchemy Worker and apps/web as a standard TanStack Website using one real existing calculator.\",\n        \"Implement the Q9-agreed native Effect RPC in packages/api/rpc with shared calculator/content Schemas, thin handlers and private generated client Layers. Use native JSON serialisation and explicitly select HTTP POST rather than the native server WebSocket default. Keep the public HTTP adapter separate and call the same named application operation.\",\n        \"Qualify checked semantic client errors, malformed-reply handling, safe RPC expected/defect/protocol replies, contract version agreement, credential/redirect/origin policy, one whole-response deadline and earlier caller interruption. Recheck every native fatal/global defect path and unknown-tag/invalid-envelope bypass as well as per-procedure encoding; an outer HTTP reporter, custom procedure defect Schema or codecFor hook alone is insufficient privacy proof. Qualify supported ingress treatment or an exact reviewed native correction where required.\",\n        \"Use native instance/request lifetimes, matching-stage service binding/public address, one Website server runner and a React-owned browser Atom graph; no extra backend runner or Effect Context through TanStack. Bind each host's own origin from native Cloudflare.Worker.URL and cross-host addresses from native resource Outputs, decoded once at application ingress. Missing Outputs fail checked configuration without guessed or concatenated addresses.\",\n        \"Select native Stack.secrets/Doppler at the infrastructure root with explicit stage/precedence; qualify bindings without applying a cloud plan.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"apps/api/src/**, apps/web/src/**, packages/api/rpc/**, packages/api/http/src/** and packages/infrastructure/src/** native composition\",\n        \"alchemy.run.ts and exact stage/secret configuration owners\",\n        \"apps/api/README.md, apps/web/README.md, packages/api/rpc/README.md, packages/api/http/README.md, packages/infrastructure/README.md and affected architecture\",\n        \"Focused client/Worker/lifetime tests and a local two-app receipt\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/api-http test\",\n        \"bun run api:smoke\",\n        \"bun run check-types\",\n        \"bun run build\",\n        \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Exercise initial render and client navigation against the matching local API.\",\n        \"Check actual post-initialisation Worker startup, browser CORS, full response decoding, slow headers/stalled bodies, abort, route change and unmount.\",\n        \"Inspect the production browser bundle for server/Alchemy/provider credentials or live domain implementations.\",\n        \"Use the actual generated RPC client and native POST/JSON server through browser URL and private server binding. Prove expected error/hydration round-trip, bad valid-JSON reply, unrelated adapter defect, version skew, malformed envelopes/unknown tags/invalid IDs, sensitive sentinels in all native reply/log/trace paths, and abort during complete body decoding.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n        \"No package/app domain code constructs a runtime or builds a live Layer mid-operation.\",\n        \"The same-stage origin/binding and deadline/cancellation claims have runtime evidence.\",\n        \"Website RPC, HTTP and later MCP reuse one checked application operation. Native RPC wire privacy and failure classification have source/version-matched proof, not assumed defaults or handwritten protocol framing.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-rpc-contract.json\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CSF-T004\",\n      \"title\": \"Finish calculator pages and the fresh package interface\",\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n---\ndocument_type: app-readme\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: taxkit-api-app-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-04\nreview_trigger: API app settings, startup, smoke command or shutdown change\n---\n\n# API App\n\nStandalone Bun process for the TaxKit Effect HTTP API.\n\n## Scope\n\n`apps/api` owns process config, Bun server startup, request dispatch to\n`@taxkit/api-http/server` and graceful shutdown. API contracts, handlers,\nschemas, generated OpenAPI and docs routes stay in `packages/api/http`.\n\n## Runtime Shape\n\nThe process entrypoint is an Effect program run with\n`@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain`. Startup reads `ApiServerConfig` from\n`ApiAppLayer`, requests are served by the Bun-backed `HttpServer` layer, and\n`SIGINT` or `SIGTERM` interrupts the root Effect fiber so scoped finalizers stop\nthe Bun server.\n\nLocal defaults:\n\n- host: `127.0.0.1`\n- port: `4000`\n\nEnvironment overrides:\n\n- `API_HOST`\n- `API_PORT`\n- `PORT` as the fallback port supplied by portless\n\n`API_PORT` takes priority. A present, invalid value fails startup rather than\nusing `PORT`; missing values use the fallback and then port 4000. Ports must\nbe whole numbers from 1 to 65535. Host names are trimmed and blank host values\nuse the default. Settings use the caller's Effect ConfigProvider; the live app\nuses the environment and tests supply isolated providers. The safe\n`ApiServerConfigError` does not include the rejected value.\n\n## Routes\n\n- `GET /api/health`\n- `GET /api/docs`\n- `GET /api/docs/openapi.json`\n- `GET /api/v1/jurisdictions`\n- `GET /api/v1/tax-years`\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators`\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId`\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId/schema`\n- `POST /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId/calculate`\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId/graph`\n- `GET /api/v1/facts`\n- `GET /api/v1/rules`\n\nPublic calculation routes are calculator, fact, rule and graph driven.\nJurisdiction and tax year are calculator context, not top-level route families.\nThe initial calculator IDs are `au.pay.take-home`, `au.pay.withholdings` and\n`au.income-tax.annual`.\n\nCalculate payloads use canonical schema values from the rule packages. The\ngenerated OpenAPI request body shows supported fact shapes under `facts.anyOf`;\nfor example, take-home-pay JSON includes tagged `GrossPay` and `Money` values.\nThe calculator service validates facts again against the selected calculator,\nso annual-tax facts sent to `au.pay.take-home` return pay-calculator input help\ninstead of being treated as a valid take-home request.\n\n## Changelog\n\nPublic API contract and deployment-facing changes are tracked in\n[CHANGELOG.md](./CHANGELOG.md). Package-level API contract changes are also\ntracked in [`@taxkit/api-http`](../../packages/api/http/CHANGELOG.md) through\nChangesets.\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api dev\nbun run --filter=api start\nbun run --filter=api smoke:public-routes\nbun run --filter=api check-types\nbun run --filter=api test\nbun run --filter=api build\nbun run --filter=api clean\n```\n\nFor local UI development, run the API and web app in separate terminals:\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api dev\nbun run --filter=web dev\n```\n\n`bun run --filter=api dev` serves this app through portless at\n`https://api.taxkit.localhost`. `bun run --filter=web dev` injects that URL\ninto `TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` for SSR and `VITE_TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` for browser\nnavigation.\n\n## Public-route smoke\n\nUse the app-owned smoke command when you need proof that the standalone Bun\nprocess serves the current public API contract:\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api smoke:public-routes\n```\n\nThe command starts `apps/api` at `http://127.0.0.1:4173` by default, waits for\n`GET /api/health`, calls the public calculator metadata route, posts a\ntake-home-pay calculation and checks the generated OpenAPI document. It then\ncreates a temp consumer workspace outside the repo, writes a dependency-free\n`fetch` consumer and runs that consumer from the temp workspace against the\nsame public HTTP routes:\n\n- `GET /api/health`\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators`\n- `POST /api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate`\n- `POST /api/v1/calculators/au.income-tax.annual/calculate`\n- `GET /api/docs/openapi.json`\n\nThe smoke script owns process lifecycle only. It validates response bodies with\nschemas exported by `@taxkit/api-http` where those schemas are public, and it\nlets the app process stop through Effect-scoped child process cleanup on\nsuccess or failure. The external consumer checks minimal public JSON evidence;\ncanonical route schema validation stays in this repo-owned smoke script. The\ntemp workspace is removed on success and failure. Failed cleanup also fails\nthe command and remains alongside an earlier command failure.\n\nWhen the default loopback port is occupied, set `TAXKIT_API_SMOKE_PORT` to an\navailable port. The isolated release-boundary harness uses this override so a\nneighbouring local development server cannot change its failure oracle.\n\nThe smoke command uses checked Config settings and arguments, named HTTP\noperations and the exported `HealthResponse`, catalog and calculation Schemas.\nThe OpenAPI check requires its calculate path before running the plain external\nconsumer. Health readiness has a 15-second total limit, including retries and\nresponse-body reading; other requests have a five-second limit. The external\nconsumer has a 30-second limit and a 1 MiB stdout limit. Its stderr is drained\nwithout retention. Successful stdout is decoded into the exact expected route\ncoverage; failures report their bounded reason and available exit code.\nCancellation stops both child processes and removes the workspace. The external\nconsumer deliberately uses ordinary JavaScript `fetch` and JSON to check a\ncaller outside the repository.\n\n`check-types` covers source, scripts, test fixtures and test configuration.\n`test` runs native Effect fixtures for settings, stalled headers/bodies,\ninvalid responses, child-process faults, cancellation and cleanup. All API\nsource and test paths receive the canonical strict rules, with execution\nadmitted only at the two existing app/command entrypoints.\n\nUse the failure simulation when you need deterministic cleanup evidence for a\ndownstream consumer failure:\n\n```sh\nbun run --filter=api smoke:public-routes -- --simulate-downstream-failure\n```\n\nThe simulation exits nonzero after the external consumer has covered the\npublic routes, then removes the temp workspace and stops the API process.\n\nUse the portless URL for local API smoke checks:\n\n```sh\ncurl https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/health\ncurl https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/v1/calculators\ncurl -X POST https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"facts\":{\"grossPay\":{\"_tag\":\"GrossPay\",\"amount\":{\"_tag\":\"Money\",\"cents\":150000,\"currency\":\"AUD\"},\"period\":\"weekly\"},\"taxFreeThresholdClaimed\":true}}'\n```\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Do not define API contracts in this app.\n- Keep app-owned schemas in `schemas.ts` and derive exported types from those\n  schemas. Runtime files should consume canonical schema values and compose\n  layers/startup logic, not redefine reusable shapes inline.\n- Do not manually wire process signal handlers, `process.exit`, mutable\n  shutdown flags or `try/catch` around Effect startup. The process entrypoint\n  should be an Effect program run through `BunRuntime.runMain`.\n- Do not create a runtime inside request handling.\n- Keep process-owned resources in `ApiAppLayer` so root fiber interruption\n  releases them through scoped finalizers.\n- Keep `apps/web` as an HTTP client of this app, not an in-process API mount.\n\n## Related Docs\n\n- `docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`\n- `docs/architecture/effect-services.md`\n- `docs/architecture/package-ownership.md`\n- `docs/product-specs/extract-api-app.md`\n---\nstatus: canonical\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-05\nsource_of_truth: package-readme\nconfidence: high\n---\n\n# Web App\n\nCurrent TanStack Start scaffold for TaxKit.\n\n## Scope\n\n`apps/web` proves the current browser/server runtime split and calls the\nstandalone Effect HTTP API service owned by `apps/api`. It is not the\nlong-term calculation engine and should not own tax-domain contracts or API\nrequest handling.\n\n## Main Areas\n\n- `src/routes/`: TanStack Router routes\n- `src/lib/runtime.server.ts`: server `ManagedRuntime`\n- `src/lib/runtime.client.ts`: client `ManagedRuntime`\n- `src/lib/route-context.ts`: route runtime contract and context selection\n- `src/lib/runtime-selection.ts`: isomorphic selection of the server/client runtime\n- `src/server.ts`: server entrypoint\n\n## Runtime Shape\n\nThe root route loads `@taxkit/api-http/client` through the route runtime and\nrenders API health status from the standalone API service over HTTP.\nServer-only API exports must stay out of browser code. The root loader uses\nthe native runtime contract and passes the Router abort signal to its existing\nHTTP operation. It returns readonly health fields without a hand-written\nPromise interface or a one-use runtime wrapper.\n\nThe web runtime reads the API origin from:\n\n- `TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` on the server\n- `VITE_TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` in the browser\n\nBoth are required runtime config values and are validated with the HTTP\npackage's Effect Config and URL Schema. The exact Vite host reads only the\npublic browser input using Vite's normal file/environment precedence, then\nSchema-encodes it into a typed build constant. Automatic public-prefix\nexposure is disabled; Vite still supplies its standard mode/SSR metadata.\nBrowser modules do not read\n`import.meta.env`. Missing or invalid raw URLs still fail at runtime; the build\ndoes not guess a URL or change that validation timing. Settings failures expose\nonly the client/server identity, settings operation and fixed safe message.\n`bun run --filter=web dev` injects both from\n`portless get api.taxkit`. Do not include `/api` in the base URL; the typed\nAPI client owns route prefixes.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Keep tax rules, facts and calculators in engine packages.\n- Use browser-safe API client exports from routes.\n- Do not import `@taxkit/api-http/server` from browser code.\n- Keep route data acquisition and trust-boundary conversion route-high. Render\n  the page shell and semantic landmarks before passing focused readonly values\n  and callbacks to leaves.\n- Keep local UI commands in leaves; keep remote or domain commands in the route\n  action or nearest policy-owning container.\n- Put loading, empty and recoverable error UI at the smallest owning boundary\n  while preserving a stable footprint and the surrounding page shell.\n- Keep the app README local; route durable architecture to `docs/architecture`.\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\nbun run --filter=api dev\nbun run --filter=web dev\nbun run --filter=web check-types\nbun run --filter=web test\nbun run --filter=web test:browser\nbun run --filter=web build\n```\n\nRun `apps/api` before loading the web root locally. Without the API process,\nthe root route should fail with an attributable HTTP transport error rather\nthan silently falling back to an in-process API.\n\nUse the portless URLs for local browser and app-to-app checks:\n\n- API: `https://api.taxkit.localhost`\n- Web: `https://taxkit.localhost`\n\n## Related Docs\n\n- `docs/architecture/frontend.md`\n- `docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`\n- `docs/architecture/deployment.md`\n- `docs/design-docs/abstraction-admission.md`\n\n## Atom compatibility proof\n\n`bun run web:test:browser` builds the web app and runs the Chromium qualification\nin `src/lib/atom-lifecycle.browser.test.tsx`. It is part of root `verification`.\nThe fixture uses Effect test scopes to dispose React roots on failure and proves\nSSR hydration without errors, one registry through StrictMode effect remount,\n50 rapid updates, scheduled/cancelled work and final resource disposal. It does\nnot yet replace the app's existing runtime or qualify RPC cancellation.\n\nThe exact candidate is Atom 4.0.0, React/React DOM 19.3.0 and Scheduler 0.28.0.\nThe root patch changes only Atom's Scheduler peer range to admit exactly 0.28.0;\nremove it when upstream metadata admits that version. One Scheduler version is\npresent in the lockfile. Bun resolves peers from registry metadata before patching\nand may still print the original peer warning; the installed manifest and runtime\nfixture are the qualified correction. Atom/Scheduler are development dependencies\nuntil the application migration adopts their runtime owner.\n\nThe browser test config extends Vite's browser conditions with `source`; replacing\nthe defaults with only `source` selects the Node renderer and is not a valid\nbrowser hydration test. The test imports the actual browser renderer and waits\nfor hydration before issuing updates.\n\n## Strict and route proof\n\nCanonical strict rules cover source, tests and all Vite/Vitest configuration.\nOnly the two existing runtime composition modules, root loader, Vite host and\nfake browser-test runtime have exact execution permissions. They retain all\nother rules; no async workflow or raw settings exception is admitted. The\ncompiler and development Knip graph include both test configurations and Vite.\nThe package test command uses Bun-hosted Vitest and native Effect tests.\n\nSettings tests cover valid, missing and invalid server/browser inputs, exact\nsecret-negative error bytes, public build-input selection and absent compiled\nbrowser settings. The real file-route Chromium tests call the actual generated\nHTTP client through a fake HTTP transport. They prove health decoding and\ninterruption of pending HTTP work when the Router retires its preload. The\nHTTP abort signal is observed as aborted. This proves the tested preload\nretirement, not all navigation/unmount paths or remote provider cancellation.\nBoth retained Atom/Scheduler cases still run. Browser dependencies are listed\nfor optimisation so Vite does not reload tests while they start.\nimport {\n  declareDocsStack,\n  docsCloudflareStackName,\n} from \"@taxkit/infrastructure/stack\";\nimport { decodeDocsCloudflareStackStage } from \"@taxkit/infrastructure/website\";\nimport * as Alchemy from \"alchemy\";\nimport * as Cloudflare from \"alchemy/Cloudflare\";\nimport { Stack } from \"alchemy/Stack\";\nimport { Stage } from \"alchemy/Stage\";\nimport * as Effect from \"effect/Effect\";\n\nexport default Alchemy.Stack(\n  docsCloudflareStackName,\n  {\n    providers: Cloudflare.providers(),\n    state: Cloudflare.state(),\n  },\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\n    const stack = yield* Stack;\n    const stage = yield* Stage.pipe(\n      Effect.flatMap(decodeDocsCloudflareStackStage)\n    );\n    return yield* declareDocsStack({ stackName: stack.name, stage });\n  })\n);\nimport * as Cloudflare from \"alchemy/Cloudflare\";\nimport * as Array from \"effect/Array\";\nimport * as Effect from \"effect/Effect\";\n\nimport {\n  docsWorkerAssetHeaders,\n  docsWorkerCompatibilityDate,\n  docsWorkerCompatibilityFlags,\n  docsWorkerMemo,\n  docsWorkerObservability,\n  docsWorkerResourceId,\n} from \"./cloudflare/website.js\";\nimport type { DocsCloudflareStackStage } from \"./cloudflare/website.js\";\n\nexport { docsCloudflareStackName } from \"./cloudflare/website.js\";\n\nexport const declareDocsStack = ({\n  stackName,\n  stage,\n}: {\n  readonly stackName: string;\n  readonly stage: DocsCloudflareStackStage;\n}) =>\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\n    const worker = yield* Cloudflare.Website.Vite(docsWorkerResourceId, {\n      assets: {\n        // Website.Vite does not infer the app-owned _headers file when its\n        // config is passed through Alchemy.\n        headers: docsWorkerAssetHeaders,\n        runWorkerFirst: false,\n      },\n      compatibility: {\n        date: docsWorkerCompatibilityDate,\n        flags: [...docsWorkerCompatibilityFlags],\n      },\n      // Alchemy's input requires mutable arrays; give it fresh boundary copies.\n      memo: {\n        ...docsWorkerMemo,\n        include: Array.fromIterable(docsWorkerMemo.include),\n        workspaces: Array.map(docsWorkerMemo.workspaces, (workspace) => ({\n          ...workspace,\n          include: Array.fromIterable(workspace.include),\n        })),\n      },\n      observability: docsWorkerObservability,\n      rootDir: \"apps/docs\",\n      workersDev: true,\n    });\n\n    return {\n      logicalResourceId: docsWorkerResourceId,\n      stackName,\n      stage,\n      workerName: worker.workerName,\n      workerUrl: worker.url,\n    };\n  });\npackages/infrastructure/src/stack.ts\napps/api/src/server.ts\napps/api/src/config.ts\napps/api/src/index.ts\napps/api/src/schemas.ts\napps/api/vitest.config.ts\napps/api/tsconfig.json\npackages/infrastructure/src/cloudflare/website.test.ts\npackages/infrastructure/src/cloudflare/website.ts\npackages/infrastructure/src/stage.ts\napps/web/vitest.config.ts\napps/web/vite.config.ts\napps/web/tsconfig.json\napps/web/package.json\napps/web/README.md\napps/web/vitest.browser.config.ts\napps/web/src/routeTree.gen.ts\napps/web/src/router.tsx\napps/web/src/styles.css\napps/api/scripts/schemas.ts\napps/api/scripts/smoke-public-routes.runtime.ts\napps/api/scripts/routes.ts\napps/api/scripts/smoke-boundaries.test.ts\napps/api/tsconfig.scripts.json\napps/api/package.json\napps/api/README.md\napps/api/tsconfig.tests.json\napps/api/CHANGELOG.md\napps/web/src/routes/__root.tsx\napps/web/src/routes/index.tsx\napps/web/src/server.ts\napps/web/src/lib/config.client-input.ts\napps/web/src/lib/runtime.client.ts\napps/web/src/lib/atom-lifecycle.browser.test.tsx\napps/web/src/lib/runtime-selection.ts\napps/web/src/lib/runtime.server.ts\napps/web/src/lib/config.boundary.test.ts\napps/web/src/lib/health-loader.boundary.browser.test.tsx\napps/web/src/lib/config.ts\napps/web/src/lib/config.server.ts\napps/web/src/lib/route-context.ts\napps/web/src/lib/config.client.ts\napps/api/test/config.test.ts\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow-evidence.test.ts (11 tests) 108ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/strict-boundaries.contract.test.ts (40 tests) 55ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/policy.test.ts (20 tests) 25ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow-artifact.test.ts (11 tests) 25ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/alchemy-memo.test.ts (1 test) 24ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/doppler-custody.test.ts (9 tests) 21ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow-plan-projection.test.ts (15 tests) 20ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/automation.check.runtime.test.ts (5 tests) 20ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow.contract.test.ts (18 tests) 19ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/automation.policy.test.ts (8 tests) 18ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/inventory-credentials.boundary.test.ts (10 tests) 16ms\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/input.boundary.test.ts (9 tests) 15ms\n"},"started_at_ms":1791131880289,"completed_at_ms":1791131880289}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T16:38:00.342Z","ordinal":15021,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a107c7-8b96-7590-abc6-9816ba710e57","call_id":"call_aq1NjL0XKKIfxP7hYbXAztCb","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"3a9d8a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000006375,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":6417,\"output\":\"      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CSF-T003\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Prove one native API and Website path\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"in_progress\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"vertical-slice\\\",\\n      \\\"acceptedFindingIds\\\": [],\\n      \\\"requirementIds\\\": [\\n        \\\"CSF-003\\\",\\n        \\\"CSF-004\\\",\\n        \\\"CSF-007\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"dependsOn\\\": [\\n        \\\"CSF-T002\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"goal\\\": \\\"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\\\",\\n      \\\"scope\\\": [\\n        \\\"Rebuild apps/api as a native Alchemy Worker and apps/web as a standard TanStack Website using one real existing calculator.\\\",\\n        \\\"Implement the Q9-agreed native Effect RPC in packages/api/rpc with shared calculator/content Schemas, thin handlers and private generated client Layers. Use native JSON serialisation and explicitly select HTTP POST rather than the native server WebSocket default. Keep the public HTTP adapter separate and call the same named application operation.\\\",\\n        \\\"Qualify checked semantic client errors, malformed-reply handling, safe RPC expected/defect/protocol replies, contract version agreement, credential/redirect/origin policy, one whole-response deadline and earlier caller interruption. Recheck every native fatal/global defect path and unknown-tag/invalid-envelope bypass as well as per-procedure encoding; an outer HTTP reporter, custom procedure defect Schema or codecFor hook alone is insufficient privacy proof. Qualify supported ingress treatment or an exact reviewed native correction where required.\\\",\\n        \\\"Use native instance/request lifetimes, matching-stage service binding/public address, one Website server runner and a React-owned browser Atom graph; no extra backend runner or Effect Context through TanStack. Bind each host's own origin from native Cloudflare.Worker.URL and cross-host addresses from native resource Outputs, decoded once at application ingress. Missing Outputs fail checked configuration without guessed or concatenated addresses.\\\",\\n        \\\"Select native Stack.secrets/Doppler at the infrastructure root with explicit stage/precedence; qualify bindings without applying a cloud plan.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"outputs\\\": [\\n        \\\"apps/api/src/**, apps/web/src/**, packages/api/rpc/**, packages/api/http/src/** and packages/infrastructure/src/** native composition\\\",\\n        \\\"alchemy.run.ts and exact stage/secret configuration owners\\\",\\n        \\\"apps/api/README.md, apps/web/README.md, packages/api/rpc/README.md, packages/api/http/README.md, packages/infrastructure/README.md and affected architecture\\\",\\n        \\\"Focused client/Worker/lifetime tests and a local two-app receipt\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"implementationPrompt\\\": \\\"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\\\",\\n      \\\"mandatoryVerification\\\": [\\n        \\\"bun run --filter=@taxkit/api-http test\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run api:smoke\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run check-types\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run build\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run test:oxlint\\\",\\n        \\\"bun run verification\\\",\\n        \\\"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"browserVerification\\\": [\\n        \\\"Exercise initial render and client navigation against the matching local API.\\\",\\n        \\\"Check actual post-initialisation Worker startup, browser CORS, full response decoding, slow headers/stalled bodies, abort, route change and unmount.\\\",\\n        \\\"Inspect the production browser bundle for server/Alchemy/provider credentials or live domain implementations.\\\",\\n        \\\"Use the actual generated RPC client and native POST/JSON server through browser URL and private server binding. Prove expected error/hydration round-trip, bad valid-JSON reply, unrelated adapter defect, version skew, malformed envelopes/unknown tags/invalid IDs, sensitive sentinels in all native reply/log/trace paths, and abort during complete body decoding.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"qualityAudits\\\": [\\n        \\\"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\\\",\\n        \\\"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\\\",\\n        \\\"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\\\",\\n        \\\"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"parentAudit\\\": {\\n        \\\"required\\\": true,\\n        \\\"basis\\\": \\\"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\\\",\\n        \\\"recovery\\\": \\\"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"completionCriteria\\\": [\\n        \\\"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\\\",\\n        \\\"No package/app domain code constructs a runtime or builds a live Layer mid-operation.\\\",\\n        \\\"The same-stage origin/binding and deadline/cancellation claims have runtime evidence.\\\",\\n        \\\"Website RPC, HTTP and later MCP reuse one checked application operation. Native RPC wire privacy and failure classification have source/version-matched proof, not assumed defaults or handwritten protocol framing.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"commitAfterPassing\\\": true,\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": [\\n        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-rpc-contract.json\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CSF-T004\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Finish calculator pages and the fresh package interface\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"vertical-slice\\\",\\n      \\\"acceptedFindingIds\\\": [],\\n      \\\"requirementIds\\\": [\\n---\\ndocument_type: app-readme\\nlifecycle: current\\nauthority: canonical\\nowner: taxkit-api-app-owner\\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-04\\nreview_trigger: API app settings, startup, smoke command or shutdown change\\n---\\n\\n# API App\\n\\nStandalone Bun process for the TaxKit Effect HTTP API.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n`apps/api` owns process config, Bun server startup, request dispatch to\\n`@taxkit/api-http/server` and graceful shutdown. API contracts, handlers,\\nschemas, generated OpenAPI and docs routes stay in `packages/api/http`.\\n\\n## Runtime Shape\\n\\nThe process entrypoint is an Effect program run with\\n`@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain`. Startup reads `ApiServerConfig` from\\n`ApiAppLayer`, requests are served by the Bun-backed `HttpServer` layer, and\\n`SIGINT` or `SIGTERM` interrupts the root Effect fiber so scoped finalizers stop\\nthe Bun server.\\n\\nLocal defaults:\\n\\n- host: `127.0.0.1`\\n- port: `4000`\\n\\nEnvironment overrides:\\n\\n- `API_HOST`\\n- `API_PORT`\\n- `PORT` as the fallback port supplied by portless\\n\\n`API_PORT` takes priority. A present, invalid value fails startup rather than\\nusing `PORT`; missing values use the fallback and then port 4000. Ports must\\nbe whole numbers from 1 to 65535. Host names are trimmed and blank host values\\nuse the default. Settings use the caller's Effect ConfigProvider; the live app\\nuses the environment and tests supply isolated providers. The safe\\n`ApiServerConfigError` does not include the rejected value.\\n\\n## Routes\\n\\n- `GET /api/health`\\n- `GET /api/docs`\\n- `GET /api/docs/openapi.json`\\n- `GET /api/v1/jurisdictions`\\n- `GET /api/v1/tax-years`\\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators`\\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId`\\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId/schema`\\n- `POST /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId/calculate`\\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId/graph`\\n- `GET /api/v1/facts`\\n- `GET /api/v1/rules`\\n\\nPublic calculation routes are calculator, fact, rule and graph driven.\\nJurisdiction and tax year are calculator context, not top-level route families.\\nThe initial calculator IDs are `au.pay.take-home`, `au.pay.withholdings` and\\n`au.income-tax.annual`.\\n\\nCalculate payloads use canonical schema values from the rule packages. The\\ngenerated OpenAPI request body shows supported fact shapes under `facts.anyOf`;\\nfor example, take-home-pay JSON includes tagged `GrossPay` and `Money` values.\\nThe calculator service validates facts again against the selected calculator,\\nso annual-tax facts sent to `au.pay.take-home` return pay-calculator input help\\ninstead of being treated as a valid take-home request.\\n\\n## Changelog\\n\\nPublic API contract and deployment-facing changes are tracked in\\n[CHANGELOG.md](./CHANGELOG.md). Package-level API contract changes are also\\ntracked in [`@taxkit/api-http`](../../packages/api/http/CHANGELOG.md) through\\nChangesets.\\n\\n## Commands\\n\\n```sh\\nbun run --filter=api dev\\nbun run --filter=api start\\nbun run --filter=api smoke:public-routes\\nbun run --filter=api check-types\\nbun run --filter=api test\\nbun run --filter=api build\\nbun run --filter=api clean\\n```\\n\\nFor local UI development, run the API and web app in separate terminals:\\n\\n```sh\\nbun run --filter=api dev\\nbun run --filter=web dev\\n```\\n\\n`bun run --filter=api dev` serves this app through portless at\\n`https://api.taxkit.localhost`. `bun run --filter=web dev` injects that URL\\ninto `TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` for SSR and `VITE_TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` for browser\\nnavigation.\\n\\n## Public-route smoke\\n\\nUse the app-owned smoke command when you need proof that the standalone Bun\\nprocess serves the current public API contract:\\n\\n```sh\\nbun run --filter=api smoke:public-routes\\n```\\n\\nThe command starts `apps/api` at `http://127.0.0.1:4173` by default, waits for\\n`GET /api/health`, calls the public calculator metadata route, posts a\\ntake-home-pay calculation and checks the generated OpenAPI document. It then\\ncreates a temp consumer workspace outside the repo, writes a dependency-free\\n`fetch` consumer and runs that consumer from the temp workspace against the\\nsame public HTTP routes:\\n\\n- `GET /api/health`\\n- `GET /api/v1/calculators`\\n- `POST /api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate`\\n- `POST /api/v1/calculators/au.income-tax.annual/calculate`\\n- `GET /api/docs/openapi.json`\\n\\nThe smoke script owns process lifecycle only. It validates response bodies with\\nschemas exported by `@taxkit/api-http` where those schemas are public, and it\\nlets the app process stop through Effect-scoped child process cleanup on\\nsuccess or failure. The external consumer checks minimal public JSON evidence;\\ncanonical route schema validation stays in this repo-owned smoke script. The\\ntemp workspace is removed on success and failure. Failed cleanup also fails\\nthe command and remains alongside an earlier command failure.\\n\\nWhen the default loopback port is occupied, set `TAXKIT_API_SMOKE_PORT` to an\\navailable port. The isolated release-boundary harness uses this override so a\\nneighbouring local development server cannot change its failure oracle.\\n\\nThe smoke command uses checked Config settings and arguments, named HTTP\\noperations and the exported `HealthResponse`, catalog and calculation Schemas.\\nThe OpenAPI check requires its calculate path before running the plain external\\nconsumer. Health readiness has a 15-second total limit, including retries and\\nresponse-body reading; other requests have a five-second limit. The external\\nconsumer has a 30-second limit and a 1 MiB stdout limit. Its stderr is drained\\nwithout retention. Successful stdout is decoded into the exact expected route\\ncoverage; failures report their bounded reason and available exit code.\\nCancellation stops both child processes and removes the workspace. The external\\nconsumer deliberately uses ordinary JavaScript `fetch` and JSON to check a\\ncaller outside the repository.\\n\\n`check-types` covers source, scripts, test fixtures and test configuration.\\n`test` runs native Effect fixtures for settings, stalled headers/bodies,\\ninvalid responses, child-process faults, cancellation and cleanup. All API\\nsource and test paths receive the canonical strict rules, with execution\\nadmitted only at the two existing app/command entrypoints.\\n\\nUse the failure simulation when you need deterministic cleanup evidence for a\\ndownstream consumer failure:\\n\\n```sh\\nbun run --filter=api smoke:public-routes -- --simulate-downstream-failure\\n```\\n\\nThe simulation exits nonzero after the external consumer has covered the\\npublic routes, then removes the temp workspace and stops the API process.\\n\\nUse the portless URL for local API smoke checks:\\n\\n```sh\\ncurl https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/health\\ncurl https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/v1/calculators\\ncurl -X POST https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/v1/calculators/au.pay.take-home/calculate \\\\\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\\\\n  -d '{\\\"facts\\\":{\\\"grossPay\\\":{\\\"_tag\\\":\\\"GrossPay\\\",\\\"amount\\\":{\\\"_tag\\\":\\\"Money\\\",\\\"cents\\\":150000,\\\"currency\\\":\\\"AUD\\\"},\\\"period\\\":\\\"weekly\\\"},\\\"taxFreeThresholdClaimed\\\":true}}'\\n```\\n\\n## Guardrails\\n\\n- Do not define API contracts in this app.\\n- Keep app-owned schemas in `schemas.ts` and derive exported types from those\\n  schemas. Runtime files should consume canonical schema values and compose\\n  layers/startup logic, not redefine reusable shapes inline.\\n- Do not manually wire process signal handlers, `process.exit`, mutable\\n  shutdown flags or `try/catch` around Effect startup. The process entrypoint\\n  should be an Effect program run through `BunRuntime.runMain`.\\n- Do not create a runtime inside request handling.\\n- Keep process-owned resources in `ApiAppLayer` so root fiber interruption\\n  releases them through scoped finalizers.\\n- Keep `apps/web` as an HTTP client of this app, not an in-process API mount.\\n\\n## Related Docs\\n\\n- `docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`\\n- `docs/architecture/effect-services.md`\\n- `docs/architecture/package-ownership.md`\\n- `docs/product-specs/extract-api-app.md`\\n---\\nstatus: canonical\\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-05\\nsource_of_truth: package-readme\\nconfidence: high\\n---\\n\\n# Web App\\n\\nCurrent TanStack Start scaffold for TaxKit.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n`apps/web` proves the current browser/server runtime split and calls the\\nstandalone Effect HTTP API service owned by `apps/api`. It is not the\\nlong-term calculation engine and should not own tax-domain contracts or API\\nrequest handling.\\n\\n## Main Areas\\n\\n- `src/routes/`: TanStack Router routes\\n- `src/lib/runtime.server.ts`: server `ManagedRuntime`\\n- `src/lib/runtime.client.ts`: client `ManagedRuntime`\\n- `src/lib/route-context.ts`: route runtime contract and context selection\\n- `src/lib/runtime-selection.ts`: isomorphic selection of the server/client runtime\\n- `src/server.ts`: server entrypoint\\n\\n## Runtime Shape\\n\\nThe root route loads `@taxkit/api-http/client` through the route runtime and\\nrenders API health status from the standalone API service over HTTP.\\nServer-only API exports must stay out of browser code. The root loader uses\\nthe native runtime contract and passes the Router abort signal to its existing\\nHTTP operation. It returns readonly health fields without a hand-written\\nPromise interface or a one-use runtime wrapper.\\n\\nThe web runtime reads the API origin from:\\n\\n- `TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` on the server\\n- `VITE_TAXKIT_API_BASE_URL` in the browser\\n\\nBoth are required runtime config values and are validated with the HTTP\\npackage's Effect Config and URL Schema. The exact Vite host reads only the\\npublic browser input using Vite's normal file/environment precedence, then\\nSchema-encodes it into a typed build constant. Automatic public-prefix\\nexposure is disabled; Vite still supplies its standard mode/SSR metadata.\\nBrowser modules do not read\\n`import.meta.env`. Missing or invalid raw URLs still fail at runtime; the build\\ndoes not guess a URL or change that validation timing. Settings failures expose\\nonly the client/server identity, settings operation and fixed safe message.\\n`bun run --filter=web dev` injects both from\\n`portless get api.taxkit`. Do not include `/api` in the base URL; the typed\\nAPI client owns route prefixes.\\n\\n## Guardrails\\n\\n- Keep tax rules, facts and calculators in engine packages.\\n- Use browser-safe API client exports from routes.\\n- Do not import `@taxkit/api-http/server` from browser code.\\n- Keep route data acquisition and trust-boundary conversion route-high. Render\\n  the page shell and semantic landmarks before passing focused readonly values\\n  and callbacks to leaves.\\n- Keep local UI commands in leaves; keep remote or domain commands in the route\\n  action or nearest policy-owning container.\\n- Put loading, empty and recoverable error UI at the smallest owning boundary\\n  while preserving a stable footprint and the surrounding page shell.\\n- Keep the app README local; route durable architecture to `docs/architecture`.\\n\\n## Commands\\n\\n```bash\\nbun run --filter=api dev\\nbun run --filter=web dev\\nbun run --filter=web check-types\\nbun run --filter=web test\\nbun run --filter=web test:browser\\nbun run --filter=web build\\n```\\n\\nRun `apps/api` before loading the web root locally. Without the API process,\\nthe root route should fail with an attributable HTTP transport error rather\\nthan silently falling back to an in-process API.\\n\\nUse the portless URLs for local browser and app-to-app checks:\\n\\n- API: `https://api.taxkit.localhost`\\n- Web: `https://taxkit.localhost`\\n\\n## Related Docs\\n\\n- `docs/architecture/frontend.md`\\n- `docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`\\n- `docs/architecture/deployment.md`\\n- `docs/design-docs/abstraction-admission.md`\\n\\n## Atom compatibility proof\\n\\n`bun run web:test:browser` builds the web app and runs the Chromium qualification\\nin `src/lib/atom-lifecycle.browser.test.tsx`. It is part of root `verification`.\\nThe fixture uses Effect test scopes to dispose React roots on failure and proves\\nSSR hydration without errors, one registry through StrictMode effect remount,\\n50 rapid updates, scheduled/cancelled work and final resource disposal. It does\\nnot yet replace the app's existing runtime or qualify RPC cancellation.\\n\\nThe exact candidate is Atom 4.0.0, React/React DOM 19.3.0 and Scheduler 0.28.0.\\nThe root patch changes only Atom's Scheduler peer range to admit exactly 0.28.0;\\nremove it when upstream metadata admits that version. One Scheduler version is\\npresent in the lockfile. Bun resolves peers from registry metadata before patching\\nand may still print the original peer warning; the installed manifest and runtime\\nfixture are the qualified correction. Atom/Scheduler are development dependencies\\nuntil the application migration adopts their runtime owner.\\n\\nThe browser test config extends Vite's browser conditions with `source`; replacing\\nthe defaults with only `source` selects the Node renderer and is not a valid\\nbrowser hydration test. The test imports the actual browser renderer and waits\\nfor hydration before issuing updates.\\n\\n## Strict and route proof\\n\\nCanonical strict rules cover source, tests and all Vite/Vitest configuration.\\nOnly the two existing runtime composition modules, root loader, Vite host and\\nfake browser-test runtime have exact execution permissions. They retain all\\nother rules; no async workflow or raw settings exception is admitted. The\\ncompiler and development Knip graph include both test configurations and Vite.\\nThe package test command uses Bun-hosted Vitest and native Effect tests.\\n\\nSettings tests cover valid, missing and invalid server/browser inputs, exact\\nsecret-negative error bytes, public build-input selection and absent compiled\\nbrowser settings. The real file-route Chromium tests call the actual generated\\nHTTP client through a fake HTTP transport. They prove health decoding and\\ninterruption of pending HTTP work when the Router retires its preload. The\\nHTTP abort signal is observed as aborted. This proves the tested preload\\nretirement, not all navigation/unmount paths or remote provider cancellation.\\nBoth retained Atom/Scheduler cases still run. Browser dependencies are listed\\nfor optimisation so Vite does not reload tests while they start.\\nimport {\\n  declareDocsStack,\\n  docsCloudflareStackName,\\n} from \\\"@taxkit/infrastructure/stack\\\";\\nimport { decodeDocsCloudflareStackStage } from \\\"@taxkit/infrastructure/website\\\";\\nimport * as Alchemy from \\\"alchemy\\\";\\nimport * as Cloudflare from \\\"alchemy/Cloudflare\\\";\\nimport { Stack } from \\\"alchemy/Stack\\\";\\nimport { Stage } from \\\"alchemy/Stage\\\";\\nimport * as Effect from \\\"effect/Effect\\\";\\n\\nexport default Alchemy.Stack(\\n  docsCloudflareStackName,\\n  {\\n    providers: Cloudflare.providers(),\\n    state: Cloudflare.state(),\\n  },\\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\\n    const stack = yield* Stack;\\n    const stage = yield* Stage.pipe(\\n      Effect.flatMap(decodeDocsCloudflareStackStage)\\n    );\\n    return yield* declareDocsStack({ stackName: stack.name, stage });\\n  })\\n);\\nimport * as Cloudflare from \\\"alchemy/Cloudflare\\\";\\nimport * as Array from \\\"effect/Array\\\";\\nimport * as Effect from \\\"effect/Effect\\\";\\n\\nimport {\\n  docsWorkerAssetHeaders,\\n  docsWorkerCompatibilityDate,\\n  docsWorkerCompatibilityFlags,\\n  docsWorkerMemo,\\n  docsWorkerObservability,\\n  docsWorkerResourceId,\\n} from \\\"./cloudflare/website.js\\\";\\nimport type { DocsCloudflareStackStage } from \\\"./cloudflare/website.js\\\";\\n\\nexport { docsCloudflareStackName } from \\\"./cloudflare/website.js\\\";\\n\\nexport const declareDocsStack = ({\\n  stackName,\\n  stage,\\n}: {\\n  readonly stackName: string;\\n  readonly stage: DocsCloudflareStackStage;\\n}) =>\\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\\n    const worker = yield* Cloudflare.Website.Vite(docsWorkerResourceId, {\\n      assets: {\\n        // Website.Vite does not infer the app-owned _headers file when its\\n        // config is passed through Alchemy.\\n        headers: docsWorkerAssetHeaders,\\n        runWorkerFirst: false,\\n      },\\n      compatibility: {\\n        date: docsWorkerCompatibilityDate,\\n        flags: [...docsWorkerCompatibilityFlags],\\n      },\\n      // Alchemy's input requires mutable arrays; give it fresh boundary copies.\\n      memo: {\\n        ...docsWorkerMemo,\\n        include: Array.fromIterable(docsWorkerMemo.include),\\n        workspaces: Array.map(docsWorkerMemo.workspaces, (workspace) => ({\\n          ...workspace,\\n          include: Array.fromIterable(workspace.include),\\n        })),\\n      },\\n      observability: docsWorkerObservability,\\n      rootDir: \\\"apps/docs\\\",\\n      workersDev: true,\\n    });\\n\\n    return {\\n      logicalResourceId: docsWorkerResourceId,\\n      stackName,\\n      stage,\\n      workerName: worker.workerName,\\n      workerUrl: worker.url,\\n    };\\n  });\\npackages/infrastructure/src/stack.ts\\napps/api/src/server.ts\\napps/api/src/config.ts\\napps/api/src/index.ts\\napps/api/src/schemas.ts\\napps/api/vitest.config.ts\\napps/api/tsconfig.json\\npackages/infrastructure/src/cloudflare/website.test.ts\\npackages/infrastructure/src/cloudflare/website.ts\\npackages/infrastructure/src/stage.ts\\napps/web/vitest.config.ts\\napps/web/vite.config.ts\\napps/web/tsconfig.json\\napps/web/package.json\\napps/web/README.md\\napps/web/vitest.browser.config.ts\\napps/web/src/routeTree.gen.ts\\napps/web/src/router.tsx\\napps/web/src/styles.css\\napps/api/scripts/schemas.ts\\napps/api/scripts/smoke-public-routes.runtime.ts\\napps/api/scripts/routes.ts\\napps/api/scripts/smoke-boundaries.test.ts\\napps/api/tsconfig.scripts.json\\napps/api/package.json\\napps/api/README.md\\napps/api/tsconfig.tests.json\\napps/api/CHANGELOG.md\\napps/web/src/routes/__root.tsx\\napps/web/src/routes/index.tsx\\napps/web/src/server.ts\\napps/web/src/lib/config.client-input.ts\\napps/web/src/lib/runtime.client.ts\\napps/web/src/lib/atom-lifecycle.browser.test.tsx\\napps/web/src/lib/runtime-selection.ts\\napps/web/src/lib/runtime.server.ts\\napps/web/src/lib/config.boundary.test.ts\\napps/web/src/lib/health-loader.boundary.browser.test.tsx\\napps/web/src/lib/config.ts\\napps/web/src/lib/config.server.ts\\napps/web/src/lib/route-context.ts\\napps/web/src/lib/config.client.ts\\napps/api/test/config.test.ts\\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow-evidence.test.ts (11 tests) 108ms\\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/strict-boundaries.contract.test.ts (40 tests) 55ms\\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/policy.test.ts (20 tests) 25ms\\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow-artifact.test.ts (11 tests) 25ms\\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/alchemy-memo.test.ts (1 test) 24ms\\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/doppler-custody.test.ts (9 tests) 21ms\\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow-plan-projection.test.ts (15 tests) 20ms\\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/automation.check.runtime.test.ts (5 tests) 20ms\\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/workflow.contract.test.ts (18 tests) 19ms\\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/automation.policy.test.ts (8 tests) 18ms\\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/inventory-credentials.boundary.test.ts (10 tests) 16ms\\n//:test:docs-deployment:task:  ✓ tools/docs-deployment/input.boundary.test.ts (9 tests) 15ms\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","create_time":1791131880.342437}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
