y/src/Cloudflare/Workers/Worker.ts:2578:    createRuntimeContext: (id) => makeWorkerRuntimeContext(id),\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Serverless/Function.ts:3:import type { BaseRuntimeContext } from \\\"../RuntimeContext.ts\\\";\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Serverless/Function.ts:5:export interface FunctionContext extends BaseRuntimeContext {\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:27:  CurrentRuntimeContext,\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:28:  RuntimeContext,\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:30:  type BaseRuntimeContext,\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:31:} from \\\"./RuntimeContext.ts\\\";\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:51: * artifact) the layer builds against the AMBIENT scope. `Effect.provide` is\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:52: * implemented with `scopedWith`, so its transient region scope would tear\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:53: * the layer down — firing init-level finalizers and releasing\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:54: * `Layer.scoped` services — the moment init completes. The runtime bridges\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:55: * evaluate the entrypoint under the instance-lifetime build scope (closed\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:63: * Output sources. Building on the session scope would keep the memo alive\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:73:      ? Effect.flatMap(Effect.scope, (scope) =>\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:74:          Effect.flatMap(Layer.buildWithScope(layer, scope), (context) =>\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:86:    | HttpEffect<InitServices | PlatformServices | RuntimeContext | Scope>\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:88:        HttpEffect<InitServices | PlatformServices | RuntimeContext | Scope>,\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:99:        PlatformServices | RuntimeContext | HttpServerRequest | Scope | Req\\nnode_modules/alchemy/src/Platform.ts:104:        PlatformServices | RuntimeContext | HttpServerRequest | Scope | Req\\nnode_module