{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T16:58:49.964Z","ordinal":15589,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b0e2cff5-2ca3-433c-9fd0-4812818f7718","process_id":"78040","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/dev74-rpc-pr.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/dev74-rpc-pr.md","name":"dev74-rpc-pr.md","path":"/private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/dev74-rpc-pr.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"Adds a private native Effect 4 POST/JSON calculation connection for DEV-74. The checked client calls the existing calculator service, keeps one five-second limit through response decoding, and preserves caller cancellation. Native request checks and fixed error encoding keep private inputs out of the tested reply and log paths.\n\nSeparates the existing report/input Schemas from live calculation imports and adds narrow exports. Old imports keep the same Schema objects and tax results. The browser client bundle no longer retains live engine, calculator or rule-pack implementations.\n\nValidation: 27 native RPC tests; a deliberate byte-limit break is caught; source/default/declaration import checks; actual SDK packed and clean downstream checks; full workspace tests/build and repository verification. Exact outcomes and limits are recorded in `docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-rpc-contract.json`.\n\nThis is a draft stacked on #127. DEV-74 remains in progress: the real API/Website, same-stage binding, browser CORS and complete native trace/failure checks still require implementation. No merge, deploy, publication, version application, provider change or Medicare correction is included.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Adds a private native Effect 4 POST/JSON calculation connection for DEV-74. The checked client calls the existing calculator service, keeps one five-second limit through response decoding, and preserves caller cancellation. Native request checks and fixed error encoding keep private inputs out of the tested reply and log paths.\n\nSeparates the existing report/input Schemas from live calculation imports and adds narrow exports. Old imports keep the same Schema objects and tax results. The browser client bundle no longer retains live engine, calculator or rule-pack implementations.\n\nValidation: 27 native RPC tests; a deliberate byte-limit break is caught; source/default/declaration import checks; actual SDK packed and clean downstream checks; full workspace tests/build and repository verification. Exact outcomes and limits are recorded in `docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-rpc-contract.json`.\n\nThis is a draft stacked on #127. DEV-74 remains in progress: the real API/Website, same-stage binding, browser CORS and complete native trace/failure checks still require implementation. No merge, deploy, publication, version application, provider change or Medicare correction is included.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7166},"formatted_output":"Adds a private native Effect 4 POST/JSON calculation connection for DEV-74. The checked client calls the existing calculator service, keeps one five-second limit through response decoding, and preserves caller cancellation. Native request checks and fixed error encoding keep private inputs out of the tested reply and log paths.\n\nSeparates the existing report/input Schemas from live calculation imports and adds narrow exports. Old imports keep the same Schema objects and tax results. The browser client bundle no longer retains live engine, calculator or rule-pack implementations.\n\nValidation: 27 native RPC tests; a deliberate byte-limit break is caught; source/default/declaration import checks; actual SDK packed and clean downstream checks; full workspace tests/build and repository verification. Exact outcomes and limits are recorded in `docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-rpc-contract.json`.\n\nThis is a draft stacked on #127. DEV-74 remains in progress: the real API/Website, same-stage binding, browser CORS and complete native trace/failure checks still require implementation. No merge, deploy, publication, version application, provider change or Medicare correction is included.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791133129964,"completed_at_ms":1791133129964}}
